{"parentUuid":"f83ac61d-939f-470e-9760-006f3fcf75f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaqokfQyUkMtoDkwhKFU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qm43FwrSL7aR9Fo6diQMSy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03.lean","offset":1610,"limit":125},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5653,"cache_read_input_tokens":201839,"output_tokens":585,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":457},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5653,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":201839,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5653},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Qm43FwrSL7aR9Fo6diQMSy":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03.lean","offset":1610,"limit":125}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5e507c46-7af3-4df7-95ee-a2c056306d6c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgaqokMZ8gAEQU8f7anZS","requestRef":"ea3b7d3c-d560-4c18-be59-7621fbc97b62","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"516dd491-fce9-4d23-9345-3c99f9f8347e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:09:37.166Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"516dd491-fce9-4d23-9345-3c99f9f8347e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06503e62-b7bb-46dd-8bf0-90c46d6d2b97","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qm43FwrSL7aR9Fo6diQMSy","type":"tool_result","content":"1610\t/-! ## Invariants (MM-03.3 §2, A1) -/\n1611\t\n1612\t/-- I1, effective exclusivity strengthened structurally (MM-03.3 §2, A1): two distinct active\n1613\tauthorities, unrelated by `origin`, covering the same leaf, `SharedMutable` leaves included,\n1614\tboth have the proper mode `Observe`. The pass-1 statement on effective modes is the theorem\n1615\t`effective_compat`. -/\n1616\tdef I1 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n1617\t  ∀ (a b : Nat) (x y : Authority) (p : Nat), a ≠ b → s.A[a]? = some x → s.A[b]? = some y →\n1618\t    x.active = true → y.active = true → p ∈ x.footprint → p ∈ y.footprint →\n1619\t    a ∉ s.ancs b → b ∉ s.ancs a → x.mode = .observe ∧ y.mode = .observe\n1620\t\n1621\t/-- I2, conservation of authorities (MM-03.3 §2): the origin of a derived authority exists, and\n1622\ton each leaf of the derived footprint, the leaf is in the footprint of the origin and the\n1623\tderived mode does not exceed the origin's. -/\n1624\tdef I2 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n1625\t  ∀ (b : Nat) (y : Authority) (a : Nat), s.A[b]? = some y → y.origin = some a →\n1626\t    ∃ x : Authority, s.A[a]? = some x ∧ ∀ p ∈ y.footprint, p ∈ x.footprint ∧ y.mode.le x.mode\n1627\t\n1628\t/-- I3, validity of dependencies (MM-03.3 §2): every anchor of a usable place is valid, that is,\n1629\tactive (pass-1 arbitrage 2). -/\n1630\tdef I3 (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∀ x ∈ s.D q, s.Active x\n1631\t\n1632\t/-- I4, validity of consumed values (MM-03.3 §2), first sentence as a state predicate: no\n1633\t`Moved` leaf is readable. The other sentences concern `transfer` and are theorems. -/\n1634\tdef I4 (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ a p, s.I p = .moved → ¬ CanReadLeaf s a p\n1635\t\n1636\t/-- `AnchorOrder` (B8 as corrected by C1): for every usable place and every anchor of it, the\n1637\tframe of the effective anchor (`S3.effAnchor`, the root of the chain of origins) is the frame of\n1638\tthe place or one of its ancestors (MM-03.3.1, `ancestor`). It holds for every anchor. -/\n1639\tdef AnchorOrder (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∀ x ∈ s.D q, EffAnchorOK s x (s.pframe q)\n1640\t\n1641\t/-- `I1 ∧ I2 ∧ I3 ∧ I4`, the invariant `Inv3` written in MM-03.3 §2, before the clause\n1642\t`AnchorOrder` that B8 adds to it. -/\n1643\tdef Inv3base (s : S3) : Prop := I1 s ∧ I2 s ∧ I3 s ∧ I4 s\n1644\t\n1645\t/-- `NoDangling` (C2): no active authority covers a leaf of a place that is not usable in the sense\n1646\tof `Usable` (existence, `dead` mark, chain of owners). It says nothing of initialisation: a leaf\n1647\t`Uninit` or `Moved` of a usable place may stay covered. -/\n1648\tdef NoDangling (s : S3) : Prop :=\n1649\t  ∀ (j : Nat) (y : Authority), s.A[j]? = some y → y.active = true →\n1650\t    ∀ q, ¬ s.Usable q → ∀ l ∈ footprint s.P q, l ∉ y.footprint\n1651\t\n1652\t/-- `Inv3` (MM-03.3 §2; B8, C1, C2): the safety invariant,\n1653\t`I1 ∧ I2 ∧ I3 ∧ I4 ∧ AnchorOrder ∧ NoDangling`. -/\n1654\tdef Inv3 (s : S3) : Prop := Inv3base s ∧ AnchorOrder s ∧ NoDangling s\n1655\t\n1656\ttheorem Inv3.base {s : S3} (h : Inv3 s) : Inv3base s := h.1\n1657\ttheorem Inv3.ao {s : S3} (h : Inv3 s) : AnchorOrder s := h.2.1\n1658\ttheorem Inv3.nd {s : S3} (h : Inv3 s) : NoDangling s := h.2.2\n1659\t\n1660\t/-- `AnchorOrder` read on the places of `P`: decidable form. -/\n1661\ttheorem anchorOrder_iff {s : S3} : AnchorOrder s ↔\n1662\t    ∀ q ∈ List.range s.P.length, s.Usable q → ∀ x ∈ s.D q, EffAnchorOK s x (s.pframe q) :=\n1663\t  ⟨fun h q _ hq => h q hq, fun h q hq => h q (List.mem_range.2 hq.lt) hq⟩\n1664\t\n1665\t/-- `NoDangling` read on the authorities of `A` and on the places containing each covered leaf:\n1666\tdecidable form. -/\n1667\ttheorem noDangling_iff {s : S3} : NoDangling s ↔\n1668\t    ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, s.Active j → ∀ l ∈ s.afp j, l < s.P.length → isLeaf s.P l →\n1669\t      ∀ q ∈ l :: chain (parentOf s.P) l, s.Usable q := by\n1670\t  constructor\n1671\t  · intro h j _ ⟨y, hy, ya⟩ l hl hlP hleaf q hq\n1672\t    have hl' : l ∈ y.footprint := by simpa [S3.afp, hy] using hl\n1673\t    exact Decidable.byContradiction fun hu => h j y hy ya q hu l\n1674\t      (mem_footprint.2 ⟨hlP, hleaf, hlP, (List.mem_cons.1 hq).imp Eq.symm id⟩) hl'\n1675\t  · intro h j y hy ya q hu l hl hly\n1676\t    obtain ⟨hlP, hleaf, -, hq⟩ := mem_footprint.1 hl\n1677\t    exact hu (h j (List.mem_range.2 (lt_of_getElem? hy)) ⟨y, hy, ya⟩ l\n1678\t      (by simp only [S3.afp, hy]; exact hly) hlP hleaf q (List.mem_cons.2 (hq.imp Eq.symm id)))\n1679\t\n1680\t/-- I4 holds in every state: the read condition requires `Init` (MM-03.3 §2, I4; §5). -/\n1681\ttheorem i4_always (s : S3) : I4 s := fun _ _ hm h => by rw [h.2.1] at hm; cases hm\n1682\t\n1683\t/-- Root place (MM-03.3.2; B1): an existing place without parent. -/\n1684\tdef RootPlace (P : List Place) (r : Nat) : Prop := r < P.length ∧ parentOf P r = none\n1685\t\n1686\tinstance (P : List Place) (r : Nat) : Decidable (RootPlace P r) :=\n1687\t  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ∧ _))\n1688\t\n1689\t/-- First clause of B1: two distinct root places have disjoint footprints. Parts and their\n1690\tcontaining places are not concerned. -/\n1691\tdef RootsDisjoint (P : List Place) : Prop :=\n1692\t  ∀ r r', RootPlace P r → RootPlace P r' → r ≠ r' → ∀ l ∈ footprint P r, l ∉ footprint P r'\n1693\t\n1694\t/-- Second clause of B1: the chain of origins of an authority covering a leaf ends at the root\n1695\tauthority of the root place of that leaf, an authority without origin whose footprint is the\n1696\tfootprint of that root place. -/\n1697\tdef RootChain (s : S3) : Prop :=\n1698\t  ∀ (a : Nat) (y : Authority) (l : Nat), s.A[a]? = some y → l ∈ y.footprint → isLeaf s.P l →\n1699\t    ∃ x z r, (x = a ∨ x ∈ s.ancs a) ∧ s.A[x]? = some z ∧ z.origin = none ∧ RootPlace s.P r ∧\n1700\t      partOf s.P l r ∧ ∀ l', l' ∈ z.footprint ↔ l' ∈ footprint s.P r\n1701\t\n1702\t/-- A4, \"Une racine reste détenue par le propriétaire de son emplacement\", a possession condition\n1703\tthat A1 keeps in `WF3`: an authority without origin is held by the owner of the root place of\n1704\tevery leaf it covers. -/\n1705\tdef RootHeld (s : S3) : Prop :=\n1706\t  ∀ (x : Nat) (z : Authority) (l r : Nat), s.A[x]? = some z → z.origin = none → l ∈ z.footprint →\n1707\t    RootPlace s.P r → partOf s.P l r → ∃ pr, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ z.holder = pr.owner\n1708\t\n1709\t/-- `WF3` (A1, A4, B1, C3): well-formedness, the domain of admissible states, separate from the\n1710\tsafety invariant `Inv3`. Origins precede their derivations; footprints are made of existing\n1711\tplaces; the stack is non-empty and without duplicates, below `nF`; owner frames are below `nF`;\n1712\towner places exist; a part comes after its parent and has its owner and its `dead` flag; every\n1713\tactive authority has a live holder (possession); B1: the chain of origins of an authority covering\n1714\ta leaf ends at the root authority of its root place (`RootChain`); A4: a root is held by the owner\n1715\tof its place (`RootHeld`). C3: the first clause of B1, `RootsDisjoint`, is not a clause: it holds\n1716\tfor every list of places (`rootsDisjoint_always`). -/\n1717\tdef WF3 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n1718\t  (∀ (b : Nat) (y : Authority) (a : Nat), s.A[b]? = some y → y.origin = some a → a < b) ∧\n1719\t  (∀ (a : Nat) (x : Authority), s.A[a]? = some x → ∀ l ∈ x.footprint, l < s.P.length) ∧\n1720\t  s.F ≠ [] ∧ s.F.Nodup ∧ (∀ f ∈ s.F, f < s.nF) ∧\n1721\t  (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (f : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .frame f → f < s.nF) ∧\n1722\t  (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (o : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .place o →\n1723\t    o < s.P.length) ∧\n1724\t  (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (r : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.parent = some r →\n1725\t    ∃ pr : Place, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ r < q ∧ pr.owner = pl.owner ∧ s.dead r = s.dead q) ∧\n1726\t  (∀ (a : Nat) (y : Authority), s.A[a]? = some y → y.active = true → HolderLive s y.holder) ∧\n1727\t  RootChain s ∧ RootHeld s\n1728\t\n1729\t/-- The pass-1 exclusivity on effective modes (MM-03.3 §2, I1) is a theorem under the\n1730\tstrengthened I1 (A1). -/\n1731\ttheorem effective_compat {s : S3} (h : I1 s) :\n1732\t    ∀ a b p m₁ m₂, a ≠ b → effective s a p = some m₁ → effective s b p = some m₂ →\n1733\t      Compat m₁ m₂ := by\n1734\t  intro a b p m₁ m₂ hab ha hb"}]},"uuid":"52fe37ac-47a9-4a39-80ca-938de7b9cc9e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:09:37.195Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM03.lean","content":"/-! ## Invariants (MM-03.3 §2, A1) -/\n\n/-- I1, effective exclusivity strengthened structurally (MM-03.3 §2, A1): two distinct active\nauthorities, unrelated by `origin`, covering the same leaf, `SharedMutable` leaves included,\nboth have the proper mode `Observe`. The pass-1 statement on effective modes is the theorem\n`effective_compat`. -/\ndef I1 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ (a b : Nat) (x y : Authority) (p : Nat), a ≠ b → s.A[a]? = some x → s.A[b]? = some y →\n    x.active = true → y.active = true → p ∈ x.footprint → p ∈ y.footprint →\n    a ∉ s.ancs b → b ∉ s.ancs a → x.mode = .observe ∧ y.mode = .observe\n\n/-- I2, conservation of authorities (MM-03.3 §2): the origin of a derived authority exists, and\non each leaf of the derived footprint, the leaf is in the footprint of the origin and the\nderived mode does not exceed the origin's. -/\ndef I2 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ (b : Nat) (y : Authority) (a : Nat), s.A[b]? = some y → y.origin = some a →\n    ∃ x : Authority, s.A[a]? = some x ∧ ∀ p ∈ y.footprint, p ∈ x.footprint ∧ y.mode.le x.mode\n\n/-- I3, validity of dependencies (MM-03.3 §2): every anchor of a usable place is valid, that is,\nactive (pass-1 arbitrage 2). -/\ndef I3 (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∀ x ∈ s.D q, s.Active x\n\n/-- I4, validity of consumed values (MM-03.3 §2), first sentence as a state predicate: no\n`Moved` leaf is readable. The other sentences concern `transfer` and are theorems. -/\ndef I4 (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ a p, s.I p = .moved → ¬ CanReadLeaf s a p\n\n/-- `AnchorOrder` (B8 as corrected by C1): for every usable place and every anchor of it, the\nframe of the effective anchor (`S3.effAnchor`, the root of the chain of origins) is the frame of\nthe place or one of its ancestors (MM-03.3.1, `ancestor`). It holds for every anchor. -/\ndef AnchorOrder (s : S3) : Prop := ∀ q, s.Usable q → ∀ x ∈ s.D q, EffAnchorOK s x (s.pframe q)\n\n/-- `I1 ∧ I2 ∧ I3 ∧ I4`, the invariant `Inv3` written in MM-03.3 §2, before the clause\n`AnchorOrder` that B8 adds to it. -/\ndef Inv3base (s : S3) : Prop := I1 s ∧ I2 s ∧ I3 s ∧ I4 s\n\n/-- `NoDangling` (C2): no active authority covers a leaf of a place that is not usable in the sense\nof `Usable` (existence, `dead` mark, chain of owners). It says nothing of initialisation: a leaf\n`Uninit` or `Moved` of a usable place may stay covered. -/\ndef NoDangling (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ (j : Nat) (y : Authority), s.A[j]? = some y → y.active = true →\n    ∀ q, ¬ s.Usable q → ∀ l ∈ footprint s.P q, l ∉ y.footprint\n\n/-- `Inv3` (MM-03.3 §2; B8, C1, C2): the safety invariant,\n`I1 ∧ I2 ∧ I3 ∧ I4 ∧ AnchorOrder ∧ NoDangling`. -/\ndef Inv3 (s : S3) : Prop := Inv3base s ∧ AnchorOrder s ∧ NoDangling s\n\ntheorem Inv3.base {s : S3} (h : Inv3 s) : Inv3base s := h.1\ntheorem Inv3.ao {s : S3} (h : Inv3 s) : AnchorOrder s := h.2.1\ntheorem Inv3.nd {s : S3} (h : Inv3 s) : NoDangling s := h.2.2\n\n/-- `AnchorOrder` read on the places of `P`: decidable form. -/\ntheorem anchorOrder_iff {s : S3} : AnchorOrder s ↔\n    ∀ q ∈ List.range s.P.length, s.Usable q → ∀ x ∈ s.D q, EffAnchorOK s x (s.pframe q) :=\n  ⟨fun h q _ hq => h q hq, fun h q hq => h q (List.mem_range.2 hq.lt) hq⟩\n\n/-- `NoDangling` read on the authorities of `A` and on the places containing each covered leaf:\ndecidable form. -/\ntheorem noDangling_iff {s : S3} : NoDangling s ↔\n    ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, s.Active j → ∀ l ∈ s.afp j, l < s.P.length → isLeaf s.P l →\n      ∀ q ∈ l :: chain (parentOf s.P) l, s.Usable q := by\n  constructor\n  · intro h j _ ⟨y, hy, ya⟩ l hl hlP hleaf q hq\n    have hl' : l ∈ y.footprint := by simpa [S3.afp, hy] using hl\n    exact Decidable.byContradiction fun hu => h j y hy ya q hu l\n      (mem_footprint.2 ⟨hlP, hleaf, hlP, (List.mem_cons.1 hq).imp Eq.symm id⟩) hl'\n  · intro h j y hy ya q hu l hl hly\n    obtain ⟨hlP, hleaf, -, hq⟩ := mem_footprint.1 hl\n    exact hu (h j (List.mem_range.2 (lt_of_getElem? hy)) ⟨y, hy, ya⟩ l\n      (by simp only [S3.afp, hy]; exact hly) hlP hleaf q (List.mem_cons.2 (hq.imp Eq.symm id)))\n\n/-- I4 holds in every state: the read condition requires `Init` (MM-03.3 §2, I4; §5). -/\ntheorem i4_always (s : S3) : I4 s := fun _ _ hm h => by rw [h.2.1] at hm; cases hm\n\n/-- Root place (MM-03.3.2; B1): an existing place without parent. -/\ndef RootPlace (P : List Place) (r : Nat) : Prop := r < P.length ∧ parentOf P r = none\n\ninstance (P : List Place) (r : Nat) : Decidable (RootPlace P r) :=\n  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ∧ _))\n\n/-- First clause of B1: two distinct root places have disjoint footprints. Parts and their\ncontaining places are not concerned. -/\ndef RootsDisjoint (P : List Place) : Prop :=\n  ∀ r r', RootPlace P r → RootPlace P r' → r ≠ r' → ∀ l ∈ footprint P r, l ∉ footprint P r'\n\n/-- Second clause of B1: the chain of origins of an authority covering a leaf ends at the root\nauthority of the root place of that leaf, an authority without origin whose footprint is the\nfootprint of that root place. -/\ndef RootChain (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ (a : Nat) (y : Authority) (l : Nat), s.A[a]? = some y → l ∈ y.footprint → isLeaf s.P l →\n    ∃ x z r, (x = a ∨ x ∈ s.ancs a) ∧ s.A[x]? = some z ∧ z.origin = none ∧ RootPlace s.P r ∧\n      partOf s.P l r ∧ ∀ l', l' ∈ z.footprint ↔ l' ∈ footprint s.P r\n\n/-- A4, \"Une racine reste détenue par le propriétaire de son emplacement\", a possession condition\nthat A1 keeps in `WF3`: an authority without origin is held by the owner of the root place of\nevery leaf it covers. -/\ndef RootHeld (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ (x : Nat) (z : Authority) (l r : Nat), s.A[x]? = some z → z.origin = none → l ∈ z.footprint →\n    RootPlace s.P r → partOf s.P l r → ∃ pr, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ z.holder = pr.owner\n\n/-- `WF3` (A1, A4, B1, C3): well-formedness, the domain of admissible states, separate from the\nsafety invariant `Inv3`. Origins precede their derivations; footprints are made of existing\nplaces; the stack is non-empty and without duplicates, below `nF`; owner frames are below `nF`;\nowner places exist; a part comes after its parent and has its owner and its `dead` flag; every\nactive authority has a live holder (possession); B1: the chain of origins of an authority covering\na leaf ends at the root authority of its root place (`RootChain`); A4: a root is held by the owner\nof its place (`RootHeld`). C3: the first clause of B1, `RootsDisjoint`, is not a clause: it holds\nfor every list of places (`rootsDisjoint_always`). -/\ndef WF3 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  (∀ (b : Nat) (y : Authority) (a : Nat), s.A[b]? = some y → y.origin = some a → a < b) ∧\n  (∀ (a : Nat) (x : Authority), s.A[a]? = some x → ∀ l ∈ x.footprint, l < s.P.length) ∧\n  s.F ≠ [] ∧ s.F.Nodup ∧ (∀ f ∈ s.F, f < s.nF) ∧\n  (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (f : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .frame f → f < s.nF) ∧\n  (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (o : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.owner = .place o →\n    o < s.P.length) ∧\n  (∀ (q : Nat) (pl : Place) (r : Nat), s.P[q]? = some pl → pl.parent = some r →\n    ∃ pr : Place, s.P[r]? = some pr ∧ r < q ∧ pr.owner = pl.owner ∧ s.dead r = s.dead q) ∧\n  (∀ (a : Nat) (y : Authority), s.A[a]? = some y → y.active = true → HolderLive s y.holder) ∧\n  RootChain s ∧ RootHeld s\n\n/-- The pass-1 exclusivity on effective modes (MM-03.3 §2, I1) is a theorem under the\nstrengthened I1 (A1). -/\ntheorem effective_compat {s : S3} (h : I1 s) :\n    ∀ a b p m₁ m₂, a ≠ b → effective s a p = some m₁ → effective s b p = some m₂ →\n      Compat m₁ m₂ := by\n  intro a b p m₁ m₂ hab ha hb","numLines":125,"startLine":1610,"totalLines":11961}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"516dd491-fce9-4d23-9345-3c99f9f8347e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
