in/lake env lean <file>` (the module is built; start scratch files with `import Ern.MM23` and `open Ern.MM03 Ern.MM23`). `lake` is not on PATH: use ~/.elan/bin/lake. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac.\n\nContext. The task brief (French) is at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/task_mm23_p1.md — read it fully, especially arbitrages K1, K2, K3 (they are normative for this pass). Specs: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md (MM-02) and /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md (MM-03.3). Project rules: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (Review section). The module under review is /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM23.lean; it imports the drafts formal/Ern/MM02.lean and formal/Ern/MM03.lean (unchanged).\n\nYour lens: the representation relation `Repr` (structure `Repr tok L s3 s2`, with `LayoutWF`, `Layout`, `AllocP`, `FrameGone`, `tokOf`). The brief says: \"revue adverse centrée sur Repr (une relation trop faible rendrait R1, R2 et R6 vides : chaque théorème doit avoir un témoin où sa conclusion n'est pas triviale)\".\n\nCheck, with evidence:\n1. Is each clause of `Repr` exactly what K1/K2/K3 say — not stronger, not weaker? Compare clause by clause: LayoutWF (a)(b)(c)(d); K2 (root ↔ allocation, part ↔ sub-range, arena block, frame token \"compatible par construction\"); K3 (usable root → live; Init leaf → bytes initialised; dead by free or frame exit → dead; dead by endUse (owned storage not freed) → live). Pay attention to the author's choices: `k` dropped from the signature (brief writes `Repr k L s3 s2`), `tok` added, the `exited` clause restricted to roots directly owned by a popped frame, the `leaked` clause generalised to every place-owned, non-usable, non-freed root (justified by K4 on exitFrame and free), tokens only for frame-owned roots, injectivity of root allocations.\n2. Is `Repr` too weak anywhere, i.e. are there pairs (s3, s2) satisfying `Repr` where the MM-02 state misrepresents the MM-03 state in a way the K1–K3 text forbids, or that would make R1/R2/R6 hold trivially? Is it too strong, i.e. does it reject a pair that K1–K3 accept, or make some R6 statement impossible for legitimate reached states? Try to build concrete counterexamples with `decide` (Repr is decidable).\n3. Do the cases at the end of the file (namespaces CaseInit and Cases) really show non-trivial conclusions for R1, R2, R4, R6, exclusive_bytes, repr_init? Are the negative tests (\"each clause of Repr rejects a wrong MM-02 state\") actually discriminating the clause they claim?\n4. Any place where an interpretation was chosen silently where K1–K3 are unclear.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity (blocking/major/minor), location (line numbers), cause (formalization error, missing coverage, spec defect), and evidence (spec quote, Lean counterexample with the exact command output, or a precise argument). No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the task. Keep the report under 900 words.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/a4d8611954a3dcdc9.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7aa2728e-e16c-4b55-9412-ad6c066d899c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang