{"parentUuid":"b5975fc2-59d5-4657-bee0-2bf17473043c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06503e62-b7bb-46dd-8bf0-90c46d6d2b97","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MUQca5YfpzUmif7cEFEcqW","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"c9f7d5b8-456e-415c-b80b-116ab4631394","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:59:29.210Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md","oldString":"- Spec files live in `~/Downloads/`","newString":"- Jalon 2 pass 1 (refinement MM-03 → MM-02, arbitrages K1-K5, 2026-10-31): branch `formal/refinement_0.1` cut from `formal/access_model_0.1`, new module `Ern.MM23` (`formal/Ern/MM23.lean`, imports MM02 and MM03 unchanged), report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` sections (a)-(f). Specs now `~/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md` and `~/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`. `Repr tok L s3 s2` is decidable (structure + `decidable_of_iff`, needs `set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096`). Axiom sweep by a Lean script walking module theorems with `collectAxioms` (grep-based sweep misses namespaced cases).\n- Spec files live in `~/Downloads/`","originalFile":"---\nname: ern-formal-mm02-exploration\ndescription: \"Conventions of the ERN formal/ exploratory passes (MM-02 and MM-03 branches, French briefs, reports/ never merged, spec kept outside the repo, lake path, axiom rule)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180\n  modified: 2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z\n---\n\nExploratory Lean passes on ERN specs arrive as pasted French task briefs.\n- MM-02 v0.2: branch `formal/memory_model_0.2`. MM-02 v0.3 (passes 1 to 4, 2026-10-28): `formal/memory_model_0.3`, module `Ern.MM02` (`formal/Ern/MM02.lean`), reports `MM02_v0.3*.md`.\n- MM-03.3 v0.2 jalon 1 (access discipline, 2026-10-29): branch `formal/access_model_0.1` cut from `formal/memory_model_0.3`, module `Ern.MM03` (`formal/Ern/MM03.lean`, imports MM02 unchanged), report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1.md`. Key finding there: Inv3 is not inductive under release, so preservation is proved under a structural invariant `WF3` (clause `Tree`).\n- MM-03.3 pass 2 (arbitrages A1-A11, 2026-10-29): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p2.md`. Code, docstrings and commit messages in English; only the report in French. The brief forbids weakening any pass-1 statement: diff statements mechanically (cut at the top-level `:=`, not the first one) and give a Lean witness for every added hypothesis or retired statement.\n- MM-03.3 pass 3 (arbitrages B1-B10, 2026-10-29): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p3.md`; `Inv3base` = pass-2 Inv3, `Inv3 = Inv3base ∧ AnchorOrder`; WF3 gained RootsDisjoint, RootChain (B1) and RootHeld (A4). Briefs save to the scratchpad as `task_mm03_p<N>.md`.\n- MM-03.3 pass 4 (arbitrages C1-C9, 2026-10-29, closes milestone 1): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p4.md` with an extra section (n) « bilan de clôture ». `Inv3 = Inv3base ∧ AnchorOrder ∧ NoDangling`; `alloc` takes a shape (enterFrame locals encoding); `RootsDisjoint` left `WF3`.\n- MM-03.3 pass 5 (arbitrages D1-D4, 2026-10-29): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p5.md` with an extra section (o) (domain changes). `S3.init statics`, `S3.arenas`, `Reachable k statics` with newArena/issue/reset. Open questions left for the arbiter: statics owned by statics, nested arena ownership, kind rule of `IsInternalFor` ((e) 1 to 6).\n- MM-03.3 pass 6 (arbitrages F1-F7, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p6.md` with extra section (p) (F7 progress). Arenas by holder of `internal`, `store`, `callParams` ghost field. F6 (`call_protects_params_safe`) is false as stated (counterexamples kept); F7 (a) second store accepted.\n- MM-03.3 pass 7 (arbitrages G1-G5, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p7.md` with extra sections (p) verdict changes and (q) status of NoOrphan / F6. G1 clause in EnterPre (EnterPreBase = pass-6 text), G2 leaf store with arrival clause, G3 NoOrphan proved via auxiliary RootLive, G4 AnchorOrderHeld checked in arrival states. F6 still false (ancestor, unblock by releases, exit re-anchoring); G2 guard bypassed by a helper then release/endUse/free/exit.\n- MM-03.3 pass 8 (arbitrages J1-J2, 2026-10-30, closes jalon 1 again): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p8.md`, sections (a)-(o), (p) verdict changes, (q) closing balance in four classes. J1: `SameShape` (ordered isomorphism, open question), `corr`/`mvTo` move held authorities and owned places to corresponding parts, issue to a free leaf only, `newArena` needs the arena value Init, `init_only_by_writes` over a `Step` union. Open: J1 bullets 2/3 conflict (issue into a Moved leaf of the arena value).\n- Spec files live in `~/Downloads/` (`ERN_Memory_model.md` = v0.2 incl. MM-03.1/03.2, `ERN_Memory_Model_v0.3_consolidee.md`, `ERN_Memory_Model_0.3.3.md` = MM-03.3 v0.2), not in `specs/`.\n\n**Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions.\n\n**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_lt_range`): sweep `#print axioms` over every theorem and replace them with local lemmas. Mathlib tactics (`set`, `tauto`) are unavailable. Reviews keep catching report errors: quote old forms from the old commit, count declarations with a command, and base an evidence claim only on a check that would fail on the defect. After fixing review findings, run a second targeted review of the fixes: in MM-03 pass 2 a fix over-rejected legitimate programs. Before calling a clause \"missing\" from an arbitrage, re-read every earlier arbitrage still in force: in pass 3 the clause needed for exitFrame_no_dangling was A4's root-holder rule, which A1 puts in WF3 and pass 2 had left out. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac: run `lake build` directly (about 2.5 min). When an arbitrage enlarges a definition used in hypotheses (pass 4: `Inv3` gained `NoDangling`), theorems whose text is unchanged silently narrow: give them only the conjunct they use. Before retiring a counterexample whose witness breaks a new invariant clause, look for another witness: pass-4 review found one and flagged the weakening as major. Check obligations against the initial state: the base frame of `S3.init` owns no place, so an obligation about it can be vacuous on reached states. A review fix can itself pick a semantic reading (pass 5: the kind conjunct of `IsInternalFor` rejected a `newArena` that D3 leaves undecided): check every fix for verdicts it changes on cases the text is silent on. Module docstrings must cite the report's own numbering, not the review's decision numbers. Arbiter-supplied theorems can be false: check them on small reached states (owned storage, a parameter that is the ancestor of another) before trying a proof. Every factual claim in the report needs a module witness, or reviewers flag it; never say \"blocked until X\" without checking escape sequences such as ending the owner value. When a precondition gains clauses, lemmas taking it as a hypothesis narrow silently: name the old precondition (pass 7: `EnterPreBase`) and give the lemmas only what they use. A guard on one operation (G2 on `store`) is usually bypassable through another (a helper authority then `release`/`endUse`/`free`/exit): look for such bypasses before claiming a configuration is excluded. A new check on an operation with a defined failure (`issue` → `fail`) must not turn that failure into `reject`. Use one adversarial reviewer per arbitrage lens; each found distinct real issues in pass 7. When a restriction rejects an old counterexample, try to rebuild a witness that satisfies the new clause before restating it as a rejection (pass 8: a same-shape destination restored `transfer_not_inv3_preserving`). Drop hypotheses a proof does not use. When cases disappear because their state is no longer reached, replay their verdicts on a new reachable state and list the drops. Machine-check every changed verdict the report lists, including the old witnesses' rejected steps. Never state \"only clause X fails\" as `X → Pre` next to `¬ X`: that is vacuous; name the other clauses (pass 8: `TransferPreBase` with an iff) and state them. Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","-  modified: 2026-10-30T20:00:00.000Z","+  modified: 2026-10-31T19:59:29.206Z"," ---"," "," Exploratory Lean passes on ERN specs arrive as pasted French task briefs."]},{"oldStart":18,"oldLines":6,"newStart":18,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - MM-03.3 pass 6 (arbitrages F1-F7, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p6.md` with extra section (p) (F7 progress). Arenas by holder of `internal`, `store`, `callParams` ghost field. F6 (`call_protects_params_safe`) is false as stated (counterexamples kept); F7 (a) second store accepted."," - MM-03.3 pass 7 (arbitrages G1-G5, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p7.md` with extra sections (p) verdict changes and (q) status of NoOrphan / F6. G1 clause in EnterPre (EnterPreBase = pass-6 text), G2 leaf store with arrival clause, G3 NoOrphan proved via auxiliary RootLive, G4 AnchorOrderHeld checked in arrival states. F6 still false (ancestor, unblock by releases, exit re-anchoring); G2 guard bypassed by a helper then release/endUse/free/exit."," - MM-03.3 pass 8 (arbitrages J1-J2, 2026-10-30, closes jalon 1 again): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p8.md`, sections (a)-(o), (p) verdict changes, (q) closing balance in four classes. J1: `SameShape` (ordered isomorphism, open question), `corr`/`mvTo` move held authorities and owned places to corresponding parts, issue to a free leaf only, `newArena` needs the arena value Init, `init_only_by_writes` over a `Step` union. Open: J1 bullets 2/3 conflict (issue into a Moved leaf of the arena value).","+- Jalon 2 pass 1 (refinement MM-03 → MM-02, arbitrages K1-K5, 2026-10-31): branch `formal/refinement_0.1` cut from `formal/access_model_0.1`, new module `Ern.MM23` (`formal/Ern/MM23.lean`, imports MM02 and MM03 unchanged), report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` sections (a)-(f). Specs now `~/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md` and `~/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`. `Repr tok L s3 s2` is decidable (structure + `decidable_of_iff`, needs `set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096`). Axiom sweep by a Lean script walking module theorems with `collectAxioms` (grep-based sweep misses namespaced cases)."," - Spec files live in `~/Downloads/` (`ERN_Memory_model.md` = v0.2 incl. MM-03.1/03.2, `ERN_Memory_Model_v0.3_consolidee.md`, `ERN_Memory_Model_0.3.3.md` = MM-03.3 v0.2), not in `specs/`."," "," **Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5975fc2-59d5-4657-bee0-2bf17473043c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"c9f7d5b8-456e-415c-b80b-116ab4631394","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgauc2iRyy1yuY1fgNoXW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VgFZNcSh9dDNYpC5VZX4s7","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md","old_string":"Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form.","new_string":"Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form. `omega` proving a conjunction goal pulls `Classical.choice`: split the goal first. `meta` is a keyword in this Lean: never name a hypothesis `meta`. `set` (Mathlib) is unavailable: use `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩`. `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated: use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`. When `S3.Usable.mono` is applied with `rfl` for `hP`, give `(s := …) (s' := …)` explicitly or it unifies the wrong way."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1079,"cache_read_input_tokens":634959,"output_tokens":1441,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":496},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1079,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1441,"cache_read_input_tokens":634959,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1079},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VgFZNcSh9dDNYpC5VZX4s7":{"file_path":"/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md","old_string":"Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form.","new_string":"Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form. `omega` proving a conjunction goal pulls `Classical.choice`: split the goal first. `meta` is a keyword in this Lean: never name a hypothesis `meta`. `set` (Mathlib) is unavailable: use `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩`. `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated: use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`. When `S3.Usable.mono` is applied with `rfl` for `hP`, give `(s := …) (s' := …)` explicitly or it unifies the wrong way."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cb784315-189d-401f-9452-a88dcf564c55","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cgauc2HdnRigELPgYHPCv","requestRef":"5a529da0-ca3b-4219-bc4f-0b56765f9aac","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f38de43a-2dc9-4725-86f8-b560fbd84450","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:59:32.296Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"f38de43a-2dc9-4725-86f8-b560fbd84450","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"06503e62-b7bb-46dd-8bf0-90c46d6d2b97","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VgFZNcSh9dDNYpC5VZX4s7","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"05bdf74f-d55d-4c50-9369-364cde167a1b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:59:32.313Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md","oldString":"Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form.","newString":"Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form. `omega` proving a conjunction goal pulls `Classical.choice`: split the goal first. `meta` is a keyword in this Lean: never name a hypothesis `meta`. `set` (Mathlib) is unavailable: use `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩`. `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated: use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`. When `S3.Usable.mono` is applied with `rfl` for `hP`, give `(s := …) (s' := …)` explicitly or it unifies the wrong way.","originalFile":"---\nname: ern-formal-mm02-exploration\ndescription: \"Conventions of the ERN formal/ exploratory passes (MM-02 and MM-03 branches, French briefs, reports/ never merged, spec kept outside the repo, lake path, axiom rule)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180\n  modified: 2026-10-31T19:59:29.206Z\n---\n\nExploratory Lean passes on ERN specs arrive as pasted French task briefs.\n- MM-02 v0.2: branch `formal/memory_model_0.2`. MM-02 v0.3 (passes 1 to 4, 2026-10-28): `formal/memory_model_0.3`, module `Ern.MM02` (`formal/Ern/MM02.lean`), reports `MM02_v0.3*.md`.\n- MM-03.3 v0.2 jalon 1 (access discipline, 2026-10-29): branch `formal/access_model_0.1` cut from `formal/memory_model_0.3`, module `Ern.MM03` (`formal/Ern/MM03.lean`, imports MM02 unchanged), report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1.md`. Key finding there: Inv3 is not inductive under release, so preservation is proved under a structural invariant `WF3` (clause `Tree`).\n- MM-03.3 pass 2 (arbitrages A1-A11, 2026-10-29): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p2.md`. Code, docstrings and commit messages in English; only the report in French. The brief forbids weakening any pass-1 statement: diff statements mechanically (cut at the top-level `:=`, not the first one) and give a Lean witness for every added hypothesis or retired statement.\n- MM-03.3 pass 3 (arbitrages B1-B10, 2026-10-29): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p3.md`; `Inv3base` = pass-2 Inv3, `Inv3 = Inv3base ∧ AnchorOrder`; WF3 gained RootsDisjoint, RootChain (B1) and RootHeld (A4). Briefs save to the scratchpad as `task_mm03_p<N>.md`.\n- MM-03.3 pass 4 (arbitrages C1-C9, 2026-10-29, closes milestone 1): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p4.md` with an extra section (n) « bilan de clôture ». `Inv3 = Inv3base ∧ AnchorOrder ∧ NoDangling`; `alloc` takes a shape (enterFrame locals encoding); `RootsDisjoint` left `WF3`.\n- MM-03.3 pass 5 (arbitrages D1-D4, 2026-10-29): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p5.md` with an extra section (o) (domain changes). `S3.init statics`, `S3.arenas`, `Reachable k statics` with newArena/issue/reset. Open questions left for the arbiter: statics owned by statics, nested arena ownership, kind rule of `IsInternalFor` ((e) 1 to 6).\n- MM-03.3 pass 6 (arbitrages F1-F7, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p6.md` with extra section (p) (F7 progress). Arenas by holder of `internal`, `store`, `callParams` ghost field. F6 (`call_protects_params_safe`) is false as stated (counterexamples kept); F7 (a) second store accepted.\n- MM-03.3 pass 7 (arbitrages G1-G5, 2026-10-30): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p7.md` with extra sections (p) verdict changes and (q) status of NoOrphan / F6. G1 clause in EnterPre (EnterPreBase = pass-6 text), G2 leaf store with arrival clause, G3 NoOrphan proved via auxiliary RootLive, G4 AnchorOrderHeld checked in arrival states. F6 still false (ancestor, unblock by releases, exit re-anchoring); G2 guard bypassed by a helper then release/endUse/free/exit.\n- MM-03.3 pass 8 (arbitrages J1-J2, 2026-10-30, closes jalon 1 again): same branch, report `formal/reports/MM03_v0.1_p8.md`, sections (a)-(o), (p) verdict changes, (q) closing balance in four classes. J1: `SameShape` (ordered isomorphism, open question), `corr`/`mvTo` move held authorities and owned places to corresponding parts, issue to a free leaf only, `newArena` needs the arena value Init, `init_only_by_writes` over a `Step` union. Open: J1 bullets 2/3 conflict (issue into a Moved leaf of the arena value).\n- Jalon 2 pass 1 (refinement MM-03 → MM-02, arbitrages K1-K5, 2026-10-31): branch `formal/refinement_0.1` cut from `formal/access_model_0.1`, new module `Ern.MM23` (`formal/Ern/MM23.lean`, imports MM02 and MM03 unchanged), report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` sections (a)-(f). Specs now `~/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md` and `~/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`. `Repr tok L s3 s2` is decidable (structure + `decidable_of_iff`, needs `set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4096`). Axiom sweep by a Lean script walking module theorems with `collectAxioms` (grep-based sweep misses namespaced cases).\n- Spec files live in `~/Downloads/` (`ERN_Memory_model.md` = v0.2 incl. MM-03.1/03.2, `ERN_Memory_Model_v0.3_consolidee.md`, `ERN_Memory_Model_0.3.3.md` = MM-03.3 v0.2), not in `specs/`.\n\n**Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions.\n\n**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_lt_range`): sweep `#print axioms` over every theorem and replace them with local lemmas. Mathlib tactics (`set`, `tauto`) are unavailable. Reviews keep catching report errors: quote old forms from the old commit, count declarations with a command, and base an evidence claim only on a check that would fail on the defect. After fixing review findings, run a second targeted review of the fixes: in MM-03 pass 2 a fix over-rejected legitimate programs. Before calling a clause \"missing\" from an arbitrage, re-read every earlier arbitrage still in force: in pass 3 the clause needed for exitFrame_no_dangling was A4's root-holder rule, which A1 puts in WF3 and pass 2 had left out. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac: run `lake build` directly (about 2.5 min). When an arbitrage enlarges a definition used in hypotheses (pass 4: `Inv3` gained `NoDangling`), theorems whose text is unchanged silently narrow: give them only the conjunct they use. Before retiring a counterexample whose witness breaks a new invariant clause, look for another witness: pass-4 review found one and flagged the weakening as major. Check obligations against the initial state: the base frame of `S3.init` owns no place, so an obligation about it can be vacuous on reached states. A review fix can itself pick a semantic reading (pass 5: the kind conjunct of `IsInternalFor` rejected a `newArena` that D3 leaves undecided): check every fix for verdicts it changes on cases the text is silent on. Module docstrings must cite the report's own numbering, not the review's decision numbers. Arbiter-supplied theorems can be false: check them on small reached states (owned storage, a parameter that is the ancestor of another) before trying a proof. Every factual claim in the report needs a module witness, or reviewers flag it; never say \"blocked until X\" without checking escape sequences such as ending the owner value. When a precondition gains clauses, lemmas taking it as a hypothesis narrow silently: name the old precondition (pass 7: `EnterPreBase`) and give the lemmas only what they use. A guard on one operation (G2 on `store`) is usually bypassable through another (a helper authority then `release`/`endUse`/`free`/exit): look for such bypasses before claiming a configuration is excluded. A new check on an operation with a defined failure (`issue` → `fail`) must not turn that failure into `reject`. Use one adversarial reviewer per arbitrage lens; each found distinct real issues in pass 7. When a restriction rejects an old counterexample, try to rebuild a witness that satisfies the new clause before restating it as a rejection (pass 8: a same-shape destination restored `transfer_not_inv3_preserving`). Drop hypotheses a proof does not use. When cases disappear because their state is no longer reached, replay their verdicts on a new reachable state and list the drops. Machine-check every changed verdict the report lists, including the old witnesses' rejected steps. Never state \"only clause X fails\" as `X → Pre` next to `¬ X`: that is vacuous; name the other clauses (pass 8: `TransferPreBase` with an iff) and state them. Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","-  modified: 2026-10-31T19:59:29.206Z","+  modified: 2026-10-31T19:59:32.308Z"," ---"," "," Exploratory Lean passes on ERN specs arrive as pasted French task briefs."]},{"oldStart":23,"oldLines":4,"newStart":23,"newLines":4,"lines":[" "," **Why:** the briefs require French commit messages (one per step), docstrings citing `MM-0x.y` rules, statement changes justified in the report, and say `formal/reports/` is exploration never merged into `main`. Later briefs add \"arbitrages\" that answer earlier report questions."," ","-**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_lt_range`): sweep `#print axioms` over every theorem and replace them with local lemmas. Mathlib tactics (`set`, `tauto`) are unavailable. Reviews keep catching report errors: quote old forms from the old commit, count declarations with a command, and base an evidence claim only on a check that would fail on the defect. After fixing review findings, run a second targeted review of the fixes: in MM-03 pass 2 a fix over-rejected legitimate programs. Before calling a clause \"missing\" from an arbitrage, re-read every earlier arbitrage still in force: in pass 3 the clause needed for exitFrame_no_dangling was A4's root-holder rule, which A1 puts in WF3 and pass 2 had left out. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac: run `lake build` directly (about 2.5 min). When an arbitrage enlarges a definition used in hypotheses (pass 4: `Inv3` gained `NoDangling`), theorems whose text is unchanged silently narrow: give them only the conjunct they use. Before retiring a counterexample whose witness breaks a new invariant clause, look for another witness: pass-4 review found one and flagged the weakening as major. Check obligations against the initial state: the base frame of `S3.init` owns no place, so an obligation about it can be vacuous on reached states. A review fix can itself pick a semantic reading (pass 5: the kind conjunct of `IsInternalFor` rejected a `newArena` that D3 leaves undecided): check every fix for verdicts it changes on cases the text is silent on. Module docstrings must cite the report's own numbering, not the review's decision numbers. Arbiter-supplied theorems can be false: check them on small reached states (owned storage, a parameter that is the ancestor of another) before trying a proof. Every factual claim in the report needs a module witness, or reviewers flag it; never say \"blocked until X\" without checking escape sequences such as ending the owner value. When a precondition gains clauses, lemmas taking it as a hypothesis narrow silently: name the old precondition (pass 7: `EnterPreBase`) and give the lemmas only what they use. A guard on one operation (G2 on `store`) is usually bypassable through another (a helper authority then `release`/`endUse`/`free`/exit): look for such bypasses before claiming a configuration is excluded. A new check on an operation with a defined failure (`issue` → `fail`) must not turn that failure into `reject`. Use one adversarial reviewer per arbitrage lens; each found distinct real issues in pass 7. When a restriction rejects an old counterexample, try to rebuild a witness that satisfies the new clause before restating it as a rejection (pass 8: a same-shape destination restored `transfer_not_inv3_preserving`). Drop hypotheses a proof does not use. When cases disappear because their state is no longer reached, replay their verdicts on a new reachable state and list the drops. Machine-check every changed verdict the report lists, including the old witnesses' rejected steps. Never state \"only clause X fails\" as `X → Pre` next to `¬ X`: that is vacuous; name the other clauses (pass 8: `TransferPreBase` with an iff) and state them. Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form.","+**How to apply:** start a new pass from the latest branch tip; run an adversarial review workflow over module and report before delivering; `lake` is not on PATH, call `~/.elan/bin/lake`; keep the Lake library name `Ern`. `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout`, never commit the deletion. A post-commit hook can make `git commit` exceed 2 minutes: give it a long timeout. The axiom rule ({propext, Quot.sound} only) forbids core lemmas that pull `Classical.choice` (`List.getElem?_mapIdx`, `List.eq_nil_iff_forall_not_mem`, `List.nodup_range`, `List.pairwise_lt_range`): sweep `#print axioms` over every theorem and replace them with local lemmas. Mathlib tactics (`set`, `tauto`) are unavailable. Reviews keep catching report errors: quote old forms from the old commit, count declarations with a command, and base an evidence claim only on a check that would fail on the defect. After fixing review findings, run a second targeted review of the fixes: in MM-03 pass 2 a fix over-rejected legitimate programs. Before calling a clause \"missing\" from an arbitrage, re-read every earlier arbitrage still in force: in pass 3 the clause needed for exitFrame_no_dangling was A4's root-holder rule, which A1 puts in WF3 and pass 2 had left out. `timeout` does not exist on this Mac: run `lake build` directly (about 2.5 min). When an arbitrage enlarges a definition used in hypotheses (pass 4: `Inv3` gained `NoDangling`), theorems whose text is unchanged silently narrow: give them only the conjunct they use. Before retiring a counterexample whose witness breaks a new invariant clause, look for another witness: pass-4 review found one and flagged the weakening as major. Check obligations against the initial state: the base frame of `S3.init` owns no place, so an obligation about it can be vacuous on reached states. A review fix can itself pick a semantic reading (pass 5: the kind conjunct of `IsInternalFor` rejected a `newArena` that D3 leaves undecided): check every fix for verdicts it changes on cases the text is silent on. Module docstrings must cite the report's own numbering, not the review's decision numbers. Arbiter-supplied theorems can be false: check them on small reached states (owned storage, a parameter that is the ancestor of another) before trying a proof. Every factual claim in the report needs a module witness, or reviewers flag it; never say \"blocked until X\" without checking escape sequences such as ending the owner value. When a precondition gains clauses, lemmas taking it as a hypothesis narrow silently: name the old precondition (pass 7: `EnterPreBase`) and give the lemmas only what they use. A guard on one operation (G2 on `store`) is usually bypassable through another (a helper authority then `release`/`endUse`/`free`/exit): look for such bypasses before claiming a configuration is excluded. A new check on an operation with a defined failure (`issue` → `fail`) must not turn that failure into `reject`. Use one adversarial reviewer per arbitrage lens; each found distinct real issues in pass 7. When a restriction rejects an old counterexample, try to rebuild a witness that satisfies the new clause before restating it as a rejection (pass 8: a same-shape destination restored `transfer_not_inv3_preserving`). Drop hypotheses a proof does not use. When cases disappear because their state is no longer reached, replay their verdicts on a new reachable state and list the drops. Machine-check every changed verdict the report lists, including the old witnesses' rejected steps. Never state \"only clause X fails\" as `X → Pre` next to `¬ X`: that is vacuous; name the other clauses (pass 8: `TransferPreBase` with an iff) and state them. Run a second targeted check after fixing verification findings: in pass 8 it caught that vacuous form. `omega` proving a conjunction goal pulls `Classical.choice`: split the goal first. `meta` is a keyword in this Lean: never name a hypothesis `meta`. `set` (Mathlib) is unavailable: use `obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = e := ⟨_, rfl⟩`. `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated: use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`. When `S3.Usable.mono` is applied with `rfl` for `hP`, give `(s := …) (s' := …)` explicitly or it unifies the wrong way."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f38de43a-2dc9-4725-86f8-b560fbd84450","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
