{"parentUuid":"00baa727-50f5-4448-ab1d-c2b17303a9d5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgauvovGtLeUZT4HUHXPv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both reviews flag the same two readings (storage owned by a freed root, locals owned by a local), plus new gaps: `tokens` being weaker than K2, missing negative tests for K1 (a)/(c), and `free` not marking storage dead per O13. I'll add the missing tests and a direct R1 witness, then update the report.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6856,"cache_read_input_tokens":644758,"output_tokens":4996,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6856,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4996,"cache_read_input_tokens":644758,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6856},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"ae4961a4-d8bf-4422-947e-cc855e3e13dd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgauvoWEBxX4P4dLFM1dM","requestRef":"04f30952-a3dc-4271-ade9-d304d4c52ce3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0a7365d3-dd9d-4bdf-8bf4-e4bb73c330c0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:04:08.817Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"0a7365d3-dd9d-4bdf-8bf4-e4bb73c330c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgauvovGtLeUZT4HUHXPv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PDMVAQEofws9H9ojaEXPaW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"ls /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review_repr/ && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/MM23.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd='''/-- Clauses K1 (a) and (c) reject a layout on their own: the field 5 of 3 in a fresh allocation 4\nother than the allocation 3 of the field 4 breaks (a) only; the range of leaf 1 past the size of\nits allocation breaks (c) only. -/\ndef m3x : MM02.State := exec m3 [.alloc 0 (topPlacement m3 (g 0)) 8 4 none]\ndef Lsa : Layout := fun q => if q = 5 then ⟨4, 0, 4⟩ else L q\nexample : ¬ (∀ r < e6.P.length, RootPlace e6.P r → ∀ l ∈ footprint e6.P r,\n    ∀ l' ∈ footprint e6.P r, (Lsa l).alloc = (Lsa l').alloc) := by decide\nexample : (∀ l < e6.P.length, ∀ l' < e6.P.length, isLeaf e6.P l → isLeaf e6.P l' → l ≠ l' →\n    (Lsa l).alloc = (Lsa l').alloc →\n      MM02.RangeDisjoint (Lsa l).off (Lsa l).len (Lsa l').off (Lsa l').len) ∧\n    (∀ l < e6.P.length, isLeaf e6.P l →\n      AllocP m3x (Lsa l).alloc fun a => (Lsa l).off + (Lsa l).len ≤ a.size) := by decide\ndef Lwi : Layout := fun q => if q = 1 then ⟨1, 6, 4⟩ else L q\nexample : ¬ (∀ l < e1.P.length, isLeaf e1.P l →\n    AllocP m1 (Lwi l).alloc fun a => (Lwi l).off + (Lwi l).len ≤ a.size) := by decide\nexample : (∀ r < e1.P.length, RootPlace e1.P r → ∀ l ∈ footprint e1.P r,\n      ∀ l' ∈ footprint e1.P r, (Lwi l).alloc = (Lwi l').alloc) ∧\n    (∀ l < e1.P.length, ∀ l' < e1.P.length, isLeaf e1.P l → isLeaf e1.P l' → l ≠ l' →\n      (Lwi l).alloc = (Lwi l').alloc →\n        MM02.RangeDisjoint (Lwi l).off (Lwi l).len (Lwi l').off (Lwi l').len) := by decide\n\n/-- R1 applied directly to the read of leaf 1 in `e3`: an allocation, the range initialised, a\nread of outcome `ok` with the bytes of the range, never `ub`. -/\nexample : ∃ al, m3.allocs (L 1).alloc = some al ∧ al.InitRange (L 1).off (L 1).len ∧\n    MM02.ReadStep obR (leafAcc m3 L .read 1) m3 (.ok (al.bytesAt (L 1).off (L 1).len)) ∧\n    ¬ MM02.ReadStep obR (leafAcc m3 L .read 1) m3 .ub :=\n  r1_read3 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).1 (reachable_invariants kc_dd r3).2.1.nd\n    (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive kc_dd r3).1 (by decide)\n    (.ok (by decide) : Read3Step 1 [1] e3 (.ok e3)) (fun _ _ => trivial) (fun l hl => by\n      rw [List.mem_singleton] at hl; subst hl; show (leafAcc m3 L .read 1).addr % 4 = 0; decide)\n    1 (List.mem_singleton_self _)\n\n/-- Gap kept (report, (f) 4): after `free` of 6, the storage 7 it owns stops being usable but is\nnot marked dead, where O13 marks dead \"le stockage qui cesse de vivre\". -/\nexample : af14.dead 7 = false ∧ ¬ af14.Usable 7 := by decide\n\nend Cases\n'''\ns=s.replace(\"end Cases\\n\", add, 1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/MM23.lean 2>&1 | head -20","description":"Add K1 (a)/(c) negative tests, direct R1 witness, O13 gap"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6856,"cache_read_input_tokens":644758,"output_tokens":4996,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3305},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6856,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4996,"cache_read_input_tokens":644758,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6856},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PDMVAQEofws9H9ojaEXPaW":{"command":"c