racines\\\".\",\"fix\":\"Narrow item 3. Say that the MM-03 hypotheses (WF3, NoDangling, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive) are proved on reached states. Say that `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK`, `TokCompat`, `MM02.WF`, `DecAlong` and the one-root hypothesis of `r6_alloc` remain open obligations, with `alloc ok` of a multi-root shape outside what is proved (see (d) 2 and (d) 4).\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reason\":\"The finding holds. Item 3 of the report (formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:26-27) says: \\\"R1, R2, R4 et R6 sont prouvés dans le périmètre de K4, sous des hypothèses explicites listées en (b), qui sont prouvées sur les états atteints.\\\" The relative clause after the comma applies to every hypothesis listed in (b). Section (b) only claims this for the MM-03 hypotheses: \\\"Les hypothèses MM-03 (`WF3`, `NoDangling`, `FpLeaves`, `FrameOwnedLive`) valent sur tout état atteint\\\". The R6 hypotheses that (b) itself lists are not discharged anywhere: `PlacementOK`, `NewLayout`, `FreeSound`, `TokCompat`, MM-02 `WF`, `DecAlong` and `rootIdx ls = [i]`. The report admits this in (d) 4: \\\"`FreeSound`, `PlacementOK` et `NewLayout` restent des hypothèses ... rien n'établit ni ne conserve `FreeSound` le long des pas\\\". It also admits in (d) 2 that R6 is not stated for \\\"`alloc` d'une forme à plusieurs racines\\\". The one-root hypothesis of `r6_alloc` fails on a reached `alloc ok` step, so item 3 overstates what is proved.\",\"evidence\":\"1. Signature of `r6_alloc` (formal/Ern/MM23.lean:1512-1518) has the hypotheses `(hwf2 : MM02.WF s2) (hpl : PlacementOK pl) ... (hone : rootIdx ls = [i]) (hNL : NewLayout L s3'.P s3.P.length s2.next g [i])`.\\n\\n2. `r6_free` (line ~1554) assumes `(hfs : FreeSound k C L s3 s2 p auth)`. `r6_enter` (line ~1597) assumes `MM02.WF s2`, `PlacementOK pl` and `NewLayout`. `r6_exit` / `r6_exit_reachable` (line 1767) assume `(htc : TokCompat C tok)`.\\n\\n3. `grep -n \\\"theorem.*reachable\\\"` on MM23.lean returns only these: `reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive`, `r1_read3_reachable`, `r2_write3_reachable`, `r2_writeShared_reachable` and `r6_exit_reachable`. No reachable version exists for `r6_alloc`, `r6_free` or `r6_enter`, and no theorem proves `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK` or `TokCompat` on reached states. `r6_exit_reachable` still takes `htc : TokCompat C tok` as a hypothesis.\\n\\n4. I reran the scratch check verif/e12b.lean (`theorem rb : Reachable KC st e12b := .alloc r11 (.ok (by decide) (by decide) : AllocStep KC 1 2 [(none, none, 0), (none, none, 0)] e11 (.ok e12b))`, plus `example : rootIdx [...] = [0, 1] := by decide`) with `cd formal &amp;&amp; ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean .../verif/e12b.lean`. It compiles with no errors and prints \\\"'rb' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\\". So a reached `alloc ok` step has `rootIdx ls = [0, 1]`, and `hone : rootIdx ls = [i]` cannot hold there.\\n\\n5. `git log -L26,27:formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` shows the sentence was introduced in 0dcbf43, which is part of this pass.\"}},{\"lens\":\"facts\",\"id\":\"F2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:29-35 (Résultats principaux, item 4)\",\"claim\":\"Item 4 says the MM03 draft departs from its text \\\"sur trois points, qui conditionnent R1 et R2\\\". (f) lists four MM03 gaps, and the third point (multi-root `alloc`) does not bear on R1 or R2. It bears on R6 for `alloc`.\",\"evidence\":\"Report (f), lines 281-307, lists points 1-4 under \\\"`Ern/MM03.lean` (brouillon) contre MM-03.3 v0.3\\\". Point 4 is that `free`/`endUse` do not mark all dying owned storage dead. `r1_read3` (MM23.lean:951-957), `r2_write3` (981-986) and `r2_writeShared` (994-999) have no hypothesis on `alloc` shapes. The one-root hypothesis appears only in `r6_alloc`, as `hone : rootIdx ls = [i]` (line 1517).\",\"fix\":\"Say that the draft departs on four points (f 1-4). Say that points 1-2 condition R1/R2, point 3 conditions R6 for `alloc`, and point 4 has no effect on `Repr`.\",\"verdict\":{\"real\":true,\"reason\":\"Confirmed. Report item 4 (line 29) says: \\\"Le brouillon `MM03` s'écarte de son texte sur trois points, qui conditionnent R1 et R2\\\". Section (f) of the same report (lines 281-307) lists four MM03 departures. The third point in item 4 (multi-root `alloc`, line 32) does not condition R1 or R2. It conditions only R6 for `alloc`, and the report says so itself at line 224 and in the `r6_alloc` row at line 106. The fourth point in (f) (free/endUse) is missing from item 4, so \\\"trois points\\\" understates the count.\",\"evidence\":\"- Report line 29: \\\"s'écarte de son texte sur trois points, qui conditionnent R1 et R2\\\". Line 32 gives the third point: \\\"`alloc` accepte des formes à plusieurs racines.\\\"\\n- Report (f), lines 281-307, lists items numbered 1, 2, 3 and 4. Item 4: \\\"`free` et `endUse` ne marquent pas morts tous les stockages possédés qui cessent de vivre\\\".\\n- MM23.lean, lines 951-999:\\n  - `r1_read3` hypotheses: `hwf : WF3 s3`, `hnd : NoDangling s3`, `hfl : FpLeaves s3`, `hR : Repr ...`, `h : Read3Step ...`, `hstat`, `hdec`.\\n  - `r2_write3` and `r2_writeShared` take the same kind of hypotheses.\\n  - None of the three mentions `AllocStep` or `rootIdx`.\\n- `grep -n rootIdx Ern/MM23.lean`: the one-root hypothesis appears only at line 1517, `(hone : rootIdx ls = [i])`, in `r6_alloc`.\\n- The invariants R1/R2 rely on do not depend on single-root alloc either:\\n  - `reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive` (MM23.lean:1233) has no shape hypothesis.\\n  - It is proven over `MM03.Reachable` (MM03.lean:8343-8379), whose `alloc` constructor accepts any `AllocStep k pr ow ls`, multi-root included.\\n- The report itself ties the alloc point to R6:\\n  - Line 106 lists \\\"forme à une racine (`rootIdx ls = [i]`)\\\" as a hypothesis of `r6_alloc` only.\\n  - Line 224 reads \\\"ni pour `alloc` d'une forme à plusieurs racines (question (e) 2)\\\". This is in the R6 coverage discussion.\"}},{\"lens\":\"facts\",\"id\":\"F3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:74-77 ((b) preamble)\",\"claim\":\"The preamble says \\\"Les hypothèses MM-02 sont les mêmes partout\\\": `dec` along the sequence (`DecAlong`) and `stat`. This does not match the signatures. Several listed theorems take no `dec`/`stat` hypothesis. `r6_alloc` and `r6_enter` take other MM-02 hypotheses. R1 and `r6_read3` state `dec` without `DecAlong`.\",\"evidence\":\"`r6_alloc` (1515-1518) has hwf, hR, hwf2 : MM02.WF s2, hpl : PlacementOK pl, hg, h, hone, hNL, with no hstat/hdec. `r6_enter` (1597-1599) also has `MM02.WF s2` and `PlacementOK`. `r6_free` (1554-1555), `r6_exit` (1639-1641), `r6_alloc_fail` (1544-1545), `r6_noStep` (1730), `r4_no_dead_cover` (1778) and `exclusive_bytes` (1798-1802) have no `dec` or `stat`. `r1_read3`/`r6_read3` take `hdec : ∀ l ∈ ls, O\n... (truncated 34656 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wtpp0z3oo.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_c73b77b1-150/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/mm23-report-verification-wf_c73b77b1-150.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_c73b77b1-150'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>19</agent_count><agents_done>19</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>2087962</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>217</tool_uses><d