{"parentUuid":"a2d02962-9903-4620-9fa3-993d15954c03","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9a916e16-61ce-465a-8d9a-4586ef4170cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013BxsYSid7onMpgxvoYLGtR","type":"tool_result","content":"CONFIRMED 10\n\n## facts/F1 [major] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:26-27 (Résultats principaux, item 3)\nCLAIM: Item 3 says R1, R2, R4 and R6 are proved within the scope of K4, under hypotheses listed in (b) \"qui sont prouvées sur les états atteints\". This is false. Only the MM-03 hypotheses (WF3, NoDangling, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive) are discharged on reached states. The R6 hypotheses are not: `rootIdx ls = [i]`, `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK`, `TokCompat`, `MM02.WF` and `DecAlong`. One of them, `rootIdx ls = [i]`, fails on a reached `alloc ok` step, so R6 is not proved for all of K4's `alloc ok` case.\nFIX: Narrow item 3. Say that the MM-03 hypotheses (WF3, NoDangling, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive) are proved on reached states. Say that `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK`, `TokCompat`, `MM02.WF`, `DecAlong` and the one-root hypothesis of `r6_alloc` remain open obligations, with `alloc ok` of a multi-root shape outside what is proved (see (d) 2 and (d) 4).\n\n## facts/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:29-35 (Résultats principaux, item 4)\nCLAIM: Item 4 says the MM03 draft departs from its text \"sur trois points, qui conditionnent R1 et R2\". (f) lists four MM03 gaps, and the third point (multi-root `alloc`) does not bear on R1 or R2. It bears on R6 for `alloc`.\nFIX: Say that the draft departs on four points (f 1-4). Say that points 1-2 condition R1/R2, point 3 conditions R6 for `alloc`, and point 4 has no effect on `Repr`.\n\n## facts/F3 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:74-77 ((b) preamble)\nCLAIM: The preamble says \"Les hypothèses MM-02 sont les mêmes partout\": `dec` along the sequence (`DecAlong`) and `stat`. This does not match the signatures. Several listed theorems take no `dec`/`stat` hypothesis. `r6_alloc` and `r6_enter` take other MM-02 hypotheses. R1 and `r6_read3` state `dec` without `DecAlong`.\nFIX: Say that `dec`/`stat` are hypotheses of R1, R2, `r6_read3` and `repr_init` only. For reads, give `dec` as a per-leaf hypothesis on `s2`. List `MM02.WF` and `PlacementOK` as MM-02 hypotheses of `r6_alloc`/`r6_enter`, as the R6 table already does.\n\n## facts/F5 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:92 ((b), R2 witnesses)\nCLAIM: The report gives \"écritures des feuilles 1, 2, 4\" as R2 witnesses. The module has no R2 witness for the write of leaf 2. `r2_write3`/`r2_write3_reachable` is never applied to it, and no example states `AllOk` for its sequence `ops3`.\nFIX: Either add an application of `r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r2 ...` to `Write3Step 2 [2] e2 (.ok e3)`, or change the report to \"feuilles 1 et 4\".\n\n## decisions/F1 [major] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, (c) 4, exitFrame bullet; formal/Ern/MM23.lean, Repr.leaked (l.121-123)\nCLAIM: The exitFrame bullet of (c) 4 has two problems. It cites a witness that does not show the claim. It also presents the LiveAlloc requirement for owned storage that dies at exitFrame as imposed by K4, but that requirement is a choice.\nFIX: Replace the witness « allocation 4 du scénario » with CaseOwnedLocal.o3' (local 1, `LiveAlloc (exec n1 (exitOps L tk o1)) 1`), or add a scenario where allocated storage dies at exitFrame without endUse. Rephrase « K4 l'impose »: K4 rules out requiring a dead allocation, and requiring a live one is a choice. List the alternative (leave such roots unconstrained) in (c) 4 or (e).\n\n## decisions/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, (c) 1\nCLAIM: The justification « Un paramètre inutilisé déclencherait l'avertissement unusedVariables » is false. Lean's unusedVariables linter does not report unused structure parameters.\nFIX: Drop the linter argument. Keep the actual reason: no clause of K3 reads K, which is already (e) 3.\n\n## deviations/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, Revue adverse, reviewer « Repr », finding 4 (lines 338-339); formal/Ern/MM23.lean Cases.Lsa and m3x (lines 2114-2124)\nCLAIM: The treatment says that Lsa and Lwi are tests \"où seule la clause visée échoue\". That holds for Lwi. Lsa does not isolate K1 (a) as the reason Repr fails: its layout also breaks the `tokens` clause of Repr. The reviewer's concern, that no negative test rejected Repr through K1 (a), is therefore not fully addressed.\nFIX: Make the fresh allocation carry the frame token, for example m3y := exec m3 [.alloc 0 (topPlacement m3 (g 0)) 8 4 (some 101)]. Then `decide (ReprNoA tk Lsa e6 m3y) = true` (checked), so Repr fails by K1 (a) only. Alternatively, reword the treatment to say that Lsa isolates (a) among the clauses of LayoutWF, not of Repr.\n\n## deviations/F3 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, Résultats principaux item 4 (lines 29-35) against section (f) (lines 279-307)\nCLAIM: The summary says the MM03 draft differs from its text \"sur trois points, qui conditionnent R1 et R2\". Section (f) lists four MM03 gaps, (f) 4 being freeS/endUseS. The third summarized point, multi-root `alloc`, conditions R6 for `alloc`, not R1 or R2.\nFIX: Reword item 4: the first two points condition R1/R2; the third conditions R6 for `alloc` (hypothesis `hone`); (f) 4 (freeS/endUseS dead marks) has no effect on Repr. Make the count match (f), including any WF3 gaps added under F1.\n\n## fixes/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:25-27 (Résultats principaux 3)\nCLAIM: The summary says the explicit hypotheses of R1, R2, R4 and R6 listed in (b) are proved on the reached states. That is overstated. Several hypotheses in (b) are not discharged on reached states: FreeSound (the hypothesis this commit narrowed), PlacementOK, NewLayout, TokCompat and dec/DecAlong. The report's own section (d) 4 says so.\nFIX: Restrict the sentence to the MM-03 hypotheses (WF3, NoDangling, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive), and state that FreeSound, PlacementOK, NewLayout, TokCompat and dec remain open obligations, pointing to (d) 4.\n\n## fixes/F3 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:29-35 (Résultats principaux 4) vs :299-307 ((f) 4)\nCLAIM: The summary says the MM03 draft departs from its text on three points that condition R1 and R2. Section (f) lists four MM03 gaps. The fourth, (f) 4, was added in this commit from the review, with witness Cases.af14, and the summary was not updated. Also, the third listed point (alloc accepting shapes with several roots) conditions r6_alloc through its hypothesis `rootIdx ls = [i]`, not R1 or R2.\nFIX: Say four points, add (f) 4 to the summary (it affects no theorem, since Usable and Repr do not depend on it), and attribute the multi-root alloc point to R6 for alloc.\n\nREFUTED 5\n- facts/F4: The R4 bullet gives its premises as \"Sur un état atteint en Repr\". It leaves out `DDSound k`, a hypothesis of `r4_no_dead_cover`. The task puts `DDSound` réel out of scope, so this is a real extra ass || The finding is not real. Taken alone, the R4 bullet does leave out `DDSound k`. But section (b) of the report says, a few lines above the bullet, that the MM-03 hypotheses hold on reached states only under `DDSound k`, and the summary points the read\n- decisions/F3: (c) 5 justifies `Repr.inj` by K2 « ↔ », but Repr encodes only one direction: distinct roots map to distinct allocations. Nothing requires every MM-02 allocation to correspond to a root, so Repr accept || The Lean facts in the finding are correct: Repr does accept a live MM-02 allocation that no root maps to. The conclusion drawn from them does not hold. The report never claims that Repr enforces a converse. (c) 5 names the direction it encodes in its\n- decisions/F4: (c) 18 calls `MM02.WF s2` « Admissibilité MM-02 » and justifies it with « MM-02.2 restreint la sémantique aux états admissibles ». MM02.WF is only the freshness component, not admissibility, so the la || This is imprecise wording in a heading, not a false or overstated claim. Item (c) 18 names the exact hypothesis (`MM02.WF s2`), and every factual statement in it checks out. The justification is valid: MM-02.2 limits the semantics to admissible state\n- deviations/F1: (f) lists only clause 4 of §2.1 as a gap of the draft WF3, but WF3, which every R1/R2/R6 theorem of MM23 takes as a hypothesis, also leaves out §2.1 clause 7 (RootHeld) and the well-foundedness of pos || The facts about the draft are correct, but the report is not wrong or overstated. The draft WF3 does accept a usable root place with no root authority, and it accepts an ownership cycle. However, the report never claims that (f) lists every MM03 devi\n- fixes/F1: The fix for the reviewer's finding that no test rejected by K1 (a) or (c) is described as tests where only the targeted clause fails. That holds for Lsa only among the three LayoutWF clauses. At the l || The Lean facts in the finding are correct, but they don't show that the report is wrong or overstated. The report's line 338 says the tests Lsa and Lwi are cases where \"seule la clause visée échoue\". The targeted clause is a K1 clause, meaning a sub-\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"334f7983-4009-4af9-a401-77beff037002","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:16:22.295Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"CONFIRMED 10\n\n## facts/F1 [major] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:26-27 (Résultats principaux, item 3)\nCLAIM: Item 3 says R1, R2, R4 and R6 are proved within the scope of K4, under hypotheses listed in (b) \"qui sont prouvées sur les états atteints\". This is false. Only the MM-03 hypotheses (WF3, NoDangling, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive) are discharged on reached states. The R6 hypotheses are not: `rootIdx ls = [i]`, `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK`, `TokCompat`, `MM02.WF` and `DecAlong`. One of them, `rootIdx ls = [i]`, fails on a reached `alloc ok` step, so R6 is not proved for all of K4's `alloc ok` case.\nFIX: Narrow item 3. Say that the MM-03 hypotheses (WF3, NoDangling, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive) are proved on reached states. Say that `FreeSound`, `NewLayout`, `PlacementOK`, `TokCompat`, `MM02.WF`, `DecAlong` and the one-root hypothesis of `r6_alloc` remain open obligations, with `alloc ok` of a multi-root shape outside what is proved (see (d) 2 and (d) 4).\n\n## facts/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:29-35 (Résultats principaux, item 4)\nCLAIM: Item 4 says the MM03 draft departs from its text \"sur trois points, qui conditionnent R1 et R2\". (f) lists four MM03 gaps, and the third point (multi-root `alloc`) does not bear on R1 or R2. It bears on R6 for `alloc`.\nFIX: Say that the draft departs on four points (f 1-4). Say that points 1-2 condition R1/R2, point 3 conditions R6 for `alloc`, and point 4 has no effect on `Repr`.\n\n## facts/F3 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:74-77 ((b) preamble)\nCLAIM: The preamble says \"Les hypothèses MM-02 sont les mêmes partout\": `dec` along the sequence (`DecAlong`) and `stat`. This does not match the signatures. Several listed theorems take no `dec`/`stat` hypothesis. `r6_alloc` and `r6_enter` take other MM-02 hypotheses. R1 and `r6_read3` state `dec` without `DecAlong`.\nFIX: Say that `dec`/`stat` are hypotheses of R1, R2, `r6_read3` and `repr_init` only. For reads, give `dec` as a per-leaf hypothesis on `s2`. List `MM02.WF` and `PlacementOK` as MM-02 hypotheses of `r6_alloc`/`r6_enter`, as the R6 table already does.\n\n## facts/F5 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:92 ((b), R2 witnesses)\nCLAIM: The report gives \"écritures des feuilles 1, 2, 4\" as R2 witnesses. The module has no R2 witness for the write of leaf 2. `r2_write3`/`r2_write3_reachable` is never applied to it, and no example states `AllOk` for its sequence `ops3`.\nFIX: Either add an application of `r2_write3_reachable kc_dd r2 ...` to `Write3Step 2 [2] e2 (.ok e3)`, or change the report to \"feuilles 1 et 4\".\n\n## decisions/F1 [major] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, (c) 4, exitFrame bullet; formal/Ern/MM23.lean, Repr.leaked (l.121-123)\nCLAIM: The exitFrame bullet of (c) 4 has two problems. It cites a witness that does not show the claim. It also presents the LiveAlloc requirement for owned storage that dies at exitFrame as imposed by K4, but that requirement is a choice.\nFIX: Replace the witness « allocation 4 du scénario » with CaseOwnedLocal.o3' (local 1, `LiveAlloc (exec n1 (exitOps L tk o1)) 1`), or add a scenario where allocated storage dies at exitFrame without endUse. Rephrase « K4 l'impose »: K4 rules out requiring a dead allocation, and requiring a live one is a choice. List the alternative (leave such roots unconstrained) in (c) 4 or (e).\n\n## decisions/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, (c) 1\nCLAIM: The justification « Un paramètre inutilisé déclencherait l'avertissement unusedVariables » is false. Lean's unusedVariables linter does not report unused structure parameters.\nFIX: Drop the linter argument. Keep the actual reason: no clause of K3 reads K, which is already (e) 3.\n\n## deviations/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, Revue adverse, reviewer « Repr », finding 4 (lines 338-339); formal/Ern/MM23.lean Cases.Lsa and m3x (lines 2114-2124)\nCLAIM: The treatment says that Lsa and Lwi are tests \"où seule la clause visée échoue\". That holds for Lwi. Lsa does not isolate K1 (a) as the reason Repr fails: its layout also breaks the `tokens` clause of Repr. The reviewer's concern, that no negative test rejected Repr through K1 (a), is therefore not fully addressed.\nFIX: Make the fresh allocation carry the frame token, for example m3y := exec m3 [.alloc 0 (topPlacement m3 (g 0)) 8 4 (some 101)]. Then `decide (ReprNoA tk Lsa e6 m3y) = true` (checked), so Repr fails by K1 (a) only. Alternatively, reword the treatment to say that Lsa isolates (a) among the clauses of LayoutWF, not of Repr.\n\n## deviations/F3 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md, Résultats principaux item 4 (lines 29-35) against section (f) (lines 279-307)\nCLAIM: The summary says the MM03 draft differs from its text \"sur trois points, qui conditionnent R1 et R2\". Section (f) lists four MM03 gaps, (f) 4 being freeS/endUseS. The third summarized point, multi-root `alloc`, conditions R6 for `alloc`, not R1 or R2.\nFIX: Reword item 4: the first two points condition R1/R2; the third conditions R6 for `alloc` (hypothesis `hone`); (f) 4 (freeS/endUseS dead marks) has no effect on Repr. Make the count match (f), including any WF3 gaps added under F1.\n\n## fixes/F2 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:25-27 (Résultats principaux 3)\nCLAIM: The summary says the explicit hypotheses of R1, R2, R4 and R6 listed in (b) are proved on the reached states. That is overstated. Several hypotheses in (b) are not discharged on reached states: FreeSound (the hypothesis this commit narrowed), PlacementOK, NewLayout, TokCompat and dec/DecAlong. The report's own section (d) 4 says so.\nFIX: Restrict the sentence to the MM-03 hypotheses (WF3, NoDangling, FpLeaves, FrameOwnedLive), and state that FreeSound, PlacementOK, NewLayout, TokCompat and dec remain open obligations, pointing to (d) 4.\n\n## fixes/F3 [minor] formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md:29-35 (Résultats principaux 4) vs :299-307 ((f) 4)\nCLAIM: The summary says the MM03 draft departs from its text on three points that condition R1 and R2. Section (f) lists four MM03 gaps. The fourth, (f) 4, was added in this commit from the review, with witness Cases.af14, and the summary was not updated. Also, the third listed point (alloc accepting shapes with several roots) conditions r6_alloc through its hypothesis `rootIdx ls = [i]`, not R1 or R2.\nFIX: Say four points, add (f) 4 to the summary (it affects no theorem, since Usable and Repr do not depend on it), and attribute the multi-root alloc point to R6 for alloc.\n\nREFUTED 5\n- facts/F4: The R4 bullet gives its premises as \"Sur un état atteint en Repr\". It leaves out `DDSound k`, a hypothesis of `r4_no_dead_cover`. The task puts `DDSound` réel out of scope, so this is a real extra ass || The finding is not real. Taken alone, the R4 bullet does leave out `DDSound k`. But section (b) of the report says, a few lines above the bullet, that the MM-03 hypotheses hold on reached states only under `DDSound k`, and the summary points the read\n- decisions/F3: (c) 5 justifies `Repr.inj` by K2 « ↔ », but Repr encodes only one direction: distinct roots map to distinct allocations. Nothing requires every MM-02 allocation to correspond to a root, so Repr accept || The Lean facts in the finding are correct: Repr does accept a live MM-02 allocation that no root maps to. The conclusion drawn from them does not hold. The report never claims that Repr enforces a converse. (c) 5 names the direction it encodes in its\n- decisions/F4: (c) 18 calls `MM02.WF s2` « Admissibilité MM-02 » and justifies it with « MM-02.2 restreint la sémantique aux états admissibles ». MM02.WF is only the freshness component, not admissibility, so the la || This is imprecise wording in a heading, not a false or overstated claim. Item (c) 18 names the exact hypothesis (`MM02.WF s2`), and every factual statement in it checks out. The justification is valid: MM-02.2 limits the semantics to admissible state\n- deviations/F1: (f) lists only clause 4 of §2.1 as a gap of the draft WF3, but WF3, which every R1/R2/R6 theorem of MM23 takes as a hypothesis, also leaves out §2.1 clause 7 (RootHeld) and the well-foundedness of pos || The facts about the draft are correct, but the report is not wrong or overstated. The draft WF3 does accept a usable root place with no root authority, and it accepts an ownership cycle. However, the report never claims that (f) lists every MM03 devi\n- fixes/F1: The fix for the reviewer's finding that no test rejected by K1 (a) or (c) is described as tests where only the targeted clause fails. That holds for Lsa only among the three LayoutWF clauses. At the l || The Lean facts in the finding are correct, but they don't show that the report is wrong or overstated. The report's line 338 says the tests Lsa and Lwi are cases where \"seule la clause visée échoue\". The targeted clause is a K1 clause, meaning a sub-","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"23cd254c-26f5-46c2-9364-a5a3999def14","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2d02962-9903-4620-9fa3-993d15954c03","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
