{"parentUuid":"66f99fce-3002-484d-9988-af10f9ebb303","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9a916e16-61ce-465a-8d9a-4586ef4170cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0175Nb1ccS97hTmgwzZsNEZy","type":"tool_result","content":"(f) lists only clause 4 of §2.1 as a gap of the draft WF3, but WF3, which every R1/R2/R6 theorem of MM23 takes as a hypothesis, also leaves out §2.1 clause 7 (RootHeld) and the well-foundedness of possession chains in clause 3. Neither gap is reported.\nEVIDENCE: Spec §2.1 clause 7: \"RootHeld : chaque emplacement racine utilisable possède son autorité racine Modify active, sans origine, détenue exactement par son propriétaire\". Clause 3: \"des chaînes de possession bien fondées\". The draft's RootHeld (MM03.lean:1705) only constrains authorities that already exist: \"∀ x z l r, s.A[x]? = some z → z.origin = none → l ∈ z.footprint → … → z.holder = pr.owner\". It never asks a root authority to exist. Clause 3 of the draft only checks `o < s.P.length`. The scratch file /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/verif/zz_lens_f_check.lean compiles. Axioms are [propext, Quot.sound]. It proves: `wf_noRoot : WF3 sNoRoot`, where sNoRoot has one place ⟨none, .frame 0, 0⟩ and A = []; `noRoot_usable : RootPlace sNoRoot.P 0 ∧ sNoRoot.Usable 0 ∧ sNoRoot.A = []`; `noRoot_not_rootLive : ¬ RootLive sNoRoot`. It also proves `wf_cyc : WF3 sCyc`, where sCyc has P = [⟨none, .place 1, 0⟩, ⟨none, .place 0, 0⟩], an ownership cycle. So the draft WF3 accepts states that the text's WF3 rejects. MM23 does not use these clauses (grep finds only hwf.fp, hwf.nodup, hwf.ownerOf, hwf.parent), so no theorem is weakened. Still, (f) 2 counts this exact kind of WF3 gap (clause 4) as a deviation, and Résultats principaux says the draft differs \"sur trois points\".\nFIX: Add to (f) under Ern/MM03.lean: the draft WF3 does not require a usable root to have its active Modify root authority (§2.1 clause 7; RootLive holds only on reached states, via reachable_rootLive). It also does not require well-founded possession chains (§2.1 clause 3). Cite the witnesses sNoRoot and sCyc, and say that MM23 does not depend on these clauses.\nauth.lean\nax1.lean\nax1.out\nax2.lean\ne12b.lean\nf2_unused.lean\nf3.lean\nmm23_compile.out\nnames.lean\npub_nongen.txt\nrefute_f1.lean\nthm_names.txt\nv1.lean\nv2.lean\nv3.lean\nv4.lean\nw.lean\nzz_lens_f_check.lean\nzz_lens_f_check2.lean\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ef1d6a05-a25a-4b87-bafd-ab2fc5be6daa","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:16:46.151Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"(f) lists only clause 4 of §2.1 as a gap of the draft WF3, but WF3, which every R1/R2/R6 theorem of MM23 takes as a hypothesis, also leaves out §2.1 clause 7 (RootHeld) and the well-foundedness of possession chains in clause 3. Neither gap is reported.\nEVIDENCE: Spec §2.1 clause 7: \"RootHeld : chaque emplacement racine utilisable possède son autorité racine Modify active, sans origine, détenue exactement par son propriétaire\". Clause 3: \"des chaînes de possession bien fondées\". The draft's RootHeld (MM03.lean:1705) only constrains authorities that already exist: \"∀ x z l r, s.A[x]? = some z → z.origin = none → l ∈ z.footprint → … → z.holder = pr.owner\". It never asks a root authority to exist. Clause 3 of the draft only checks `o < s.P.length`. The scratch file /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/verif/zz_lens_f_check.lean compiles. Axioms are [propext, Quot.sound]. It proves: `wf_noRoot : WF3 sNoRoot`, where sNoRoot has one place ⟨none, .frame 0, 0⟩ and A = []; `noRoot_usable : RootPlace sNoRoot.P 0 ∧ sNoRoot.Usable 0 ∧ sNoRoot.A = []`; `noRoot_not_rootLive : ¬ RootLive sNoRoot`. It also proves `wf_cyc : WF3 sCyc`, where sCyc has P = [⟨none, .place 1, 0⟩, ⟨none, .place 0, 0⟩], an ownership cycle. So the draft WF3 accepts states that the text's WF3 rejects. MM23 does not use these clauses (grep finds only hwf.fp, hwf.nodup, hwf.ownerOf, hwf.parent), so no theorem is weakened. Still, (f) 2 counts this exact kind of WF3 gap (clause 4) as a deviation, and Résultats principaux says the draft differs \"sur trois points\".\nFIX: Add to (f) under Ern/MM03.lean: the draft WF3 does not require a usable root to have its active Modify root authority (§2.1 clause 7; RootLive holds only on reached states, via reachable_rootLive). It also does not require well-founded possession chains (§2.1 clause 3). Cite the witnesses sNoRoot and sCyc, and say that MM23 does not depend on these clauses.\nauth.lean\nax1.lean\nax1.out\nax2.lean\ne12b.lean\nf2_unused.lean\nf3.lean\nmm23_compile.out\nnames.lean\npub_nongen.txt\nrefute_f1.lean\nthm_names.txt\nv1.lean\nv2.lean\nv3.lean\nv4.lean\nw.lean\nzz_lens_f_check.lean\nzz_lens_f_check2.lean","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"82765077-9c57-473c-ac56-1a09686abdc8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"66f99fce-3002-484d-9988-af10f9ebb303","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop",