r₂ x : Nat}, partOf s.P r₁ src → partOf s.P r₂ src → corr s.P src dst r₁ = some x → corr s.P src dst r₂ = some x → r₁ = r₂\\n```\\n- **Exact match:** in a copy of the file, three `example`s typed with the task's exact statements and original binder names (`hw`, `hs`, `hno`) were each proved by applying the theorem directly. They compiled with no output and exit code 0.\\n- **Nothing added or weakened:** no hypothesis was added, and none of the three conclusions is weaker than required.\\n- **Renamed hypotheses:** the only difference is the declared rename of three unused hypotheses (`_hw` in `corr_leaf_back`; `_hs` and `_hno` in `corr_inj`). Their types are unchanged.\\n- **New definitions:** the file defines no `def`, so none of `corr`, `SameShape`, `overlap`, `footprint` or `partOf` is redefined; all come from MM03.\\n\\n**(4) Forbidden tokens.** This grep found nothing (exit code 1):\\n```\\ngrep -nE '\\\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide|noncomputable)\\\\b|^\\\\s*axiom\\\\b|#print|#eval|set_option' corr_leaves.lean\\ngrep exit 1\\n```\\nThe file has no leftover `#print` lines.\\n\\nThe 12 theorem names do not exist as declarations in `formal/Ern/MM03.lean` or `formal/Ern/MM23.lean` (grep exit code 1).\\n\\nThe copy now holds the statement-match examples rather than the `#print axioms` lines (the axiom output above came from the earlier run on it). I did not compare the docstring citations against the spec text in `~/Downloads`. Because `formal/Ern/MM23.lean` is being edited concurrently, its name-collision check should be repeated at merge time.\"},{\"key\":\"pinned\",\"file\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work/pinned_live.lean\",\"prover\":\"File: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work/pinned_live.lean\\n\\nAll four statements are true and proved. No counterexample was needed.\\n\\nStatements proved (inside `name