{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","hash":"06146115e648cc7a83ae8c097e86abecf4206898e63db6ce927174e213e2cb55","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>wkfdh0aki</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01W3pdB4VuzVdimrRifEHGQE</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wkfdh0aki.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Prove two independent MM-03 lemma families for MM23 pass 2 in scratch files, then verify each\" completed</summary>\n<result>[{\"key\":\"corr\",\"file\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work/corr_leaves.lean\",\"prover\":\"All three theorems are proved in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work/corr_leaves.lean. Every theorem in the file depends only on propext and Quot.sound, and the final check command prints nothing.\\n\\n**One change to the requested text:** three hypotheses that no proof uses now start with an underscore (`_hw`, `_hs`, `_hno`). Otherwise the unused-variable linter warns, and the repo already uses this convention (for example `_hwf` in MM03.lean:4963). The types are unchanged. Any caller that passes these arguments by name, such as `(hw := …)`, would need the new names.\\n\\nStatements proved:\\n```lean\\ntheorem corr_leaf_fwd {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hd : dst &lt; s.P.length)\\n    (hsh : SameShape s.P src dst) {l : Nat} (hl : l ∈ footprint s.P src) :\\n    ∃ l', corr s.P src dst l = some l' ∧ l' ∈ footprint s.P dst\\n\\ntheorem corr_leaf_back {s : S3} (_hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat} (hsh : SameShape s.P src dst)\\n    {l' : Nat} (hl' : l' ∈ footprint s.P dst) :\\n    ∃ l ∈ footprint s.P src, corr s.P src dst l = some l'\\n\\ntheorem corr_inj {s : S3} (hw : WF3 s) {src dst : Nat}\\n    (_hs : src &lt; s.P.length) (hd : dst &lt; s.P.length) (_hno : ¬ overlap s.P src dst)\\n    {r₁ r₂ x : Nat} (h₁ : partOf s.P r₁ src) (h₂ : partOf s.P r₂ src)\\n    (e₁ : corr s.P src dst r₁ = some x) (e₂ : corr s.P src dst r₂ = some x) : r₁ = r₂\\n```\\n\\n- **`corr_inj` needs no extra hypothesis, not even SameShape.** It also does not use `_hs` or `_hno`; it needs only `hw` and `hd`. The proof is by induction. The image of a strict part of `src` has a parent that is a part of `dst`, so that image is never `dst` itself. For two strict parts, equal images have the same parent, so their parents are equal by induction. The child lists are strictly increasing, so the same position means the same child.\\n- **`corr_leaf_back` does not use `WF3`.** It follows from the two clauses of `SameShape` alone.\\n\\nHelper lemmas in the same file: `posIn_cons_eq`, `posIn_cons_ne`, `posIn_inj`, `index_inj_of_lt`, `kids_lt`, `partOf_parent_of_ne`, `corr_parent`, `corr_ne_dst`, `corr_inj_aux`. I named the parent lemma `partOf_parent_of_ne` because MM03.lean already has a different `partOf_parent` (line 4189). None of these names exists in MM03.lean or MM23.lean.\\n\\nSpec passage covered: `~/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md`, O4 precondition 2 (the ordered isomorphism). Each docstring cites MM-03.3 O4.2 / J1.\\n\\nFinal check (`cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal &amp;&amp; ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work/corr_leaves.lean`) output, exit code 0:\\n```\\n```\\n\\nI did not run `lake build` and did not touch the repository. `git status` already shows `formal/Ern/MM23.lean` modified and `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` deleted, from the other work running in parallel.\",\"verifier\":\"VERIFIED\\n\\nAll four checks pass. The file is /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work/corr_leaves.lean, and the axiom check copy is /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/p2work/check_corr_leaves.lean.\\n\\n**(1) Compile.** The check command printed nothing (no errors, no warnings) and exited with code 0:\\n```\\ncd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal &amp;&amp; ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean .../p2work/corr_leaves.lean\\nexit=0\\n```\\nThe file starts with `import Ern.MM03`, `open Ern.MM03`, `namespace Ern.MM23` and ends with `end Ern.MM23`. It does not import Ern.MM23.\\n\\n**(2) Axioms.** I added `#print axioms` for all 12 theorems to the copy. Exit code 0:\\n```\\n'Ern.MM23.posIn_cons_eq' depends on axioms: [propext]\\n'Ern.MM23.posIn_cons_ne' depends on axioms: [propext]\\n'Ern.MM23.posIn_inj' depends on axioms: [propext]\\n'Ern.MM23.index_inj_of_lt' depends on axioms: [propext]\\n'Ern.MM23.kids_lt' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n'Ern.MM23.partOf_parent_of_ne' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n'Ern.MM23.corr_parent' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n'Ern.MM23.corr_ne_dst' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n'Ern.MM23.corr_inj_aux' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n'Ern.MM23.corr_leaf_fwd' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n'Ern.MM23.corr_leaf_back' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n'Ern.MM23.corr_inj' depends on axioms: [propext, Quot.sound]\\n```\\nNone of them uses Classical.choice.\\n\\n**(3) Statements.** The `#check` output shows the thre