{"parentUuid":"57fc003e-e33c-4ce2-8524-6cf6dca143bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb5qRNjE9cpDhsG4QxPY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NR7Lc1w2nez9Rooi5FiBRc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern && git checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git add formal/Ern/MM23.lean && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nMM23 pass 2, step 2: R6 for transfer, store, issue (L6)\n\nWhy: arbitrage L6 maps transfer to per-leaf read+write copies with the\nbytes read (provenance included), store and issue to one write of the\nbytes of a pointer (ptrBytes), reset to no step.\n\nWhat:\n- Correspondence of the leaves of a transfer under SameShape:\n  corr_leaf_fwd, corr_leaf_back, corr_inj (no hypothesis beyond WF3 and\n  dst existing; proved in a scratch workflow, verified independently).\n- transferPairs, copyOps, transferOps; r6_transfer (ok outcomes, Repr\n  kept, via ReprB.transport for the change of owners);\n  transfer_copies: under SameSizeAlong, each destination range holds\n  exactly the bytes of its source range, value and provenance, and the\n  source ranges are unchanged.\n- PtrEnc / PtrEncOK (decode, provenance), regionAddr, regionProv,\n  ptrBytes, storeOps, issueOps; r6_store, r6_issue (ok, Repr, the range\n  holds the pointer bytes); ptr_target: the provenance of the pointer is\n  the live allocation of the first leaf of the region and its address is\n  base + offset of that leaf. reset stays in NoStep.\n\nHow proved: lake build clean; no sorry/admit/axiom/native_decide; the 203\ntheorem constants use at most propext and Quot.sound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit step 2 of pass 2"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":907366,"output_tokens":1266,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":505},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":439,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":907366,"cache_creation_input_tokens":439,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":439},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NR7Lc1w2nez9Rooi5FiBRc":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern && git checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git add formal/Ern/MM23.lean && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nMM23 pass 2, step 2: R6 for transfer, store, issue (L6)\n\nWhy: arbitrage L6 maps transfer to per-leaf read+write copies with the\nbytes read (provenance included), store and issue to one write of the\nbytes of a pointer (ptrBytes), reset to no step.\n\nWhat:\n- Correspondence of the leaves of a transfer under SameShape:\n  corr_leaf_fwd, corr_leaf_back, corr_inj (no hypothesis beyond WF3 and\n  dst existing; proved in a scratch workflow, verified independently).\n- transferPairs, copyOps, transferOps; r6_transfer (ok outcomes, Repr\n  kept, via ReprB.transport for the change of owners);\n  transfer_copies: under SameSizeAlong, each destination range holds\n  exactly the bytes of its source range, value and provenance, and the\n  source ranges are unchanged.\n- PtrEnc / PtrEncOK (decode, provenance), regionAddr, regionProv,\n  ptrBytes, storeOps, issueOps; r6_store, r6_issue (ok, Repr, the range\n  holds the pointer bytes); ptr_target: the provenance of the pointer is\n  the live allocation of the first leaf of the region and its address is\n  base + offset of that leaf. reset stays in NoStep.\n\nHow proved: lake build clean; no sorry/admit/axiom/native_decide; the 203\ntheorem constants use at most propext and Quot.sound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit step 2 of pass 2"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"476cae1f-ca1c-4e49-93fc-50bc1c3d7f1e","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb5qR4dAvLGDiwg4fJb6","requestRef":"f2dd726c-8adb-4c7a-bef0-1ce511433f9a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"14a41cc3-733f-46b9-b3ee-af93c7ed73be","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:13:40.740Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
