{"parentUuid":"7d7a52cf-72df-44c8-b018-ae047b3d9e09","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"afea6d65-2af9-420c-969b-b55d07c96f18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, Skill, Workflow, Write, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up, mcp__terminal__read_terminal</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Standing mode.** Earlier the user invoked `/ub-mode`. Under it I:\n     - work make it work → make it right → practice: TDD, the smallest change, commits often;\n     - keep a log of every action and its reason, and report that log at completion;\n     - do NOT push to main: the briefs' « Pas de merge, pas de PR » takes precedence.\n   - **Pass 1 (done).** Brief « Tâche : jalon 2, passe 1 — raffinement MM-03 → MM-02 (disposition, relation de représentation, accès, allocation, cadres) »:\n     - branch `formal/refinement_0.1` from `formal/access_model_0.1`; module `formal/Ern/MM23.lean`;\n     - report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md`;\n     - arbitrages K1–K5. All done and committed.\n   - **Pass 2 (current).** Brief « Tâche : jalon 2, passe 2 — raffinement MM-03 → MM-02 (transfer, store, issue, DDSound, épinglage, simulation) ».\n     - **Git:** « Même branche `formal/refinement_0.1`, à la suite. Pas de merge, pas de PR. Tout sous `formal/`. `Ern/MM02.lean` et `Ern/MM03.lean` inchangés ; tout ajout va dans `Ern/MM23.lean` ou un module voisin. »\n     - **Language:** code, docstrings, comments and commits in English; the report in French.\n     - **Arbitrages L1–L8 font foi:**\n       - **L1:** locals of `enterFrame` are owned directly by the frame (an owning element is out of the language, as a hypothesis or as an envelope); statics may be owned by statics; `K.Deallocable` is false on statics.\n       - **L2:** an `alloc` shape has exactly one root.\n       - **L3:** `MM02.WF s2` is a clause of `Repr`; `Repr` does not take `k`; `Moved`/`Uninit` leaves impose nothing.\n       - **L4:** the token of an allocated allocation is the provider's; ghost `provOf`; `FreeCompat p auth` is instantiated by `Compatible auth (ptok (provOf p))`; `freeSound_derived` replaces the `FreeSound` hypothesis, its content being the conservation of the token along the trace, imposed by `Repr`.\n       - **L5:** `free` maps to a single `DeallocStep`; owned storage leaks (the `leaked` clause is kept); same rule at exit.\n       - **L6:**\n         - `transfer` maps to a per-pair `ReadStep` then `WriteStep`, with the bytes read, provenance included; hypothesis `SameSizeAlong`;\n         - `store` maps to a `WriteStep` of `ptrBytes`, with the obligation that `decode` gives the address of the first leaf (base + offset) and that each byte's provenance is that region's allocation;\n         - `issue` maps to a `WriteStep` of `ptrBytes` of the block (provenance: the arena storage's allocation); `available`/`issued` are library state;\n         - `reset` maps to no step.\n       - **L7:** prove `ddSound_of_layout` (byte-disjointness instantiation satisfies `DDSound`; the obligation is classed « bibliothèque »).\n       - **L8:** prove `pinned_address_stable` (pinned leaf keeps a LIVE allocation and the same base+offset; the docstring says MM-02 models no physical move).\n     - **Steps (one commit each):**\n       1. L1–L5.\n       2. L6.\n       3. L7.\n       4. L8.\n       5. `simulation`: for every `Reachable` execution from `S3.init statics`, with L, placement, tokens and `ptrBytes` fixed once (never chosen per step), there is an MM-02 execution from `repr_init`'s initial state, all outcomes `ok`, in `Repr` at each step; the remaining hypotheses are listed in the statement.\n       6. Cases: one witness per new operation, plus a full execution (allocation, arena, emission, `store`, `transfer` to the caller, `free`, frame exit) translated step by step.\n     - **Out of scope:** concurrency, finite addresses (spec 11), arena metadata representation, low-level translation, fixes to the MM-03 draft.\n     - **Rules:**\n       - zero `sorry`; `#print axioms` ⊆ {propext, Quot.sound} on all module constants; no `noncomputable`; a build without warnings;\n       - docstrings cite the clause or arbitrage; nothing invented; no statement weakened; counterexamples kept;\n       - adversarial review centred on L4 (circularity), L6 (provenance or address lost or fabricated), L7, and the simulation (per-step parameters making it vacuous).\n     - **Deliverable:** `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md` with:\n       - (a) clause → declaration;\n       - (b) status of R1, R2, R4, R6 (full scope), `ddSound_of_layout`, `pinned_address_stable`, `freeSound_derived`, `simulation`;\n       - (c) decisions;\n       - (d) not proved;\n       - (e) questions;\n       - (f) final list of `simulation` hypotheses, each classed spec 4 (types) / spec 11 (ABI) / bibliothèque / ouverte.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Toolchain.** Lean 4 core v4.35, no Mathlib.\n     - Build with `~/.elan/bin/lake build` in `formal/`; scratch checks with `~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>`.\n     - Axiom checker: `$SP/mm23/axcheck.lean` walks module theorems with `collectAxioms`. Run it with `~/.elan/bin/lake env lean …/axcheck.lean`; it prints `theorems in Ern.MM23: N` and `outside propext, Quot.sound: #[]`.\n     - `SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad`.\n   - **Relation design.**\n     - `ReprB tok ptok provOf L s3 s2` is decidable, with fields lwf, inj, tokens, provTokens, live, init, freed, exited, leaked. Its instance needs `set_option synthInstance.maxSize 8192`.\n     - `Repr` extends `ReprB` with `wf2 : MM02.WF s2`, which is not decidable. Cases build it as `⟨by decide, wf_mX⟩`.\n   - **MM-02 sequences.**\n     - `Op2` with `eff`, `exec`, `Along`; `AllOk` = `Along OpOk`; `DecAlong` = `Along Op2.Dec`.\n     - Ops builders: `readOps`, `writeOps`, `allocOps`, `deallocOps`, `exitOps`, `copyOps`/`transferOps`, `storeOps`, `issueOps`, `initOps`.\n     - `Dom` (allocations kept) and `exec_wf`.\n   - **Simulation infrastructure.**\n     - `Op3`, `Step3` (envelope L1: `NoOwner`; L2: `∃ i, rootIdx ls = [i]`), `Exec3`, `Params` (`L`, `tok`, `ptok`, `pl`, `geom` by root place index, `pe`, `w0`), `assoc`, `provStep` (the ghost is updated by `alloc` only), `Trans` (canonical translation).\n     - `Oblig` = `LayoutObl` ∧ `DecAlong` ∧ `FreeOblig`; `SimRun` (`Trans` with per-step `Oblig` premises, init premises for the statics' layout and dec).\n     - `simulation` takes the global hypotheses `DDSound k`, `stat` (R and W), `PlacementOK`, alignments `hg : ∀ r, 0 < (π.geom r).align ∧ Pow2`, and `TokCompat C π.tok`.\n   - **Known pitfalls:**\n     - `omega` on conjunction goals pulls in `Classical.choice`.\n     - `meta` is a keyword.\n     - Mathlib's `set` doesn't exist.\n     - `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`ite_cond_eq_true` are deprecated; use `simp only [h, ↓reduceIte]`.\n     - `S3.Usable.mono` needs `(s := …) (s' := …)` given explicitly.\n     - Dot notation `hr.ofStep` fails because `Reachable.ofStep` lives in `Ern.MM23`.\n     - `formal/Ern/.gitkeep` keeps showing as deleted: restore it with `git checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep` before committing.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`formal/Ern/MM23.lean`** (main module, about 3400 lines; 303 theorem constants after step 5).\n     - **Step 1:** `ReprB` / `Repr`.\n       ```lean\n       structure Repr (tok ptok : Nat → Nat) (provOf : Nat → Option Nat) (L : Layout) (s3 : S3)\n           (s2 : MM02.State) : Prop extends ReprB tok ptok provOf L s3 s2 where\n         wf2 : MM02.WF s2\n       ```\n       - `provTokens : ∀ r < s3.P.length, RootPlace s3.P r → OptP (provOf r) (fun pr => ∀ l ∈ footprint s3.P r, AllocP s2 (L l).alloc (·.freeAuth = some (ptok pr))) True`.\n       - `freeSound_derived (hR : ReprB …) (hp : RootPlace s3.P p) (hfc : k.FreeCompat p auth → FreeCompatInst C ptok provOf p auth) : FreeSound k C L s3 s2 p auth`.\n       - `FreeCompatInst C ptok provOf p auth := ∃ pr, provOf p = some pr ∧ C auth (ptok pr)`.\n     - **R6 restatements:**\n       - `r6_alloc`: hypotheses `hR : Repr …`, `hpl`, `hg`, `h`, `hone : rootIdx ls = [i]`, `hprov : provOf (s3.P.length + i) = some pr`, `hNL`; the ops end in `(some (ptok pr))`.\n       - `r6_free`: takes `hfc : k.FreeCompat p auth → FreeCompatInst …`.\n       - `r6_enter`: takes `hprov : ∀ i ∈ rootIdx ls, provOf (s3.P.length + i) = none`; the `hwf2` hypothesis is dropped.\n       - `repr_init`: takes `hprov : ∀ i ∈ rootIdx (statics.map (·.1)), provOf i = none` and concludes `Repr`.\n     - **Step 2:** `transfer_copies` says that each destination range equals the initial source range and that source ranges are unchanged, under `SameSizeAlong`. Also `r6_transfer`, `r6_store`, `r6_issue` (the last two also conclude `rangeBytes … = some (map init ptrBytes)`), `ptr_target`, `ReprB.transport`, and `corr_leaf_fwd/back/inj`, where `corr_inj` takes only `hw` and `hd`.\n     - **Step 3:**\n       - `ddSound_of_layout (h : ∀ r r', k.DeclaredDisjoint r r' → ByteDisjoint L r r') (hpos : ∀ r r', k.DeclaredDisjoint r r' → ∀ l ∈ r, 0 < (L l).len) : DDSound k`;\n       - `ddSound_instance`;\n       - counterexample `ddSound_of_layout_needs_size`, plus a `LayoutWF` witness for it;\n       - `byteDisjoint_of_leaves`.\n     - **Step 4:** `pinned_address_stable` takes `provOf provOf'`, `hdd`, `hr : Reachable`, `hs : Step`, `hR`, `hR'`, and a pinned leaf. It concludes `LiveAlloc s2 … ∧ LiveAlloc (exec s2 ops) … ∧ leafAddr (exec s2 ops) L l = leafAddr s2 L l`.\n     - **Step 5:** `simulation`.\n       ```lean\n       theorem simulation … (hdd : DDSound k) (hstatR …) (hstatW …) (hpl : PlacementOK π.pl)\n           (hg : ∀ r, 0 < (π.geom r).align ∧ MM02.Pow2 (π.geom r).align) (htc : TokCompat C π.tok) :\n           ∀ {ops s3 pv os s2}, SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2 →\n             AllOk C ObR ObW MM02.State.empty os ∧ exec MM02.State.empty os = s2 ∧\n             Repr π.tok π.ptok pv π.L s3 s2 ∧ Reachable k statics s3 ∧ ∀ r, s3.P.length ≤ r → pv r = none\n       ```\n       Also `simulation_pinned`, `SimRun.trans`, `SimRun.exec3`, `Trans.of_exec`.\n     - **Cases** (ported pass 1, in namespaces `CaseInit`, `Cases`, `CaseOwnedLocal`, `DraftGaps`):\n       - `Cases` defines `ptk := fun pr => 6 + pr` and `prov := fun r => if r = 6 ∨ r = 7 then some 1 else none`, plus WF theorems `wf_m0`, `wf_m1`, `wf_m2`, `wf_m3`, `wf_m7`, `wf_m8`, `wf_m12`, `wf_m16`, `wf_mF`, built from `exec_wf`.\n       - New L4 tests: `¬ ReprB tk (fun pr => 9 + pr) prov L e12 m12` and the corresponding positive check on `e11`/`m8`.\n   - **Scratch files:**\n     - `$SP/p2work/` holds `MM23_p1.lean` (pass-1 backup), `cases_p1.lean`, `cases_p2a.lean`, `corr_leaves.lean`, `pinned_live.lean`, `sim.lean`.\n     - `$SP/mm23/log.md` is the ub-mode log, with 18 entries from pass 1; pass-2 entries are still to add.\n   - **`formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md`:** pass-1 report, committed.\n   - **Memory file** `/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md` has a pass-1 entry plus pitfalls. A pass-2 entry is still to add.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Repr decidability:** the `maxSize` limit was raised to 8192.\n   - **Missing fields after adding `provTokens`:** fixed by adding refine bullets in the transport lemmas.\n   - **`exec_wf` used before its definition:** moved it earlier in the file.\n   - **Implicit arguments not inferred:**\n     - `C` in `repr_writes` and `copyOps_run`: passed `(C := C)`;\n     - `k` in `r6_noStep`: passed `(k := k)`;\n     - `ptok`/`provOf`/`pr` in the cases: passed them explicitly.\n   - **`bytesOf` pattern:** needed `MM02.AByte.init`.\n   - **`FrameGone` rewrite** in `ReprB.transport`: used an intermediate `have`.\n   - **`corr_inj` usage:** went through `List.Pairwise.filterMap` with `R` including `partOf`, and `imp_of_mem`.\n   - **`exec_keeps_base` deallocation case:** gave the witness explicitly.\n   - **Unused simp args** (`Nat.add_sub_cancel_left`, `Option.mem_def`): removed.\n   - **`Reachable.ofStep` dot notation:** replaced by explicit calls.\n   - **Design flaw I caught myself** (vacuity risk): the first simulation quantified its obligations over all `Trans` configurations. It was rewritten with `SimRun`, whose step premises are `Oblig` on that run only.\n   - **Unused-hypothesis concern:** the `corr_inj`/`corr_leaf_back` unused hypotheses were removed, which makes the statements stronger.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Steps 1–5 are done and committed**, build clean, all constants within {propext, Quot.sound}: 9c08116, cf09f12, 837a192, 5fd6d8a, 10b837c.\n   - **Found issues to report:**\n     - L7 as stated is false with zero-size leaves (K1 (d)); counterexample kept.\n     - `r6_transfer` doesn't need `SameSizeAlong`; only `transfer_copies` does. `SameSizeAlong` is therefore not a hypothesis of `simulation`; record this in (c).\n     - `r6_enter` doesn't need L1; the L1/L2 envelope lives in `Step3`.\n     - `Deallocable` being false on statics is not needed.\n     - The ghost `provOf` evolves via `provStep`, so no consistency hypothesis is needed.\n     - Simulation obligations are per run (`SimRun`): `LayoutObl`, `DecAlong`, `FreeOblig`, plus the init layout and dec.\n     - Long lines over 100 chars remain (about 38): a style issue, optional cleanup.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The pass-1 brief (pasted, French): « Tâche : jalon 2, passe 1 — raffinement MM-03 → MM-02 … », with Git rules (« Pas de merge, pas de PR. Tout sous `formal/`. `Ern/MM02.lean` et `Ern/MM03.lean` inchangés … »), Langue, K1–K5, Étapes 1–6, Hors périmètre, Règles, Livrable.\n   - The pass-2 brief (pasted, French): « Tâche : jalon 2, passe 2 — raffinement MM-03 → MM-02 (transfer, store, issue, DDSound, épinglage, simulation) »:\n     - **Git:** « Même branche `formal/refinement_0.1`, à la suite. Pas de merge, pas de PR. Tout sous `formal/`. `Ern/MM02.lean` et `Ern/MM03.lean` inchangés ; tout ajout va dans `Ern/MM23.lean` ou un module voisin. »\n     - **Language:** code, docstrings, comments and commits in English; the report in French.\n     - L1–L8 (as in section 1), steps 1–6, hors périmètre, règles, livrable `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md` (a)–(f).\n   - Earlier (before this window), the user invoked `/ub-mode`.\n   - No other user messages; the rest were system and task notifications.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Step 6 (cases), committed:**\n     - one witness per new operation: `transfer`, `store`, `issue`, `reset`;\n     - a full execution as a `SimRun` built step by step with `decide`-proved `Oblig` (allocation, arena, emission, `store`, `transfer` to the caller, `free`, frame exit), applying `simulation`;\n     - non-trivial checks: copied bytes and provenance (`transfer_copies`), pointer bytes decode and provenance live (`ptr_target`), and `simulation_pinned` if feasible.\n   - **Adversarial review** (workflow, ultracode on) centred on L4 circularity, L6 provenance, L7, and simulation vacuity; then fixes and a second targeted check.\n   - **Report** `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md`, sections:\n     - (a) clause → declaration;\n     - (b) status of R1, R2, R4, R6 (full scope), `ddSound_of_layout`, `pinned_address_stable`, `freeSound_derived`, `simulation`;\n     - (c) decisions: envelope for L1/L2, `SameSizeAlong` used only for the copy, `provOf` as evolving ghost, `SimRun` obligations, `Repr` split into `ReprB`/`Repr`, `ddSound` positivity, statements made stronger;\n     - (d) not proved;\n     - (e) questions: L7 false with zero-size leaves; the order of the isomorphism taken as source footprint index order; empty regions give `ptrBytes` provenance none;\n     - (f) classified list of the `simulation` hypotheses:\n\n       | Hypothesis | Class |\n       |---|---|\n       | `DDSound` | bibliothèque, via `ddSound_of_layout` |\n       | `stat` | ouverte (Spec 2; true in the sequential fragment per K5) |\n       | `PlacementOK` | spec 11, and bibliothèque for `alloc` |\n       | alignments | spec 11 |\n       | `TokCompat` | spec 11 |\n       | `LayoutObl` | spec 4/11 |\n       | `DecAlong` | spec 4/11 |\n       | `FreeOblig` | bibliothèque |\n       | `ShapeOK` | MM-03 |\n       | envelope L1/L2 | language |\n     - Verify the report, commit, update the memory file and the ub-mode log, call `wrap_up` and give the final message, which reports the ub-mode log. No push.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just committed step 5 (`10b837c` \"MM23 pass 2, step 5: simulation\"). The build is clean, `theorems in Ern.MM23: 303`, nothing outside propext and Quot.sound. The plan list has steps 1–5 done; the next item is \"Step 6: cases and a full traced execution\".\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Start step 6 per the brief: « 6. Cas : un témoin par nouvelle opération, plus une exécution complète (allocation, arène, émission, `store`, `transfer` vers l'appelant, `free`, sortie de cadre) traduite pas à pas. »\n   - Add a new namespace (e.g. `CaseSim`) in `formal/Ern/MM23.lean`.\n   - Build a concrete `Params` π: layout `L`, `tok`, `ptok`, `topPlacement`, `geom`, a concrete `PtrEnc` satisfying `PtrEncOK`, and `w0`.\n   - Build a concrete K with `FreeCompat`/`Deallocable`/`Satisfiable` instances.\n   - Build the execution as a `SimRun` derivation constructor by constructor: `Step3` proofs by `.ok (by decide)`, `Oblig` by `decide` with the needed decidable instances.\n   - Apply `simulation` to obtain `AllOk`/`Repr`; add witnesses for `r6_transfer`/`transfer_copies`, `r6_store`/`ptr_target`, `r6_issue`, and `reset`.\n   - Then build, check axioms and commit; then run the adversarial-review workflow, write the report, verify, and commit.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"f2409576-4d1a-43d2-b3ca-13834274fa57","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:24:19.598Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":20,"turnIndex":51},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["6869effc-2595-4ed6-a111-c62a03f8bf9f"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
