{"parentUuid":"2393cac8-90ce-4e28-892e-30c3565eccbc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"afea6d65-2af9-420c-969b-b55d07c96f18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015jjmcNBPaD3NjxjNeJXBpJ","type":"tool_result","content":"3040\thas an effective mode on a leaf `l'` whose range overlaps the range of `l` (same allocation, ranges\n3041\tnot disjoint). The task asks it of the active authorities that do not descend from `a`; neither\n3042\tcondition is used: an active descendant of `a` covering `l` would remove the effective `Modify` of\n3043\t`a` (MM-03.3.5), and an inactive authority has no effective mode. Memory justification of\n3044\tnon-aliasing, on the side of the kernel only. -/\n3045\ttheorem exclusive_bytes {L : Layout} {s3 : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} (hlw : LayoutWF L s3 s2)\n3046\t    (hI1 : I1 s3) {a b l l' : Nat} (hl : l < s3.P.length) (hlf : isLeaf s3.P l)\n3047\t    (hl' : l' < s3.P.length) (hlf' : isLeaf s3.P l') (ha : effective s3 a l = some .modify)\n3048\t    (hab : a ≠ b) (hsame : (L l).alloc = (L l').alloc)\n3049\t    (hover : ¬ MM02.RangeDisjoint (L l).off (L l).len (L l').off (L l').len) :\n3050\t    effective s3 b l' = none := by\n3051\t  by_cases e : l = l'\n3052\t  · subst e; exact effective_exclusive hI1 hab ha\n3053\t  · exact absurd (hlw.disjoint l hl l' hl' hlf hlf' e hsame) hover\n3054\t\n3055\t/-! ## Simulation (step 5 of the task) -/\n3056\t\n3057\t/-- An operation of MM-03 with its arguments (MM-03.3 §3–6), the bytes written by `write3` and\n3058\t`writeShared` included: they are data of the program, not a choice of the refinement. -/\n3059\tinductive Op3 where\n3060\t  | derive (src q : Nat) (m : Mode)\n3061\t  | split (src : Nat) (rs : List (List Nat))\n3062\t  | release (a : Nat)\n3063\t  | transfer (src dst : Nat)\n3064\t  | depend (q x : Nat)\n3065\t  | enter (ps : List Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n3066\t  | exit\n3067\t  | read (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n3068\t  | write (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat) (w : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat)\n3069\t  | writeShared (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat) (w : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat)\n3070\t  | pin (p : Nat)\n3071\t  | unpin (p : Nat)\n3072\t  | endUse (p : Nat)\n3073\t  | free (p auth : Nat)\n3074\t  | alloc (pr ow : Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n3075\t  | newArena (st i : Nat)\n3076\t  | issue (i via : Nat) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat)\n3077\t  | reset (i via : Nat)\n3078\t  | store (a p : Nat)\n3079\t\n3080\t/-- L1: the shape of an `enterFrame` has no owning element: its locals are owned by the frame. -/\n3081\tdef NoOwner (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat)) : Prop :=\n3082\t  ∀ i < ls.length, (ls[i]?).bind (·.2.1) = none\n3083\t\n3084\t/-- An `ok` step of MM-03 labelled by its operation, within the envelope of L1 (an `enterFrame`\n3085\twhose shape has an owning element is outside the language) and L2 (the shape of `alloc` has exactly\n3086\tone root). -/\n3087\tdef Step3 (k : K) : Op3 → S3 → S3 → Prop\n3088\t  | .derive src q m, s, s' => DeriveStep src q m s (.ok s')\n3089\t  | .split src rs, s, s' => SplitStep k src rs s (.ok s')\n3090\t  | .release a, s, s' => ReleaseStep a s (.ok s')\n3091\t  | .transfer src dst, s, s' => TransferStep k src dst s (.ok s')\n3092\t  | .depend q x, s, s' => DependStep q x s (.ok s')\n3093\t  | .enter ps ls, s, s' => NoOwner ls ∧ EnterStep ps ls s (.ok s')\n3094\t  | .exit, s, s' => ExitStep k s (.ok s')\n3095\t  | .read a ls, s, s' => Read3Step a ls s (.ok s')\n3096\t  | .write a ls _, s, s' => Write3Step a ls s (.ok s')\n3097\t  | .writeShared a ls _, s, s' => WriteSharedStep k a ls s (.ok s')\n3098\t  | .pin p, s, s' => PinStep p s (.ok s')\n3099\t  | .unpin p, s, s' => UnpinStep k p s (.ok s')\n3100\t  | .endUse p, s, s' => EndUseStep k p s (.ok s')\n3101\t  | .free p auth, s, s' => FreeStep k p auth s (.ok s')\n3102\t  | .alloc pr ow ls, s, s' => (∃ i, rootIdx ls = [i]) ∧ AllocStep k pr ow ls s (.ok s')\n3103\t  | .newArena st i, s, s' => NewArenaStep st i s (.ok s')\n3104\t  | .issue i via region dst, s, s' => IssueAt k i via region dst s (.ok s')\n3105\t  | .reset i via, s, s' => ResetAtStep k i via s (.ok s')\n3106\t  | .store a p, s, s' => StoreStep a p s (.ok s')\n3107\t\n3108\t/-- A labelled step is a step of `Reachable` (MM-03.3 §10). -/\n3109\ttheorem Step3.step {k : K} {op : Op3} {s s' : S3} (h : Step3 k op s s') : Step k s s' := by\n3110\t  cases op with\n3111\t  | derive => exact .kernel (.derive h)\n3112\t  | split => exact .kernel (.split h)\n3113\t  | release => exact .kernel (.release h)\n3114\t  | transfer => exact .kernel (.transfer h)\n3115\t  | depend => exact .kernel (.depend h)\n3116\t  | enter => exact .kernel (.enter h.2)\n3117\t  | exit => exact .kernel (.exit h)\n3118\t  | read => exact .kernel (.read h)\n3119\t  | write => exact .kernel (.write h)\n3120\t  | writeShared => exact .kernel (.writeShared h)\n3121\t  | pin => exact .kernel (.pin h)\n3122\t  | unpin => exact .kernel (.unpin h)\n3123\t  | endUse => exact .kernel (.endUse h)\n3124\t  | free => exact .kernel (.free h)\n3125\t  | alloc => exact .kernel (.alloc h.2)\n3126\t  | newArena => exact .newArena h\n3127\t  | issue => exact .issue h\n3128\t  | reset => exact .reset h\n3129\t  | store => exact .kernel (.store h)\n3130\t\n3131\t/-- An execution of MM-03 from `S3.init statics` within the envelope of L1 and L2: the operations,\n3132\tmost recent first, and the state reached. -/\n3133\tinductive Exec3 (k : K) (statics : Statics) : List Op3 → S3 → Prop where\n3134\t  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) → Exec3 k statics [] (S3.init statics)\n3135\t  | step {ops : List Op3} {s s' : S3} {op : Op3} : Exec3 k statics ops s → Step3 k op s s' →\n3136\t      Exec3 k statics (op :: ops) s'\n3137\t\n3138\ttheorem Exec3.reachable {k : K} {statics : Statics} {ops : List Op3} {s : S3}\n3139\t    (h : Exec3 k statics ops s) : Reachable k statics s := by\n3140\t  induction h with\n3141\t  | init hsh => exact .init hsh\n3142\t  | step _ hs ih => exact Reachable.ofStep ih hs.step\n3143\t\n3144\t/-- Parameters of the refinement fixed once for a whole execution (step 5): the layout, the frame\n3145\tand provider tokens (K2, L4), the placement (K2), the geometry of the allocation of each root place,\n3146\tread on its index, the encoding of pointers (L6), the initial bytes of the statics (K3). -/\n3147\tstructure Params where\n3148\t  L : Layout\n3149\t  tok : Nat → Nat\n3150\t  ptok : Nat → Nat\n3151\t  pl : Placement\n3152\t  geom : Nat → Geom\n3153\t  pe : PtrEnc\n3154\t  w0 : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat\n3155\t\n3156\t/-- K4, L6: the MM-02 sequence associated with an MM-03 operation from the states `s3`, `s2`. -/\n3157\tdef assoc (π : Params) : Op3 → S3 → MM02.State → List Op2\n3158\t  | .read _ ls, _, s2 => readOps s2 π.L ls\n3159\t  | .write _ ls w, _, s2 => writeOps s2 π.L w ls\n3160\t  | .writeShared _ ls w, _, s2 => writeOps s2 π.L w ls\n3161\t  | .transfer src dst, s3, s2 => transferOps s2 π.L s3.P src dst\n3162\t  | .store a p, s3, s2 => storeOps π.pe s2 π.L s3 a p\n3163\t  | .issue _ _ region dst, _, s2 => issueOps π.pe s2 π.L region dst\n3164\t  | .alloc pr _ ls, s3, s2 =>\n3165\t    allocOps π.pl (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (some (π.ptok pr)) s2 (rootIdx ls)\n3166\t  | .enter _ ls, s3, s2 =>\n3167\t    allocOps π.pl (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (some (π.tok s3.nF)) s2 (rootIdx ls)\n3168\t  | .free p auth, s3, _ => deallocOps [rootAlloc π.L s3.P p] auth\n3169\t  | .exit, s3, _ => exitOps π.L π.tok s3\n3170\t  | _, _, _ => []\n3171\t\n3172\t/-- L4: the ghost `provOf` after an operation: `alloc pr _ ls` maps the places it creates to the\n3173\tprovider `pr`; no other operation changes it. -/\n3174\tdef provStep : Op3 → S3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → Nat → Option Nat\n3175\t  | .alloc pr _ ls, s3, pv => fun r =>\n3176\t    if s3.P.length ≤ r ∧ r < s3.P.length + ls.length then some pr else pv r\n3177\t  | _, _, pv => pv\n3178\t\n3179\t/-- K3: the MM-02 operations of the initial state with the parameters `π`. -/\n3180\tdef initOpsOf (π : Params) (statics : Statics) : List Op2 :=\n3181\t  initOps π.pl π.geom π.tok π.L π.w0 statics\n3182\t\n3183\t/-- The lock-step translation of an MM-03 execution: the operations (most recent first), the MM-03\n3184\tstate, the ghost `provOf`, the MM-02 operations (in the order of execution) and the MM-02 state.\n3185\tIt starts with the MM-02 run of `repr_init`; each MM-03 step appends its associated sequence. It is\n3186\tdetermined by the execution and the parameters. -/\n3187\tinductive Trans (k : K) (statics : Statics) (π : Params) :\n3188\t    List Op3 → S3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → List Op2 → MM02.State → Prop where\n3189\t  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) →\n3190\t      Trans k statics π [] (S3.init statics) (fun _ => none) (initOpsOf π statics)\n3191\t        (exec MM02.State.empty (initOpsOf π statics))\n3192\t  | step {ops : List Op3} {s3 s3' : S3} {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2}\n3193\t      {s2 : MM02.State} {op : Op3} :\n3194\t      Trans k statics π ops s3 pv os s2 → Step3 k op s3 s3' →\n3195\t      Trans k statics π (op :: ops) s3' (provStep op s3 pv) (os ++ assoc π op s3 s2)\n3196\t        (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2))\n3197\t\n3198\t/-- Every MM-03 execution has a translation. -/\n3199\ttheorem Trans.of_exec {k : K} {statics : Statics} (π : Params) {ops : List Op3} {s3 : S3}\n3200\t    (h : Exec3 k statics ops s3) : ∃ pv os s2, Trans k statics π ops s3 pv os s2 := by\n3201\t  induction h with\n3202\t  | init hsh => exact ⟨_, _, _, .init hsh⟩\n3203\t  | step _ hs ih => obtain ⟨pv, os, s2, ht⟩ := ih; exact ⟨_, _, _, ht.step hs⟩\n3204\t\n3205\t/-- K1, K2: the layout obligation of an operation that creates root places: the new roots are laid\n3206\tout in fresh allocations, within their geometry (`NewLayout`). -/\n3207\tdef LayoutObl (π : Params) : Op3 → S3 → S3 → MM02.State → Prop\n3208\t  | .enter _ ls, s3, s3', s2 =>\n3209\t    NewLayout π.L s3'.P s3.P.length s2.next (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (rootIdx ls)\n3210\t  | .alloc _ _ ls, s3, s3', s2 =>\n3211\t    NewLayout π.L s3'.P s3.P.length s2.next (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (rootIdx ls)\n3212\t  | _, _, _, _ => True\n3213\t\n3214\ttheorem ReprB.provOf_congr {tok ptok : Nat → Nat} {pv pv' : Nat → Option Nat} {L : Layout}\n3215\t    {s3 : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} (hR : ReprB tok ptok pv L s3 s2)\n3216\t    (h : ∀ r < s3.P.length, pv' r = pv r) : ReprB tok ptok pv' L s3 s2 :=\n3217\t  { hR with provTokens := fun r hr hrt => by rw [h r hr]; exact hR.provTokens r hr hrt }\n3218\t\n3219\ttheorem decAlong_readOps {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {s2 s2' : MM02.State}\n3220\t    {L : Layout} : ∀ {ls : List Nat}, DecAlong ObR ObW s2 (readOps s2' L ls) →\n3221\t      ∀ l ∈ ls, ObR.dec s2 (leafAcc s2' L .read l)\n3222\t  | [], _, _, h => by cases h\n3223\t  | _ :: _, ⟨h0, h⟩, _, hl => by\n3224\t    rcases List.mem_cons.1 hl with rfl | hl\n3225\t    · exact h0\n3226\t    · exact decAlong_readOps h _ hl\n3227\t\n3228\t/-- L4: the obligation of the contracts at a `free` of the run: `FreeCompat` is instantiated by\n3229\tthe token of the provider recorded by the ghost `provOf` (`FreeCompatInst`). -/\n3230\tdef FreeOblig (k : K) (C : Nat → Nat → Prop) (π : Params) : Op3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → Prop\n3231\t  | .free p auth, pv => k.FreeCompat p auth → FreeCompatInst C π.ptok pv p auth\n3232\t  | _, _ => True\n3233\t\n3234\t/-- The obligations of one step of the run, on the states where it runs: the layout of the new\n3235\troots (`LayoutObl`, K1, K2), `dec` along its MM-02 sequence (K5), and `FreeOblig` (L4). -/\n3236\tdef Oblig (k : K) (C : Nat → Nat → Prop) (ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec) (ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec)\n3237\t    (π : Params) (op : Op3) (s3 s3' : S3) (pv : Nat → Option Nat) (s2 : MM02.State) : Prop :=\n3238\t  LayoutObl π op s3 s3' s2 ∧ DecAlong ObR ObW s2 (assoc π op s3 s2) ∧ FreeOblig k C π op pv\n3239\t\n3240\t/-- An execution of MM-03 with its translation (`Trans`) whose every step meets its obligations\n3241\t(`Oblig`), and whose initial run meets the layout of the statics and `dec`. The obligations bear on\n3242\tthe states of this execution and its run only. -/\n3243\tinductive SimRun (k : K) (C : Nat → Nat → Prop) (ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec)\n3244\t    (ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec) (statics : Statics) (π : Params) :\n3245\t    List Op3 → S3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → List Op2 → MM02.State → Prop where\n3246\t  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) →\n3247\t      NewLayout π.L (S3.init statics).P 0 0 π.geom (rootIdx (statics.map (·.1))) →\n3248\t      DecAlong ObR ObW MM02.State.empty (initOpsOf π statics) →\n3249\t      SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π [] (S3.init statics) (fun _ => none) (initOpsOf π statics)\n3250\t        (exec MM02.State.empty (initOpsOf π statics))\n3251\t  | step {ops : List Op3} {s3 s3' : S3} {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2}\n3252\t      {s2 : MM02.State} {op : Op3} :\n3253\t      SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2 → Step3 k op s3 s3' →\n3254\t      Oblig k C ObR ObW π op s3 s3' pv s2 →\n3255\t      SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π (op :: ops) s3' (provStep op s3 pv) (os ++ assoc π op s3 s2)\n3256\t        (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2))\n3257\t\n3258\t/-- A `SimRun` is the canonical translation of its execution. -/\n3259\ttheorem SimRun.trans {k : K} {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}\n3260\t    {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} {ops : List Op3} {s3 : S3}\n3261\t    {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2} {s2 : MM02.State}\n3262\t    (h : SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2) : Trans k statics π ops s3 pv os s2 := by\n3263\t  induction h with\n3264\t  | init hsh _ _ => exact .init hsh\n3265\t  | step _ hs _ ih => exact ih.step hs\n3266\t\n3267\t/-- A `SimRun` is an execution of MM-03. -/\n3268\ttheorem SimRun.exec3 {k : K} {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}\n3269\t    {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} {ops : List Op3} {s3 : S3}\n3270\t    {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2} {s2 : MM02.State}\n3271\t    (h : SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2) : Exec3 k statics ops s3 := by\n3272\t  induction h with\n3273\t  | init hsh _ _ => exact .init hsh\n3274\t  | step _ hs _ ih => exact ih.step hs\n3275\t\n3276\t/-- `simulation` (step 5): along every execution of MM-03 from `S3.init statics` within the\n3277\tenvelope of L1 and L2, translated with parameters `π` fixed once for the whole execution, whose\n3278\tsteps meet their obligations (`SimRun`), the MM-02 run starts with the run of `repr_init`, appends\n3279\tat each step the sequence associated by K4 and L6, has only `ok` outcomes, reaches the state `s2`,\n3280\tand is in `Repr` with the MM-03 state; the MM-03 state is reached, and the ghost `provOf` is empty\n3281\tbeyond the places. Since every prefix of a `SimRun` is a `SimRun`, this holds at each step. The\n3282\tremaining hypotheses: `DDSound k` (L7: `ddSound_of_layout`); `stat` (K5); the obligation of the\n3283\tplacement and valid alignments (K2); the compatibility of the frame tokens (K2). -/\n3284\ttheorem simulation {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec}\n3285\t    {k : K} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} (hdd : DDSound k)\n3286\t    (hstatR : ∀ s ac, ObR.stat s ac) (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)\n3287\t    (hpl : PlacementOK π.pl) (hg : ∀ r, 0 < (π.geom r).align ∧ MM02.Pow2 (π.geom r).align)\n3288\t    (htc : TokCompat C π.tok) :\n3289\t    ∀ {ops s3 pv os s2}, SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2 →\n3290\t      AllOk C ObR ObW MM02.State.empty os ∧ exec MM02.State.empty os = s2 ∧\n3291\t      Repr π.tok π.ptok pv π.L s3 s2 ∧ Reachable k statics s3 ∧\n3292\t      ∀ r, s3.P.length ≤ r → pv r = none := by\n3293\t  intro ops s3 pv os s2 ht\n3294\t  induction ht with\n3295\t  | init hsh hlay0 hdec0 =>\n3296\t    have := repr_init (C := C) (ObR := ObR) (ObW := ObW) (tok := π.tok) (ptok := π.ptok)\n3297\t      (provOf := fun _ => none) hsh hpl (fun i _ => hg i) hlay0 (fun _ _ => rfl) hstatW hdec0\n3298\t    exact ⟨this.1, rfl, this.2, .init hsh, fun _ _ => rfl⟩\n3299\t  | @step ops s3 s3' pv os s2 op _ hs hob ih =>\n3300\t    obtain ⟨hok, hex, hR, hr, hpv⟩ := ih\n3301\t    obtain ⟨hly, hdc, hfc⟩ := hob\n3302\t    have hwf := (reachable_invariants hdd hr).1\n3303\t    have hnd := (reachable_invariants hdd hr).2.1.nd\n3304\t    have hfl := (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive hdd hr).1\n3305\t    have hfo := (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive hdd hr).2\n3306\t    have hr' : Reachable k statics s3' := Reachable.ofStep hr hs.step\n3307\t    -- the MM-02 side of the step\n3308\t    have key : AllOk C ObR ObW s2 (assoc π op s3 s2) ∧\n3309\t        Repr π.tok π.ptok (provStep op s3 pv) π.L s3' (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2)) := by\n3310\t      cases op with\n3311\t      | derive => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.derive hs)\n3312\t      | split => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.split hs)\n3313\t      | release => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.release hs)\n3314\t      | transfer => exact r6_transfer hwf hR hs hstatR hstatW hdc\n3315\t      | depend => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.depend hs)\n3316\t      | enter ps ls =>\n3317\t        exact r6_enter hwf hR hpl (fun i _ => hg _) hs.2 (fun i _ => hpv _ (Nat.le_add_right _ _))\n3318\t          hly\n3319\t      | exit => exact r6_exit hwf hfo hR htc hs\n3320\t      | read => exact r6_read3 hwf hnd hfl hR hs hstatR (decAlong_readOps hdc)\n3321\t      | write => exact r2_write3 hwf hnd hfl hR hs hstatW hdc\n3322\t      | writeShared => exact r2_writeShared hwf hnd hfl hR hs hstatW hdc\n3323\t      | pin => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.pin hs)\n3324\t      | unpin => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.unpin hs)\n3325\t      | endUse => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.endUse hs)\n3326\t      | free p auth => exact r6_free hwf hR hfc hs\n3327\t      | alloc pr ow ls =>\n3328\t        obtain ⟨⟨i, hone⟩, hs'⟩ := hs\n3329\t        have hi : i < ls.length := (rootIdx_mem (k := 0) (by rw [hone]; rfl)).1\n3330\t        have hR₁ : Repr π.tok π.ptok (provStep (.alloc pr ow ls) s3 pv) π.L s3 s2 :=\n3331\t          ⟨hR.toReprB.provOf_congr fun r hr => by\n3332\t            simp only [provStep, show ¬ (s3.P.length ≤ r ∧ r < s3.P.length + ls.length) from\n3333\t              fun h => absurd h.1 (Nat.not_le.2 hr), ↓reduceIte], hR.wf2⟩\n3334\t        have := r6_alloc (C := C) (ObR := ObR) (ObW := ObW) (pl := π.pl)\n3335\t          (g := fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (i := i) hwf hR₁ hpl (hg _) hs' hone\n3336\t          (by simp only [provStep, show s3.P.length ≤ s3.P.length + i ∧\n3337\t              s3.P.length + i < s3.P.length + ls.length from ⟨Nat.le_add_right _ _, by omega⟩,\n3338\t              and_self, ↓reduceIte])\n3339\t          (by simp only [LayoutObl] at hly; rw [hone] at hly; exact hly)\n3340\t        simp only [assoc, hone]\n3341\t        exact this\n3342\t      | newArena => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.newArena hs)\n3343\t      | issue => exact (r6_issue hwf hR hs hstatW hdc.1).imp id fun h => h.1\n3344\t      | reset => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.reset hs)\n3345\t      | store => exact (r6_store hwf hR hs hstatW hdc.1).imp id fun h => h.1\n3346\t    refine ⟨along_append.2 ⟨hok, hex ▸ key.1⟩, by rw [exec_append, hex], key.2, hr', fun r hr => ?_⟩\n3347\t    have hlen := (step_extends hwf hs.step).1\n3348\t    cases op with\n3349\t    | alloc pr ow ls =>\n3350\t      have hP : s3'.P.length = s3.P.length + ls.length := by\n3351\t        obtain ⟨-, hs'⟩ := hs\n3352\t        cases hs' with\n3353\t        | ok _ _ => exact allocP_len s3 ow ls\n3354\t      simp only [provStep, show ¬ (s3.P.length ≤ r ∧ r < s3.P.length + ls.length) from\n3355\t        fun h => by omega, ↓reduceIte]\n3356\t      exact hpv r (by omega)\n3357\t    | _ => exact hpv r (by omega)\n3358\t\n3359\t/-- L8 along the simulation: at every step of a `SimRun`, a leaf pinned before the step has a live\n3360\tallocation before and after it, and the same address. -/\n3361\ttheorem simulation_pinned {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}\n3362\t    {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {k : K} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} (hdd : DDSound k)\n3363\t    (hstatR : ∀ s ac, ObR.stat s ac) (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)\n3364\t    (hpl : PlacementOK π.pl) (hg : ∀ r, 0 < (π.geom r).align ∧ MM02.Pow2 (π.geom r).align)\n3365\t    (htc : TokCompat C π.tok) {ops : List Op3} {s3 s3' : S3} {pv : Nat → Option Nat}\n3366\t    {os : List Op2} {s2 : MM02.State} {op : Op3}\n3367\t    (ht : SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2) (hs : Step3 k op s3 s3')\n3368\t    (hob : Oblig k C ObR ObW π op s3 s3' pv s2) {l : Nat} (hl : l < s3.P.length)\n3369\t    (hlf : isLeaf s3.P l) (hpin : s3.pin l = true ∨ k.Pinned l) :\n3370\t    LiveAlloc s2 (π.L l).alloc ∧ LiveAlloc (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2)) (π.L l).alloc ∧\n3371\t      leafAddr (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2)) π.L l = leafAddr s2 π.L l := by\n3372\t  have h₁ := simulation hdd hstatR hstatW hpl hg htc ht\n3373\t  have h₂ := simulation hdd hstatR hstatW hpl hg htc (ht.step hs hob)\n3374\t  exact pinned_address_stable hdd h₁.2.2.2.1 hs.step h₁.2.2.1 h₂.2.2.1 hl hlf hpin\n3375\t\n3376\t/-! ## Cases (step 6 of the task)\n3377\t\n3378\tEach verdict is checked by `decide` on the precondition of the MM-03 step and on `Repr`, which is\n3379\tdecidable; the MM-02 sequences are exhibited by the definitions `opsN` and their effects. Each\n3380\trefinement theorem is applied to a step of one scenario reached from `S3.init`. The obligations `dec` of the\n3381\ttest cases ask an access aligned on 4 bytes, a non-trivial instance (K5); `stat` is `True`, as K5\n3382\tfixes for the sequential fragment. -/\n3383\t\n3384\tnamespace CaseInit"}]},"uuid":"c1de48da-35a9-434c-a6b6-ccdc6b8f668c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:24:52.388Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM23.lean","content":"has an effective mode on a leaf `l'` whose range overlaps the range of `l` (same allocation, ranges\nnot disjoint). The task asks it of the active authorities that do not descend from `a`; neither\ncondition is used: an active descendant of `a` covering `l` would remove the effective `Modify` of\n`a` (MM-03.3.5), and an inactive authority has no effective mode. Memory justification of\nnon-aliasing, on the side of the kernel only. -/\ntheorem exclusive_bytes {L : Layout} {s3 : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} (hlw : LayoutWF L s3 s2)\n    (hI1 : I1 s3) {a b l l' : Nat} (hl : l < s3.P.length) (hlf : isLeaf s3.P l)\n    (hl' : l' < s3.P.length) (hlf' : isLeaf s3.P l') (ha : effective s3 a l = some .modify)\n    (hab : a ≠ b) (hsame : (L l).alloc = (L l').alloc)\n    (hover : ¬ MM02.RangeDisjoint (L l).off (L l).len (L l').off (L l').len) :\n    effective s3 b l' = none := by\n  by_cases e : l = l'\n  · subst e; exact effective_exclusive hI1 hab ha\n  · exact absurd (hlw.disjoint l hl l' hl' hlf hlf' e hsame) hover\n\n/-! ## Simulation (step 5 of the task) -/\n\n/-- An operation of MM-03 with its arguments (MM-03.3 §3–6), the bytes written by `write3` and\n`writeShared` included: they are data of the program, not a choice of the refinement. -/\ninductive Op3 where\n  | derive (src q : Nat) (m : Mode)\n  | split (src : Nat) (rs : List (List Nat))\n  | release (a : Nat)\n  | transfer (src dst : Nat)\n  | depend (q x : Nat)\n  | enter (ps : List Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n  | exit\n  | read (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n  | write (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat) (w : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat)\n  | writeShared (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat) (w : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat)\n  | pin (p : Nat)\n  | unpin (p : Nat)\n  | endUse (p : Nat)\n  | free (p auth : Nat)\n  | alloc (pr ow : Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n  | newArena (st i : Nat)\n  | issue (i via : Nat) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat)\n  | reset (i via : Nat)\n  | store (a p : Nat)\n\n/-- L1: the shape of an `enterFrame` has no owning element: its locals are owned by the frame. -/\ndef NoOwner (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat)) : Prop :=\n  ∀ i < ls.length, (ls[i]?).bind (·.2.1) = none\n\n/-- An `ok` step of MM-03 labelled by its operation, within the envelope of L1 (an `enterFrame`\nwhose shape has an owning element is outside the language) and L2 (the shape of `alloc` has exactly\none root). -/\ndef Step3 (k : K) : Op3 → S3 → S3 → Prop\n  | .derive src q m, s, s' => DeriveStep src q m s (.ok s')\n  | .split src rs, s, s' => SplitStep k src rs s (.ok s')\n  | .release a, s, s' => ReleaseStep a s (.ok s')\n  | .transfer src dst, s, s' => TransferStep k src dst s (.ok s')\n  | .depend q x, s, s' => DependStep q x s (.ok s')\n  | .enter ps ls, s, s' => NoOwner ls ∧ EnterStep ps ls s (.ok s')\n  | .exit, s, s' => ExitStep k s (.ok s')\n  | .read a ls, s, s' => Read3Step a ls s (.ok s')\n  | .write a ls _, s, s' => Write3Step a ls s (.ok s')\n  | .writeShared a ls _, s, s' => WriteSharedStep k a ls s (.ok s')\n  | .pin p, s, s' => PinStep p s (.ok s')\n  | .unpin p, s, s' => UnpinStep k p s (.ok s')\n  | .endUse p, s, s' => EndUseStep k p s (.ok s')\n  | .free p auth, s, s' => FreeStep k p auth s (.ok s')\n  | .alloc pr ow ls, s, s' => (∃ i, rootIdx ls = [i]) ∧ AllocStep k pr ow ls s (.ok s')\n  | .newArena st i, s, s' => NewArenaStep st i s (.ok s')\n  | .issue i via region dst, s, s' => IssueAt k i via region dst s (.ok s')\n  | .reset i via, s, s' => ResetAtStep k i via s (.ok s')\n  | .store a p, s, s' => StoreStep a p s (.ok s')\n\n/-- A labelled step is a step of `Reachable` (MM-03.3 §10). -/\ntheorem Step3.step {k : K} {op : Op3} {s s' : S3} (h : Step3 k op s s') : Step k s s' := by\n  cases op with\n  | derive => exact .kernel (.derive h)\n  | split => exact .kernel (.split h)\n  | release => exact .kernel (.release h)\n  | transfer => exact .kernel (.transfer h)\n  | depend => exact .kernel (.depend h)\n  | enter => exact .kernel (.enter h.2)\n  | exit => exact .kernel (.exit h)\n  | read => exact .kernel (.read h)\n  | write => exact .kernel (.write h)\n  | writeShared => exact .kernel (.writeShared h)\n  | pin => exact .kernel (.pin h)\n  | unpin => exact .kernel (.unpin h)\n  | endUse => exact .kernel (.endUse h)\n  | free => exact .kernel (.free h)\n  | alloc => exact .kernel (.alloc h.2)\n  | newArena => exact .newArena h\n  | issue => exact .issue h\n  | reset => exact .reset h\n  | store => exact .kernel (.store h)\n\n/-- An execution of MM-03 from `S3.init statics` within the envelope of L1 and L2: the operations,\nmost recent first, and the state reached. -/\ninductive Exec3 (k : K) (statics : Statics) : List Op3 → S3 → Prop where\n  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) → Exec3 k statics [] (S3.init statics)\n  | step {ops : List Op3} {s s' : S3} {op : Op3} : Exec3 k statics ops s → Step3 k op s s' →\n      Exec3 k statics (op :: ops) s'\n\ntheorem Exec3.reachable {k : K} {statics : Statics} {ops : List Op3} {s : S3}\n    (h : Exec3 k statics ops s) : Reachable k statics s := by\n  induction h with\n  | init hsh => exact .init hsh\n  | step _ hs ih => exact Reachable.ofStep ih hs.step\n\n/-- Parameters of the refinement fixed once for a whole execution (step 5): the layout, the frame\nand provider tokens (K2, L4), the placement (K2), the geometry of the allocation of each root place,\nread on its index, the encoding of pointers (L6), the initial bytes of the statics (K3). -/\nstructure Params where\n  L : Layout\n  tok : Nat → Nat\n  ptok : Nat → Nat\n  pl : Placement\n  geom : Nat → Geom\n  pe : PtrEnc\n  w0 : Nat → Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat\n\n/-- K4, L6: the MM-02 sequence associated with an MM-03 operation from the states `s3`, `s2`. -/\ndef assoc (π : Params) : Op3 → S3 → MM02.State → List Op2\n  | .read _ ls, _, s2 => readOps s2 π.L ls\n  | .write _ ls w, _, s2 => writeOps s2 π.L w ls\n  | .writeShared _ ls w, _, s2 => writeOps s2 π.L w ls\n  | .transfer src dst, s3, s2 => transferOps s2 π.L s3.P src dst\n  | .store a p, s3, s2 => storeOps π.pe s2 π.L s3 a p\n  | .issue _ _ region dst, _, s2 => issueOps π.pe s2 π.L region dst\n  | .alloc pr _ ls, s3, s2 =>\n    allocOps π.pl (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (some (π.ptok pr)) s2 (rootIdx ls)\n  | .enter _ ls, s3, s2 =>\n    allocOps π.pl (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (some (π.tok s3.nF)) s2 (rootIdx ls)\n  | .free p auth, s3, _ => deallocOps [rootAlloc π.L s3.P p] auth\n  | .exit, s3, _ => exitOps π.L π.tok s3\n  | _, _, _ => []\n\n/-- L4: the ghost `provOf` after an operation: `alloc pr _ ls` maps the places it creates to the\nprovider `pr`; no other operation changes it. -/\ndef provStep : Op3 → S3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → Nat → Option Nat\n  | .alloc pr _ ls, s3, pv => fun r =>\n    if s3.P.length ≤ r ∧ r < s3.P.length + ls.length then some pr else pv r\n  | _, _, pv => pv\n\n/-- K3: the MM-02 operations of the initial state with the parameters `π`. -/\ndef initOpsOf (π : Params) (statics : Statics) : List Op2 :=\n  initOps π.pl π.geom π.tok π.L π.w0 statics\n\n/-- The lock-step translation of an MM-03 execution: the operations (most recent first), the MM-03\nstate, the ghost `provOf`, the MM-02 operations (in the order of execution) and the MM-02 state.\nIt starts with the MM-02 run of `repr_init`; each MM-03 step appends its associated sequence. It is\ndetermined by the execution and the parameters. -/\ninductive Trans (k : K) (statics : Statics) (π : Params) :\n    List Op3 → S3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → List Op2 → MM02.State → Prop where\n  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) →\n      Trans k statics π [] (S3.init statics) (fun _ => none) (initOpsOf π statics)\n        (exec MM02.State.empty (initOpsOf π statics))\n  | step {ops : List Op3} {s3 s3' : S3} {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2}\n      {s2 : MM02.State} {op : Op3} :\n      Trans k statics π ops s3 pv os s2 → Step3 k op s3 s3' →\n      Trans k statics π (op :: ops) s3' (provStep op s3 pv) (os ++ assoc π op s3 s2)\n        (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2))\n\n/-- Every MM-03 execution has a translation. -/\ntheorem Trans.of_exec {k : K} {statics : Statics} (π : Params) {ops : List Op3} {s3 : S3}\n    (h : Exec3 k statics ops s3) : ∃ pv os s2, Trans k statics π ops s3 pv os s2 := by\n  induction h with\n  | init hsh => exact ⟨_, _, _, .init hsh⟩\n  | step _ hs ih => obtain ⟨pv, os, s2, ht⟩ := ih; exact ⟨_, _, _, ht.step hs⟩\n\n/-- K1, K2: the layout obligation of an operation that creates root places: the new roots are laid\nout in fresh allocations, within their geometry (`NewLayout`). -/\ndef LayoutObl (π : Params) : Op3 → S3 → S3 → MM02.State → Prop\n  | .enter _ ls, s3, s3', s2 =>\n    NewLayout π.L s3'.P s3.P.length s2.next (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (rootIdx ls)\n  | .alloc _ _ ls, s3, s3', s2 =>\n    NewLayout π.L s3'.P s3.P.length s2.next (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (rootIdx ls)\n  | _, _, _, _ => True\n\ntheorem ReprB.provOf_congr {tok ptok : Nat → Nat} {pv pv' : Nat → Option Nat} {L : Layout}\n    {s3 : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} (hR : ReprB tok ptok pv L s3 s2)\n    (h : ∀ r < s3.P.length, pv' r = pv r) : ReprB tok ptok pv' L s3 s2 :=\n  { hR with provTokens := fun r hr hrt => by rw [h r hr]; exact hR.provTokens r hr hrt }\n\ntheorem decAlong_readOps {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {s2 s2' : MM02.State}\n    {L : Layout} : ∀ {ls : List Nat}, DecAlong ObR ObW s2 (readOps s2' L ls) →\n      ∀ l ∈ ls, ObR.dec s2 (leafAcc s2' L .read l)\n  | [], _, _, h => by cases h\n  | _ :: _, ⟨h0, h⟩, _, hl => by\n    rcases List.mem_cons.1 hl with rfl | hl\n    · exact h0\n    · exact decAlong_readOps h _ hl\n\n/-- L4: the obligation of the contracts at a `free` of the run: `FreeCompat` is instantiated by\nthe token of the provider recorded by the ghost `provOf` (`FreeCompatInst`). -/\ndef FreeOblig (k : K) (C : Nat → Nat → Prop) (π : Params) : Op3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → Prop\n  | .free p auth, pv => k.FreeCompat p auth → FreeCompatInst C π.ptok pv p auth\n  | _, _ => True\n\n/-- The obligations of one step of the run, on the states where it runs: the layout of the new\nroots (`LayoutObl`, K1, K2), `dec` along its MM-02 sequence (K5), and `FreeOblig` (L4). -/\ndef Oblig (k : K) (C : Nat → Nat → Prop) (ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec) (ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec)\n    (π : Params) (op : Op3) (s3 s3' : S3) (pv : Nat → Option Nat) (s2 : MM02.State) : Prop :=\n  LayoutObl π op s3 s3' s2 ∧ DecAlong ObR ObW s2 (assoc π op s3 s2) ∧ FreeOblig k C π op pv\n\n/-- An execution of MM-03 with its translation (`Trans`) whose every step meets its obligations\n(`Oblig`), and whose initial run meets the layout of the statics and `dec`. The obligations bear on\nthe states of this execution and its run only. -/\ninductive SimRun (k : K) (C : Nat → Nat → Prop) (ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec)\n    (ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec) (statics : Statics) (π : Params) :\n    List Op3 → S3 → (Nat → Option Nat) → List Op2 → MM02.State → Prop where\n  | init : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1)) →\n      NewLayout π.L (S3.init statics).P 0 0 π.geom (rootIdx (statics.map (·.1))) →\n      DecAlong ObR ObW MM02.State.empty (initOpsOf π statics) →\n      SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π [] (S3.init statics) (fun _ => none) (initOpsOf π statics)\n        (exec MM02.State.empty (initOpsOf π statics))\n  | step {ops : List Op3} {s3 s3' : S3} {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2}\n      {s2 : MM02.State} {op : Op3} :\n      SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2 → Step3 k op s3 s3' →\n      Oblig k C ObR ObW π op s3 s3' pv s2 →\n      SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π (op :: ops) s3' (provStep op s3 pv) (os ++ assoc π op s3 s2)\n        (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2))\n\n/-- A `SimRun` is the canonical translation of its execution. -/\ntheorem SimRun.trans {k : K} {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}\n    {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} {ops : List Op3} {s3 : S3}\n    {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2} {s2 : MM02.State}\n    (h : SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2) : Trans k statics π ops s3 pv os s2 := by\n  induction h with\n  | init hsh _ _ => exact .init hsh\n  | step _ hs _ ih => exact ih.step hs\n\n/-- A `SimRun` is an execution of MM-03. -/\ntheorem SimRun.exec3 {k : K} {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}\n    {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} {ops : List Op3} {s3 : S3}\n    {pv : Nat → Option Nat} {os : List Op2} {s2 : MM02.State}\n    (h : SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2) : Exec3 k statics ops s3 := by\n  induction h with\n  | init hsh _ _ => exact .init hsh\n  | step _ hs _ ih => exact ih.step hs\n\n/-- `simulation` (step 5): along every execution of MM-03 from `S3.init statics` within the\nenvelope of L1 and L2, translated with parameters `π` fixed once for the whole execution, whose\nsteps meet their obligations (`SimRun`), the MM-02 run starts with the run of `repr_init`, appends\nat each step the sequence associated by K4 and L6, has only `ok` outcomes, reaches the state `s2`,\nand is in `Repr` with the MM-03 state; the MM-03 state is reached, and the ghost `provOf` is empty\nbeyond the places. Since every prefix of a `SimRun` is a `SimRun`, this holds at each step. The\nremaining hypotheses: `DDSound k` (L7: `ddSound_of_layout`); `stat` (K5); the obligation of the\nplacement and valid alignments (K2); the compatibility of the frame tokens (K2). -/\ntheorem simulation {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec}\n    {k : K} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} (hdd : DDSound k)\n    (hstatR : ∀ s ac, ObR.stat s ac) (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)\n    (hpl : PlacementOK π.pl) (hg : ∀ r, 0 < (π.geom r).align ∧ MM02.Pow2 (π.geom r).align)\n    (htc : TokCompat C π.tok) :\n    ∀ {ops s3 pv os s2}, SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2 →\n      AllOk C ObR ObW MM02.State.empty os ∧ exec MM02.State.empty os = s2 ∧\n      Repr π.tok π.ptok pv π.L s3 s2 ∧ Reachable k statics s3 ∧\n      ∀ r, s3.P.length ≤ r → pv r = none := by\n  intro ops s3 pv os s2 ht\n  induction ht with\n  | init hsh hlay0 hdec0 =>\n    have := repr_init (C := C) (ObR := ObR) (ObW := ObW) (tok := π.tok) (ptok := π.ptok)\n      (provOf := fun _ => none) hsh hpl (fun i _ => hg i) hlay0 (fun _ _ => rfl) hstatW hdec0\n    exact ⟨this.1, rfl, this.2, .init hsh, fun _ _ => rfl⟩\n  | @step ops s3 s3' pv os s2 op _ hs hob ih =>\n    obtain ⟨hok, hex, hR, hr, hpv⟩ := ih\n    obtain ⟨hly, hdc, hfc⟩ := hob\n    have hwf := (reachable_invariants hdd hr).1\n    have hnd := (reachable_invariants hdd hr).2.1.nd\n    have hfl := (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive hdd hr).1\n    have hfo := (reachable_fpLeaves_frameOwnedLive hdd hr).2\n    have hr' : Reachable k statics s3' := Reachable.ofStep hr hs.step\n    -- the MM-02 side of the step\n    have key : AllOk C ObR ObW s2 (assoc π op s3 s2) ∧\n        Repr π.tok π.ptok (provStep op s3 pv) π.L s3' (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2)) := by\n      cases op with\n      | derive => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.derive hs)\n      | split => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.split hs)\n      | release => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.release hs)\n      | transfer => exact r6_transfer hwf hR hs hstatR hstatW hdc\n      | depend => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.depend hs)\n      | enter ps ls =>\n        exact r6_enter hwf hR hpl (fun i _ => hg _) hs.2 (fun i _ => hpv _ (Nat.le_add_right _ _))\n          hly\n      | exit => exact r6_exit hwf hfo hR htc hs\n      | read => exact r6_read3 hwf hnd hfl hR hs hstatR (decAlong_readOps hdc)\n      | write => exact r2_write3 hwf hnd hfl hR hs hstatW hdc\n      | writeShared => exact r2_writeShared hwf hnd hfl hR hs hstatW hdc\n      | pin => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.pin hs)\n      | unpin => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.unpin hs)\n      | endUse => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.endUse hs)\n      | free p auth => exact r6_free hwf hR hfc hs\n      | alloc pr ow ls =>\n        obtain ⟨⟨i, hone⟩, hs'⟩ := hs\n        have hi : i < ls.length := (rootIdx_mem (k := 0) (by rw [hone]; rfl)).1\n        have hR₁ : Repr π.tok π.ptok (provStep (.alloc pr ow ls) s3 pv) π.L s3 s2 :=\n          ⟨hR.toReprB.provOf_congr fun r hr => by\n            simp only [provStep, show ¬ (s3.P.length ≤ r ∧ r < s3.P.length + ls.length) from\n              fun h => absurd h.1 (Nat.not_le.2 hr), ↓reduceIte], hR.wf2⟩\n        have := r6_alloc (C := C) (ObR := ObR) (ObW := ObW) (pl := π.pl)\n          (g := fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (i := i) hwf hR₁ hpl (hg _) hs' hone\n          (by simp only [provStep, show s3.P.length ≤ s3.P.length + i ∧\n              s3.P.length + i < s3.P.length + ls.length from ⟨Nat.le_add_right _ _, by omega⟩,\n              and_self, ↓reduceIte])\n          (by simp only [LayoutObl] at hly; rw [hone] at hly; exact hly)\n        simp only [assoc, hone]\n        exact this\n      | newArena => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.newArena hs)\n      | issue => exact (r6_issue hwf hR hs hstatW hdc.1).imp id fun h => h.1\n      | reset => exact r6_noStep (k := k) hR (.reset hs)\n      | store => exact (r6_store hwf hR hs hstatW hdc.1).imp id fun h => h.1\n    refine ⟨along_append.2 ⟨hok, hex ▸ key.1⟩, by rw [exec_append, hex], key.2, hr', fun r hr => ?_⟩\n    have hlen := (step_extends hwf hs.step).1\n    cases op with\n    | alloc pr ow ls =>\n      have hP : s3'.P.length = s3.P.length + ls.length := by\n        obtain ⟨-, hs'⟩ := hs\n        cases hs' with\n        | ok _ _ => exact allocP_len s3 ow ls\n      simp only [provStep, show ¬ (s3.P.length ≤ r ∧ r < s3.P.length + ls.length) from\n        fun h => by omega, ↓reduceIte]\n      exact hpv r (by omega)\n    | _ => exact hpv r (by omega)\n\n/-- L8 along the simulation: at every step of a `SimRun`, a leaf pinned before the step has a live\nallocation before and after it, and the same address. -/\ntheorem simulation_pinned {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}\n    {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {k : K} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} (hdd : DDSound k)\n    (hstatR : ∀ s ac, ObR.stat s ac) (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)\n    (hpl : PlacementOK π.pl) (hg : ∀ r, 0 < (π.geom r).align ∧ MM02.Pow2 (π.geom r).align)\n    (htc : TokCompat C π.tok) {ops : List Op3} {s3 s3' : S3} {pv : Nat → Option Nat}\n    {os : List Op2} {s2 : MM02.State} {op : Op3}\n    (ht : SimRun k C ObR ObW statics π ops s3 pv os s2) (hs : Step3 k op s3 s3')\n    (hob : Oblig k C ObR ObW π op s3 s3' pv s2) {l : Nat} (hl : l < s3.P.length)\n    (hlf : isLeaf s3.P l) (hpin : s3.pin l = true ∨ k.Pinned l) :\n    LiveAlloc s2 (π.L l).alloc ∧ LiveAlloc (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2)) (π.L l).alloc ∧\n      leafAddr (exec s2 (assoc π op s3 s2)) π.L l = leafAddr s2 π.L l := by\n  have h₁ := simulation hdd hstatR hstatW hpl hg htc ht\n  have h₂ := simulation hdd hstatR hstatW hpl hg htc (ht.step hs hob)\n  exact pinned_address_stable hdd h₁.2.2.2.1 hs.step h₁.2.2.1 h₂.2.2.1 hl hlf hpin\n\n/-! ## Cases (step 6 of the task)\n\nEach verdict is checked by `decide` on the precondition of the MM-03 step and on `Repr`, which is\ndecidable; the MM-02 sequences are exhibited by the definitions `opsN` and their effects. Each\nrefinement theorem is applied to a step of one scenario reached from `S3.init`. The obligations `dec` of the\ntest cases ask an access aligned on 4 bytes, a non-trivial instance (K5); `stat` is `True`, as K5\nfixes for the sequential fragment. -/\n\nnamespace CaseInit","numLines":345,"startLine":3040,"totalLines":3865}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2393cac8-90ce-4e28-892e-30c3565eccbc","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
