{"parentUuid":"7d39c427-b3f9-4994-9e15-87c93412e23f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb7KtEQCQoJ3o1FZH2Ee","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HcCoV3EmsNPpPY1WMgUiJf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad; cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<EOF\nsrc=open('$SP/p2work/sim_case.lean').read()\nbody=src[src.index(\"namespace CaseSim\"):]\n# docstrings\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"namespace CaseSim\n\nabbrev KS\"\"\",\"\"\"namespace CaseSim\n\n/-- Step 6 of the task: a full execution translated step by step through `simulation`. Contracts:\nleaf 0 (the metadata of the arena) `SharedMutable`; `ExternalDone` for 1; the storage 4\ndeallocable with the authority 7. Frame 1 has the locals 0 (arena value), 1 (allocator value), 2\n(destination of the block) and 3. `alloc` gives the storage 4, parts 5 and 6, owned by 0, of root\nauthority 4 (L2: one root); `newArena 4 4` registers it. The caller derives 5 (`Observe` on 0) and\n6 (`Modify` on 2), pins 1, and calls with `[5, 6]`; the callee has the locals 7 and 8. `issue` gives\nthe block 9 on the region `[5]`, held by 7; `store 5 8` writes a pointer to 0 into 8; `transfer 7 2`\nmoves the block to the caller; `exitFrame`; `endUse 2`; `reset`; `unpin 1`; `free 4 7`;\n`exitFrame`. -/\nabbrev KS\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"def C : Nat → Nat → Prop := fun a d => a = d\ndef L : Layout\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- MM-02 parameters fixed once for the run (`Params`): compatibility by equality of tokens (so\n`TokCompat`); frame token `100 + f`, provider token `6 + pr` (the allocator at place 1 has the\ntoken 7); geometry of 16 bytes aligned on 8 for every root; layout: one allocation per root, leaves\nof 8 bytes, the parts 5 and 6 at offsets 0 and 8 of the allocation of 4; pointers of 8 bytes, little\nendian, each byte carrying the provenance; the bytes written in leaf `l` are `10 l + i`. -/\ndef C : Nat → Nat → Prop := fun a d => a = d\ndef L : Layout\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"def obR : MM02.ReadOblSpec\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- Test obligations (K5): `dec`, an access aligned on 4 bytes; `stat`, true. -/\ndef obR : MM02.ReadOblSpec\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"def pv0 : Nat → Option Nat\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The ghost `provOf` (L4): empty, then the places 4, 5, 6 allocated from the provider 1. -/\ndef pv0 : Nat → Option Nat\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"def n0 : MM02.State\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The MM-02 states of the translation: the run of `repr_init` (no static), then the sequence\nassociated with each step (`assoc`); the steps without MM-02 operation keep the state. -/\ndef n0 : MM02.State\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"abbrev Run (s3\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- A prefix of the execution with its translation, the ghost and the MM-02 state named. -/\nabbrev Run (s3\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"theorem run0 :\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The execution, step by step: each `ok` step of MM-03 (`Step3`, checked by `decide`) with its\nobligations (`Oblig`: `NewLayout` for `enterFrame` and `alloc`, `dec` along its sequence, and\n`FreeOblig` for `free 4 7`, met by the provider 1 of 4 and `ptok 1 = 7`). -/\ntheorem run0 :\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"theorem sim {s3\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- `simulation` on every prefix of the run: an MM-02 run from `State.empty` with only `ok`\noutcomes, reaching the state of the translation, in `Repr`. -/\ntheorem sim {s3\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"example : ∃ os, AllOk C obR obW MM02.State.empty os ∧ exec MM02.State.empty os = n18\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- The whole execution: every MM-02 operation `ok`, `Repr` at the end; every allocation is dead at\nthe end (the storage 4 freed with the token 7, the locals deallocated at the exits). -/\nexample : ∃ os, AllOk C obR obW MM02.State.empty os ∧ exec MM02.State.empty os = n18\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"\n/-- Per-operation witnesses, from the run. -/\ntheorem inv\"\"\",\"\"\"\n/-- The invariants of MM-03 and `Repr` on a prefix of the run. -/\ntheorem inv\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"-- issue\nexample\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- `issue` (L6): R6 on the step of the run, and `pointer_sound_issue`: the bytes written in the\ndestination 7 decode to the address 104 of the leaf 5 (base of the allocation 4 of the storage, plus\noffset 0), and each carries the provenance 4, a live allocation. -/\nexample\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"-- store\nexample\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- `store` (L6), `pointer_sound_store`: the bytes written in 8 decode to the address 8 of the leaf 0\ncovered by the authority 5, and each carries the provenance 0, the allocation of 0. -/\nexample\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"-- transfer\nexample\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- `transfer` to the caller (L6), `transfer_copies`: the range of the destination 2 holds the bytes\nof the source 7, the pointer to the block with its provenance 4; the source range is unchanged. -/\nexample\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"-- reset: no MM-02 step; only the library state of the arena entry changes\nexample\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- `reset` (L6): no MM-02 step; only the library state of the arena entry (`available`, `issued`)\nchanges. -/\nexample\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"-- the block is now held by the leaf 2 of the caller\nexample\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- After `transfer`, the block 9 is held by the leaf 2 of the caller (J1). -/\nexample\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"-- without the write of `issue` or of `transfer`, `Repr` fails\nexample\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- Without the write of `issue` or of `transfer`, `Repr` fails (K3: an `Init` leaf has its bytes\ninitialised). -/\nexample\"\"\")\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"-- pin (L8 along the run): leaf 1 pinned before the transfer\nexample\"\"\",\"\"\"/-- L8 along the run (`simulation_pinned`): the leaf 1, pinned before the transfer, keeps a live\nallocation and its address across the reads and writes of the step. -/\nexample\"\"\")\ns=open('Ern/MM23.lean').read()\nassert s.endswith(\"end DraftGaps\\n\\nend Ern.MM23\\n\")\ns=s[:-len(\"end Ern.MM23\\n\")]+body+\"\\nend Ern.MM23\\n\"\nopen('Ern/MM23.lean','w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^--\" Ern/MM23.lean | head; tail -5 Ern/MM23.lean; time ~/.elan/bin/lake build 2>&1 | grep -v \"^✔\\|^⣿\\|Building\\|Replayed\" | head -30","description":"Insert the CaseSim namespace into the module and build","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1876,"cache_read_input_tokens":246855,"output_tokens":4115,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1407},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1876,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4115,"cache_read_input_tokens":246855,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1876},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HcCoV3EmsNPpPY1WMgUiJf":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad; cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<EOF\nsrc=open('$SP/p2work/sim_case.lean').read()\nbody=src[src.index(\"namespace CaseSim\"):]\n# docstrings\nbody=body.replace(\"\"\"namespace CaseSim\n\nabbrev KS\"\"\",\"\"\"namespace CaseSim\n\n/-- Step 6 of the task: a full execution translated step by step through `simulation`. Contracts:\nleaf 0 (the metadata of the arena) `SharedMutable`; `ExternalDone` for 1; the storage 4\ndeallocable with the authority 7. Frame 1 has the locals 0 (arena value), 1 (allocator value), 2\n(destination of the block) and 3. `alloc` gives the storage 4, parts 5 and 6, owned by 