{"parentUuid":"c7996910-cdce-4333-9b60-7c2d59c78638","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb7c11e2vRBLjCzmAs7r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Starting the adversarial review with five lens reviewers covering circularity, provenance, simulation vacuity, and a general pass on the remaining criteria; any findings will then go through a verifier that tries to refute them.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2526,"cache_read_input_tokens":274077,"output_tokens":6675,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2801},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6675,"cache_read_input_tokens":274077,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"9aa974f3-5cb2-425a-9058-40dc96cf7fe1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb7bzmFp2imaUxKtPJvv","requestRef":"272c8e41-b9bd-4379-be52-7bb3b844116a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c680c37-34e7-49d6-a84b-7e2759d38cfe","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:37:08.815Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"3c680c37-34e7-49d6-a84b-7e2759d38cfe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb7c11e2vRBLjCzmAs7r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ty86F6zaSqkpaJThzjt57k","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'mm23-p2-review',\n  description: 'Adversarial review of MM23 pass 2 by lens (L4, L6, L7, simulation, general), then refutation of each finding',\n  phases: [\n    { title: 'Review', detail: 'one reviewer per lens' },\n    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'one refuter per lens with findings' },\n  ],\n}\n\nconst SP = '/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad'\n\nconst COMMON = `You are an adversarial, read-only reviewer of a Lean 4 formalization (Lean core v4.35, no Mathlib).\nRepository: /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern, branch formal/refinement_0.1. Module under review: formal/Ern/MM23.lean (refinement MM-03 -> MM-02, about 4100 lines). It imports formal/Ern/MM02.lean and formal/Ern/MM03.lean (drafts, unchanged by this pass).\nThis pass (pass 2) = commits 9c08116..579808d; pass 1 ended at cd079be. Use git log / git diff cd079be 579808d -- formal/Ern/MM23.lean.\nTask brief of this pass (arbitrages L1-L8; they replace the K arbitrages of pass 1 where they say so): ${SP}/task_mm23_p2.md. Pass-1 brief (K1-K5): ${SP}/task_mm23_p1.md.\nNormative specs: /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM02_v04.md (MM-01, MM-02 v0.4) and /Users/guygouri/Downloads/ERN_MM-03.3_v0.3_revisee.md.\nFollow the Review section of AGENTS.md. Do NOT modify any file in the repository. For experiments, write Lean files only under ${SP}/review/<your lens>/ and check them with:\n  cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>\nwith the header \"import Ern.MM23\" then \"open Ern Ern.MM03 Ern.MM23\". The build is up to date; do not run lake build. decide works on concrete states (see the namespaces Cases and CaseSim at the end of MM23.lean).\nEvery finding needs evidence: a quote from the spec or brief, a Lean counterexample you checked (give the file path and the output), or command output. No evidence, no finding. Do not ask for additions beyond the brief. Severity: blocking (a statement wrong, vacuous, circular or weakened), major, minor. Cause: formalization error, missing coverage, spec defect.\nReturn only findings that survive your own check. An empty list is a valid answer.`\n\nconst LENSES = [\n  { key: 'L4', prompt: `Lens L4: circularity of freeSound_derived. Read ReprB (clause provTokens), FreeCompatInst, freeSound_derived, the pass-1 hypothesis FreeSound it replaces (find its definition), FreeOblig, provStep, r6_free, r6_alloc (hypothesis hprov), r6_enter, repr_init, and how simulation handles the ghost provOf.\nQuestions: is the conservation of the provider token along the trace actually imposed by Repr and derived, or assumed in a way that makes freeSound_derived circular or trivial? Does the ghost provOf change only at alloc, and could it be chosen per step to fit? Is the instantiation of FreeCompat p auth by Compatible auth (ptok (provOf p)) faithful to L4, including the direction of the implication in FreeOblig? Can a root created by alloc have provOf none, or a frame local or a static have provOf some, on a reached state of a SimRun? Is any statement stronger or weaker than L4 says?` },\n  { key: 'L6', prompt: `Lens L6: provenance or address lost or fabricated. Read transferPairs, copyOps, transferOps, bytesOf, SameSizeAlong, transfer_copies, r6_transfer; regionAddr, regionProv, ptrBytes, PtrEnc, PtrEncAt (it replaced PtrEncOK in commit 579808d), storeOps, issueOps, ptr_target, r6_store, r6_issue, pointer_sound_store, pointer_sound_issue; reset with no step.\nQuestions: does a definition lose or fabricate a provenance or an address (bytesOf defaults to (0, none) for a byte that is not initialised; empty regions; a region whose first leaf is not the lowest address; corresponding leaves of different sizes; the order of the pairs versus the ordered isomorphism of O4.2 / J1)? Is the L6 obligation of store (decode gives base + offset of the first leaf; each byte carries the provenance of the region's allocation) stated and proved, and not weakened? SameSizeAlong is a hypothesis of transfer_copies but not of r6_transfer nor of simulation: is that correct, and is it not a weakening of what L6 asks? Is the change PtrEncOK -> PtrEncAt a weakening of any statement? For issue, is the provenance the allocation of the arena storage?` },\n  { key: 'L7', prompt: `Lens L7: ddSound_of_layout. L7 says: prove ddSound_of_layout: under LayoutWF, instantiating K.DeclaredDisjoint by the byte-range disjointness of the leaves of both regions satisfies DDSound; the obligation is classed \"bibliothèque\". Read ddSound_of_layout, ByteDisjoint, ddSound_instance, the counterexample ddSound_of_layout_needs_size with its LayoutWF witness, byteDisjoint_of_leaves, and DDSound in MM03.lean.\nQuestions: does the statement match L7 (hypotheses and quantifiers; is LayoutWF used, or replaced by something else)? Is the extra positivity hypothesis justified, that is, is L7 false as literally stated (check the counterexample yourself, in Lean)? Is any hypothesis unsatisfiable or making the theorem trivial? Is ddSound_instance a faithful instantiation?` },\n  { key: 'SIM', prompt: `Lens simulation: vacuity through per-step parameters. Brief, step 5: \"for every Reachable execution from S3.init statics, with L, placement, tokens and ptrBytes fixed once (never chosen per step), there is an MM-02 execution from repr_init's initial state, all outcomes ok, in Repr at each step; the remaining hypotheses are listed in the statement\". Read Op3, NoOwner, Step3, Exec3, Params, assoc, provStep, initOpsOf, Trans, LayoutObl, FreeOblig, Oblig, SimRun, simulation, simulation_pinned, and the run in namespace CaseSim.\nQuestions: is anything chosen per step (layout, placement, tokens, pointer encoding, ghost, MM-02 sequence)? Are the per-step obligations in SimRun conditions on the fixed parameters along this run, or do they let the statement assume its conclusion? Are the hypotheses of simulation jointly satisfiable with a non-trivial run (check CaseSim)? Does the envelope of Step3 drop executions the brief requires: compare Step3 and Exec3 with Step and Reachable in MM03.lean (alloc fail, issue fail, steps whose outcome is not ok, enterFrame with an owning element, alloc with several roots)? Is \"in Repr at each step\" really obtained? Is the theorem weaker than the brief in a way not stated in its docstring?` },\n  { key: 'GEN', prompt: `Lens general: L1-L3, L5, L8, the R statements, no weakening, citations. Check Repr and ReprB against L3 (WF clause; Repr does not take k; Moved and Uninit impose nothing), r6_enter against L1, r6_alloc against L2, r6_free and r6_exit against L5 (owned storage leaks; the clause leaked), pinned_address_stable against L8 (LIVE allocation before and after, same base + offset; the docstring says MM-02 models no physical move).\nNo weakening: mechanically compare every theorem statement present at cd079be with its statement at HEAD (cut at the top-level :=, not the first one); for each changed statement say whether it is weaker (added hypothesis, narrower domain, weaker conclusion) and whether the brief allows the change; check that a removed theorem is replaced. Check that every definition or theorem that encodes a rule cites its clause or arbitrage in its docstring.` },\n]\n\nconst FINDINGS = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          id: { type: 'string' },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocking', 'major', 'minor'] },\n          location: { type: 'string' },\n          cause: { type: 'string' },\n          claim: { type: 'string' },\n          evidence: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n        required: ['id', 'severity', 'location', 'cause', 'claim', 'evidence'],\n      },\n    },\n    checked: { type: 'string', description: 'what you checked and found sound, briefly' },\n  },\n  required: ['findings', 'checked'],\n}\n\nconst VERDICTS = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    verdicts: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          id: { type: 'string' },\n          real: { type: 'boolean' },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocking', 'major', 'minor'] },\n          reason: { type: 'string' },\n          evidence: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n        required: ['id', 'real', 'severity', 'reason', 'evidence'],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  required: ['verdicts'],\n}\n\nconst results = await pipeline(\n  LENSES,\n  l => agent(`${COMMON}\\n\\n${l.prompt}\\n\\nUse ids ${l.key}-1, ${l.key}-2, ...`,\n    { label: `review:${l.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: FINDINGS }),\n  (rev, l) => {\n    if (!rev || rev.findings.length === 0) return { lens: l.key, review: rev, verdicts: [] }\n    return agent(`${COMMON.replace('reviewer', 'verifier')}\n\nA reviewer reported the findings below on the lens ${l.key}. For each one, try to REFUTE it: re-read the code and the spec or brief passage, rerun or rebuild its counterexample, check whether the defect really holds and whether the brief or an arbitrage allows it. Set real=false when the evidence does not hold up or the behaviour is what the brief asks; give your own severity when real.\n\nFindings:\n${JSON.stringify(rev.findings, null, 2)}`,\n      { label: `verify:${l.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERDICTS })\n      .then(v => ({ lens: l.key, review: rev, verdicts: v ? v.verdicts : null }))\n  },\n)\nreturn results\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2526,"cache_read_input_tokens":274077,