{"parentUuid":"452a07bf-90ba-4cfc-9ede-d2f926067c4c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e8b5e291-8f60-4fc9-8d4e-2bfcd70fe451","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wdps7v5g5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Ty86F6zaSqkpaJThzjt57k</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdps7v5g5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Adversarial review of MM23 pass 2 by lens (L4, L6, L7, simulation, general), then refutation of each finding\" completed</summary>\n<result>[{\"lens\":\"L4\",\"review\":{\"findings\":[],\"checked\":\"Lens L4 (is freeSound_derived circular?). Reviewed the committed MM23.lean at 579808d. No finding survived checking.\\n\\n1. **Is the conservation imposed and derived, or assumed?** It is imposed by Repr and derived along the trace, so there is no circularity.\\n   - `ReprB.provTokens` (MM23.lean:116) requires that every root r with `provOf r = some pr` has all its leaves in an allocation with `freeAuth = some (ptok pr)`.\\n   - `freeSound_derived` (1766) is a projection of that clause, combined with `FreeCompatInst`. The brief asks for exactly this: \\\"content = conservation along the trace ... (Repr imposes it)\\\".\\n   - The token is set when the allocation is created: `assoc` maps `.alloc pr` to `allocOps ... (some (π.ptok pr))`, and `r6_alloc` uses `hprov : provOf (n+i) = some pr`.\\n   - It is then preserved through `Dom` (MM23.lean:330, which includes `a'.freeAuth = a.freeAuth`) in ReprB.change, transport, shrink, repr_deallocs and repr_extend.\\n   - MM02 `State.write`, `dealloc` and `alloc` never change an existing `freeAuth`.\\n   - `simulation` re-establishes Repr at every step. Nothing about the token is assumed in a form that already contains FreeSound: FreeSound reads `k`, `auth` and `s2`, while provTokens reads only `ptok`, `provOf` and `s2`.\\n   - The pass-1 `FreeSound` definition is unchanged. It is no longer a hypothesis anywhere; its only use is as the conclusion of `freeSound_derived`, which `r6_free` calls (1795).\\n\\n2. **Does the ghost change only at alloc, and can it be chosen per step to fit?**\\n   - `provStep` changes the ghost only for `.alloc`. `SimRun`/`Trans` start from `fun _ =&gt; none` and thread `provStep op s3 pv` through each step, so the ghost is fixed by the run and `π`. It cannot be chosen per step.\\n   - `simulation` also proves `pv r = none` for every `r` beyond `P.length`. Indices are never reused, so a value, once set, never changes. The per-step `FreeOblig` is therefore equivalent to one instantiation for the whole execution.\\n   - Only enterP, allocP and transferEff modify P.\\n\\n3. **Instantiation and direction in FreeOblig.**\\n   - `FreeOblig` is `k.FreeCompat p auth → ∃ pr, pv p = some pr ∧ C auth (ptok pr)`, which matches `CanDealloc` (`Compatible auth d`).\\n   - FreeStep requires FreeCompat, so the implication is never vacuous on a free step.\\n   - FreeCompat is only a gate on `free`. Keeping only the → direction therefore weakens a hypothesis without weakening any conclusion.\\n\\n4. **Reached states of a SimRun.**\\n   - **Alloc'd roots never have provOf none:** provStep maps every index in `[len, len + ls.length)` to `some pr`.\\n   - **Statics never have provOf some:** the ghost starts at `none`, and `repr_init` takes `hprov = none`.\\n   - **Frame locals never have provOf some:** enter does not touch the ghost, and the beyond-length invariant gives `none`, which `r6_enter` uses through `hprov`.\\n   - **Owner kind is invariant:** shapeOwner gives an alloc'd root a place owner. mvTo maps a place owner to a place owner and leaves frame owners alone (heldIn of a frame is False). So an alloc'd root never meets the `tokens` (`tok f`) clause or `exitOps`.\\n   - **Uncovered frees are outside the envelope:** a free of a static or of a non-alloc'd root cannot meet FreeOblig. Under L1 (`Deallocable` false on statics, `NoOwner` in `Step3`), such a free never takes an ok step anyway.\\n   - **Parts also receive the provider in the ghost:** this changes no behaviour. provTokens quantifies only over RootPlace, and free requires OwnedRoot.\\n\\n5. **Checks run in Lean.**\\n   - Ern/MM23.olean was absent, and the working tree has an uncommitted 8-line `example` added to MM23.lean, which I did not review. I therefore compiled a copy of `git show 579808d:formal/Ern/MM23.lean` with my experiments appended:\\n     - copy: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L4/full.lean\\n     - experiments: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L4/ghost.lean\\n     - output: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L4/full.out\\n   - Result: no errors. `freeSound_derived`, `simulation` and `r6_free` each depend only on [propext, Quot.sound].\\n   - On the CaseSim run, `decide` confirms:\\n     - `pvA 4 = some 1`, and `pvA` is `none` on frame locals 0, 1, 2, 3, 7 and 8;\\n     - `¬ ReprB` with a wrong ghost (4 ↦ 2) at x3/n3, so the ghost is not free inside Repr;\\n     - `¬ FreeOblig` for a free of frame local 1 when FreeCompat holds.\\n\\n6. **Strength of statements against L4.**\\n   - `r6_alloc` now fixes the token to `ptok pr`.\\n   - `r6_free` now takes the FreeCompatInst implication instead of FreeSound.\\n   - The `hp : RootPlace` hypothesis of `freeSound_derived` matches O13 precondition 1 (OwnedRoot), and `r6_free` derives it.\\n   - No statement is stronger or weaker than L4.\\n   - Out of lens, not reported: the module header (MM23.lean lines 5–15) still says \\\"pass 1\\\" and lists transfer, store, issue, DDSound and pinned addresses as out of scope.\"},\"verdicts\":[]},{\"lens\":\"L6\",\"review\":{\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"L6-1\",\"severity\":\"major\