{"parentUuid":"398edc9f-76c2-47e9-9859-ef9e0c74e391","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb949VTbvHW1PooHGbSd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've confirmed issues L6-1 through L6-5, L7-1, and GEN-2, including a docstring problem on `r6_transfer`, while L7-2 and GEN-3 were refuted. Now I'll review the reviewers' \"checked\" notes for the simulation and general lenses before deciding on fixes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7124,"cache_read_input_tokens":360353,"output_tokens":468,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":215},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":360353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7124},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"bc272831-76c5-4757-9d4f-46aae1bbd79f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgb94979rXmP2gow1DGUH","requestRef":"972b3ba5-5066-4b13-a6c6-696a73b25b76","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"23e23f7b-bd96-4a64-a037-97063584e376","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:55:46.175Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"23e23f7b-bd96-4a64-a037-97063584e376","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb949VTbvHW1PooHGbSd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QZHxHeW1AqzMA41NcZ7o9w","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdps7v5g5.output'\ndata=json.load(open(p))['result']\nfor r in data:\n    if r['lens'] in ('SIM','GEN','L6','L7'):\n        print(\"=== \", r['lens']); print(r['review']['checked']); print()\nEOF","description":"Print the reviewers' notes on what they found sound"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7124,"cache_read_input_tokens":360353,"output_tokens":468,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":215},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":360353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7124},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QZHxHeW1AqzMA41NcZ7o9w":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wdps7v5g5.output'\ndata=json.load(open(p))['result']\nfor r in data:\n    if r['lens'] in ('SIM','GEN','L6','L7'):\n        print(\"=== \", r['lens']); print(r['review']['checked']); print()\nEOF","description":"Print the reviewers' notes on what they found sound"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bc272831-76c5-4757-9d4f-46aae1bbd79f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgb94979rXmP2gow1DGUH","requestRef":"972b3ba5-5066-4b13-a6c6-696a73b25b76","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5681156d-328b-43de-a414-44ce3719e9f3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:55:47.044Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"5681156d-328b-43de-a414-44ce3719e9f3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e8b5e291-8f60-4fc9-8d4e-2bfcd70fe451","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QZHxHeW1AqzMA41NcZ7o9w","type":"tool_result","content":"===  L6\nRead transferPairs, copyOps, transferOps, bytesOf, rangeBytes, SameSizeAlong, copyOps_run, copyOps_bytes, transfer_copies, ReprB.transport, r6_transfer, PtrEnc, PtrEncAt, regionAddr, regionProv, ptrBytes, storeOps, issueOps, ptr_target, r6_store, r6_issue, pointer_sound_store, pointer_sound_issue, r6_noStep for reset, and the simulation statement. I compared them with the L6 brief, MM-03.3 (O4, O8, O18, O19, §9.1) and MM02 (ReadStep, Alloc.write, State.write).\n\nSound:\n- Pairing: transferPairs follows source footprint order and pairs each leaf through corr (ordered isomorphism, J1/O4.2). SameShape ensures every destination leaf is reached (corr_leaf_back).\n- Copy fidelity: an MM-02 read returns the raw bytesAt with provenance, so bytesOf matches \"the bytes read\". Under SameSizeAlong and Repr.init, the (0, none) default of bytesOf is never reached, and transfer_copies proves destination range = source range (value and provenance) with source ranges unchanged.\n- r6_transfer, r6_store and r6_issue correctly give AllOk and Repr.\n- ptr_target proves the live allocation and base + off for non-empty regions.\n- Regions lie within one root, so they map to one allocation.\n- reset has no step: r6_noStep plus the CaseSim example.\n- PtrEncOK -> PtrEncAt is not a weakening: at 10b837c PtrEncOK was defined but used by no theorem, and PtrEncAt is implied by PtrEncOK and appears only as a hypothesis. The decode conjunct of pointer_sound_* is that hypothesis restated, as the brief's obligation framing implies.\n\nExperiments: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L6/IssueRegion.lean, SizeRun.lean and StoreEmpty.lean in the same directory. All three pass with exit=0 against the current olean.\n\nNote: the working tree is not clean. It contains an uncommitted example appended to MM23.lean (the report's witness for question (e) 2) and a deleted formal/Ern/.gitkeep. I did not make either change, and neither touches the definitions under review. I did not re-check axioms.\n\n===  L7\nStatement vs L7. ddSound_of_layout does not take LayoutWF. In its place it takes (h) that every declaration implies ByteDisjoint L and (hpos) that leaves of the first declared region have positive length. Dropping LayoutWF makes it stronger, not weaker. LayoutWF cannot help: an index shared by both regions forces a range to be disjoint from itself. hpos is restricted to declared regions and to r only, which is minimal. Neither hypothesis is unsatisfiable or trivialising: in my file, Lq l := ⟨0,l,1⟩ gives ByteDisjoint Lq [0] [1] and DDSound of the instance via ddSound_instance. The proof is not circular, since DDSound is not assumed.\n\nddSound_instance is a faithful instantiation: `{k with DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint L}`. ByteDisjoint compares every leaf of r with every leaf of r': different allocation, or MM02.RangeDisjoint. This matches byte disjointness, because MM-02 bytes are per allocation (Alloc.bytes). Regions are lists of leaves (K docstring, MM03.lean). Its hypothesis `∀ l, 0 < len` is exactly necessary (my inst_iff).\n\nThe repo counterexample and its LayoutWF witness re-check in my file. byteDisjoint_of_leaves is correct and uses LayoutWF.disjoint.\n\nDocstrings cite L7 and MM-03.3.8. #print axioms for ddSound_of_layout, ddSound_instance, ddSound_of_layout_needs_size and byteDisjoint_of_leaves gives [propext, Quot.sound].\n\nThe untracked draft report formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md still has placeholders in (e). I did not treat that as a finding, since it is outside the commits under review. The draft's simulation-hypothesis table does mention the non-empty-range condition.\n\nSkipped: whether the MM03 draft's leaf-level DDSound matches spec §8 wording (MM-03 draft fixes are out of scope). No repository file was modified.\n\n===  SIM\nNothing is chosen per step. `Params` (L, tok, ptok, pl, geom, pe, w0) is one implicit argument, universally quantified in `simulation`. `assoc` computes the MM-02 sequence deterministically from π, op, s3 and s2. `provStep` updates the ghost deterministically (alloc only), starting from `fun _ => none`. `Trans` and `SimRun` append `assoc` and `exec` it, with no free choice. The `w` of `Op3.write`/`writeShared` is program data that `Step3` ignores; it is universally quantified, so it only makes the theorem more general.\n\nThe `SimRun` obligations are conditions on the fixed parameters along this run, and none of them assumes the conclusion:\n- `LayoutObl` is `NewLayout` of π.L for the new places against s2.next and π.geom (K1/K2). It can always be met by one L for the whole run, because `s2.next` does not depend on L and len 0 is allowed.\n- `DecAlong` is the K5 `dec` part only. The `Read`, `CanWrite` and `CanDealloc` parts of `AllOk` come from `Repr`.\n- `FreeOblig` is the L4 instantiation `k.FreeCompat → ∃ pr, pv p = some pr ∧ C auth (ptok pr)`. The token itself comes from `Repr.provTokens`, as L4 requires. `FreeOblig` only excludes frees of statics, which L1 forbids (Deallocable false on statics), since under NoOwner every other owned root comes from alloc.\n\nEnvelope: `Op3` and `Step3` have exactly the 19 constructors of `Reachable` and `Step` (KStep plus newArena, issue, reset), with the same `ok` relations. They add only NoOwner (L1, enter) and `rootIdx ls = [i]` (L2, alloc), and the docstring states both. alloc fail and issue fail (`.fail s`, state unchanged), as well as reject, are outside `Reachable` too, so no reachable state is lost.\n\nConclusion: `AllOk` from `State.empty` over `initOpsOf ++` the step sequences, `exec = s2`, `Repr` (including `MM02.WF`), `Reachable`, and the ghost empty beyond the places. Every prefix of a `SimRun` is a sub-derivation, so `Repr` holds at each MM-03 step.\n\nSatisfiability:\n- `CaseSim` runs 18 steps (enter, write, alloc, newArena, derive, pin, issue, store, transfer to caller, exit, endUse, reset, unpin, free with FreeOblig met by ptok 1 = 7, exit) through `simulation`. Its `dec` is non-trivial (addr % 4 = 0), and the `¬ReprB` examples show `Repr` rejects wrong states.\n- I checked a run with non-empty statics plus enter, write and exit through `simulation`, in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/simulation/statics_run.lean. It compiles with no output.\n- `#print axioms` for simulation, simulation_pinned, CaseSim.run18 and CaseSim.sim gives [propext, Quot.sound].\n\nI found no weakening of the theorem against the brief's step 5 that the docstring leaves out.\n\nNot checked: the strength of `Repr` itself (pass-1 lens), L7 positivity, and pointer soundness along the run. Brief step 5 does not ask for pointer soundness: `pe` carries no obligation in `simulation`, and the `PtrEncAt` obligation stays per step in `pointer_sound_*`.\n\n===  GEN\nI compared every theorem statement mechanically. A script cut each statement at the top-level := (or at the first top-level match arm) in cd079be and 579808d: 97 theorems before, 177 after, 72 identical, 21 changed, 4 removed. The script and outputs are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/general/ (stmts.py, stmts.out, defs.py).\n\n**Removed theorems.** All four are replaced:\n- Repr.change by ReprB.change and Repr.shrink by ReprB.shrink, with the same statements apart from the Repr→ReprB signature.\n- Cases.wfm8 by Cases.wf_m8.\n- Cases.wf2 is covered by exec_wf and wf_m0.\n\n**Changed definitions.** Only Repr changed. ReprB is the old Repr plus provTokens, and Repr is ReprB plus wf2, so every clause got stronger.\n\n**Changed theorem statements, none weakened beyond what the brief allows:**\n- **No weakening at all:** repr_writes, repr_of_nil, covered_live, repr_deallocs. They now use ReprB, or the old Repr plus provTokens, in hypothesis and conclusion.\n- **Added ghost hypothesis that is trivial with provOf := none, conclusion stronger:** repr_extend, repr_init, r6_enter.\n- **Hypothesis gains MM02.WF:** r1_read3, r2_*, r6_read3, r6_noStep, r6_exit(_reachable), r4_no_dead_cover. L3 allows this, and WF also appears in the conclusions.\n- **r6_alloc:** the old version quantified over any token fa; the new one fixes it to some (ptok pr) and adds hprov. L4 requires this.\n- **r6_free:** the FreeSound hypothesis is replaced by k.FreeCompat → FreeCompatInst. L4 says this replaces FreeSound. Under Repr this hypothesis implies FreeSound (freeSound_derived). Owned locals and statics, which the old version also covered, are out of the language by L1.\n\n**Pass-1 counterexamples.** All kept, restated with ReprB; ¬ReprB is stronger than ¬Repr.\n\n**L3.** Repr extends ReprB with the clause wf2 : MM02.WF s2. Its parameters are tok, ptok, provOf, L, s3 and s2, with no k (`#print Repr` output). Only the init clause reads I, and only for .init, so Moved and Uninit impose nothing.\n\n**L1.**\n- Step3 requires NoOwner ls for enter, and NoOwner checks the owning element (.2.1).\n- r6_enter is proved without that condition, which makes it more general, and its docstring says so.\n- Statics with owning elements are allowed: SimRun.init only requires ShapeOK.\n- A free of a static cannot occur in a SimRun. FreePre needs FreeCompat, FreeOblig then needs pv p = some pr, and pv is none on statics. This matches \"K.Deallocable false on statics\".\n\n**L2.** r6_alloc has hone : rootIdx ls = [i], and Step3 for alloc requires ∃ i, rootIdx ls = [i].\n\n**L5.**\n- r6_free issues exactly one DeallocStep, on rootAlloc of p.\n- exitOps deallocates only frameRoots, the roots owned by the frame.\n- The leaked clause (not usable, not freed, owned by a place ⇒ allocation live) appears in Repr's conclusion. The witnesses e16/m16 and af14/na14 confirm the owned storage stays live.\n\n**L8.** pinned_address_stable concludes:\n- LiveAlloc before;\n- LiveAlloc after;\n- leafAddr (base + offset) after equals leafAddr before.\n\nIt covers dynamic pins (s3.pin) and static pins (k.Pinned), and its docstring says MM-02 models no physical move. It holds for any `ops` after which Repr holds, which is more general than \"the step's own sequence\". simulation_pinned instantiates it with assoc, and the CaseSim witness at line 4118 applies it, so it is not vacuous.\n\n**Axioms.** `#print axioms` gives only [propext, Quot.sound] for pinned_address_stable, simulation, simulation_pinned, r6_free, r6_enter, r6_exit, r6_alloc and freeSound_derived (gen_check.lean output).\n\n**Citations.** Every new rule-encoding declaration cites its clause or arbitrage, apart from GEN-3 and helper lemmas such as posIn_*, index_inj_of_lt, mem_transferPairs and decAlong_readOps.\n\n**Out of scope for this lens:** I did not judge the content of L4, L6 and L7, the arena cases, or whether the per-step simulation obligations make it vacuous. I did not re-run lake build.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ab621def-f522-4f38-89a1-3bb4fad2a805","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:55:47.625Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"===  L6\nRead transferPairs, copyOps, transferOps, bytesOf, rangeBytes, SameSizeAlong, copyOps_run, copyOps_bytes, transfer_copies, ReprB.transport, r6_transfer, PtrEnc, PtrEncAt, regionAddr, regionProv, ptrBytes, storeOps, issueOps, ptr_target, r6_store, r6_issue, pointer_sound_store, pointer_sound_issue, r6_noStep for reset, and the simulation statement. I compared them with the L6 brief, MM-03.3 (O4, O8, O18, O19, §9.1) and MM02 (ReadStep, Alloc.write, State.write).\n\nSound:\n- Pairing: transferPairs follows source footprint order and pairs each leaf through corr (ordered isomorphism, J1/O4.2). SameShape ensures every destination leaf is reached (corr_leaf_back).\n- Copy fidelity: an MM-02 read returns the raw bytesAt with provenance, so bytesOf matches \"the bytes read\". Under SameSizeAlong and Repr.init, the (0, none) default of bytesOf is never reached, and transfer_copies proves destination range = source range (value and provenance) with source ranges unchanged.\n- r6_transfer, r6_store and r6_issue correctly give AllOk and Repr.\n- ptr_target proves the live allocation and base + off for non-empty regions.\n- Regions lie within one root, so they map to one allocation.\n- reset has no step: r6_noStep plus the CaseSim example.\n- PtrEncOK -> PtrEncAt is not a weakening: at 10b837c PtrEncOK was defined but used by no theorem, and PtrEncAt is implied by PtrEncOK and appears only as a hypothesis. The decode conjunct of pointer_sound_* is that hypothesis restated, as the brief's obligation framing implies.\n\nExperiments: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/L6/IssueRegion.lean, SizeRun.lean and StoreEmpty.lean in the same directory. All three pass with exit=0 against the current olean.\n\nNote: the working tree is not clean. It contains an uncommitted example appended to MM23.lean (the report's witness for question (e) 2) and a deleted formal/Ern/.gitkeep. I did not make either change, and neither touches the definitions under review. I did not re-check axioms.\n\n===  L7\nStatement vs L7. ddSound_of_layout does not take LayoutWF. In its place it takes (h) that every declaration implies ByteDisjoint L and (hpos) that leaves of the first declared region have positive length. Dropping LayoutWF makes it stronger, not weaker. LayoutWF cannot help: an index shared by both regions forces a range to be disjoint from itself. hpos is restricted to declared regions and to r only, which is minimal. Neither hypothesis is unsatisfiable or trivialising: in my file, Lq l := ⟨0,l,1⟩ gives ByteDisjoint Lq [0] [1] and DDSound of the instance via ddSound_instance. The proof is not circular, since DDSound is not assumed.\n\nddSound_instance is a faithful instantiation: `{k with DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint L}`. ByteDisjoint compares every leaf of r with every leaf of r': different allocation, or MM02.RangeDisjoint. This matches byte disjointness, because MM-02 bytes are per allocation (Alloc.bytes). Regions are lists of leaves (K docstring, MM03.lean). Its hypothesis `∀ l, 0 < len` is exactly necessary (my inst_iff).\n\nThe repo counterexample and its LayoutWF witness re-check in my file. byteDisjoint_of_leaves is correct and uses LayoutWF.disjoint.\n\nDocstrings cite L7 and MM-03.3.8. #print axioms for ddSound_of_layout, ddSound_instance, ddSound_of_layout_needs_size and byteDisjoint_of_leaves gives [propext, Quot.sound].\n\nThe untracked draft report formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md still has placeholders in (e). I did not treat that as a finding, since it is outside the commits under review. The draft's simulation-hypothesis table does mention the non-empty-range condition.\n\nSkipped: whether the MM03 draft's leaf-level DDSound matches spec §8 wording (MM-03 draft fixes are out of scope). No repository file was modified.\n\n===  SIM\nNothing is chosen per step. `Params` (L, tok, ptok, pl, geom, pe, w0) is one implicit argument, universally quantified in `simulation`. `assoc` computes the MM-02 sequence deterministically from π, op, s3 and s2. `provStep` updates the ghost deterministically (alloc only), starting from `fun _ => none`. `Trans` and `SimRun` append `assoc` and `exec` it, with no free choice. The `w` of `Op3.write`/`writeShared` is program data that `Step3` ignores; it is universally quantified, so it only makes the theorem more general.\n\nThe `SimRun` obligations are conditions on the fixed parameters along this run, and none of them assumes the conclusion:\n- `LayoutObl` is `NewLayout` of π.L for the new places against s2.next and π.geom (K1/K2). It can always be met by one L for the whole run, because `s2.next` does not depend on L and len 0 is allowed.\n- `DecAlong` is the K5 `dec` part only. The `Read`, `CanWrite` and `CanDealloc` parts of `AllOk` come from `Repr`.\n- `FreeOblig` is the L4 instantiation `k.FreeCompat → ∃ pr, pv p = some pr ∧ C auth (ptok pr)`. The token itself comes from `Repr.provTokens`, as L4 requires. `FreeOblig` only excludes frees of statics, which L1 forbids (Deallocable false on statics), since under NoOwner every other owned root comes from alloc.\n\nEnvelope: `Op3` and `Step3` have exactly the 19 constructors of `Reachable` and `Step` (KStep plus newArena, issue, reset), with the same `ok` relations. They add only NoOwner (L1, enter) and `rootIdx ls = [i]` (L2, alloc), and the docstring states both. alloc fail and issue fail (`.fail s`, state unchanged), as well as reject, are outside `Reachable` too, so no reachable state is lost.\n\nConclusion: `AllOk` from `State.empty` over `initOpsOf ++` the step sequences, `exec = s2`, `Repr` (including `MM02.WF`), `Reachable`, and the ghost empty beyond the places. Every prefix of a `SimRun` is a sub-derivation, so `Repr` holds at each MM-03 step.\n\nSatisfiability:\n- `CaseSim` runs 18 steps (enter, write, alloc, newArena, derive, pin, issue, store, transfer to caller, exit, endUse, reset, unpin, free with FreeOblig met by ptok 1 = 7, exit) through `simulation`. Its `dec` is non-trivial (addr % 4 = 0), and the `¬ReprB` examples show `Repr` rejects wrong states.\n- I checked a run with non-empty statics plus enter, write and exit through `simulation`, in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/simulation/statics_run.lean. It compiles with no output.\n- `#print axioms` for simulation, simulation_pinned, CaseSim.run18 and CaseSim.sim gives [propext, Quot.sound].\n\nI found no weakening of the theorem against the brief's step 5 that the docstring leaves out.\n\nNot checked: the strength of `Repr` itself (pass-1 lens), L7 positivity, and pointer soundness along the run. Brief step 5 does not ask for pointer soundness: `pe` carries no obligation in `simulation`, and the `PtrEncAt` obligation stays per step in `pointer_sound_*`.\n\n===  GEN\nI compared every theorem statement mechanically. A script cut each statement at the top-level := (or at the first top-level match arm) in cd079be and 579808d: 97 theorems before, 177 after, 72 identical, 21 changed, 4 removed. The script and outputs are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review/general/ (stmts.py, stmts.out, defs.py).\n\n**Removed theorems.** All four are replaced:\n- Repr.change by ReprB.change and Repr.shrink by ReprB.shrink, with the same statements apart from the Repr→ReprB signature.\n- Cases.wfm8 by Cases.wf_m8.\n- Cases.wf2 is covered by exec_wf and wf_m0.\n\n**Changed definitions.** Only Repr changed. ReprB is the old Repr plus provTokens, and Repr is ReprB plus wf2, so every clause got stronger.\n\n**Changed theorem statements, none weakened beyond what the brief allows:**\n- **No weakening at all:** repr_writes, repr_of_nil, covered_live, repr_deallocs. They now use ReprB, or the old Repr plus provTokens, in hypothesis and conclusion.\n- **Added ghost hypothesis that is trivial with provOf := none, conclusion stronger:** repr_extend, repr_init, r6_enter.\n- **Hypothesis gains MM02.WF:** r1_read3, r2_*, r6_read3, r6_noStep, r6_exit(_reachable), r4_no_dead_cover. L3 allows this, and WF also appears in the conclusions.\n- **r6_alloc:** the old version quantified over any token fa; the new one fixes it to some (ptok pr) and adds hprov. L4 requires this.\n- **r6_free:** the FreeSound hypothesis is replaced by k.FreeCompat → FreeCompatInst. L4 says this replaces FreeSound. Under Repr this hypothesis implies FreeSound (freeSound_derived). Owned locals and statics, which the old version also covered, are out of the language by L1.\n\n**Pass-1 counterexamples.** All kept, restated with ReprB; ¬ReprB is stronger than ¬Repr.\n\n**L3.** Repr extends ReprB with the clause wf2 : MM02.WF s2. Its parameters are tok, ptok, provOf, L, s3 and s2, with no k (`#print Repr` output). Only the init clause reads I, and only for .init, so Moved and Uninit impose nothing.\n\n**L1.**\n- Step3 requires NoOwner ls for enter, and NoOwner checks the owning element (.2.1).\n- r6_enter is proved without that condition, which makes it more general, and its docstring says so.\n- Statics with owning elements are allowed: SimRun.init only requires ShapeOK.\n- A free of a static cannot occur in a SimRun. FreePre needs FreeCompat, FreeOblig then needs pv p = some pr, and pv is none on statics. This matches \"K.Deallocable false on statics\".\n\n**L2.** r6_alloc has hone : rootIdx ls = [i], and Step3 for alloc requires ∃ i, rootIdx ls = [i].\n\n**L5.**\n- r6_free issues exactly one DeallocStep, on rootAlloc of p.\n- exitOps deallocates only frameRoots, the roots owned by the frame.\n- The leaked clause (not usable, not freed, owned by a place ⇒ allocation live) appears in Repr's conclusion. The witnesses e16/m16 and af14/na14 confirm the owned storage stays live.\n\n**L8.** pinned_address_stable concludes:\n- LiveAlloc before;\n- LiveAlloc after;\n- leafAddr (base + offset) after equals leafAddr before.\n\nIt covers dynamic pins (s3.pin) and static pins (k.Pinned), and its docstring says MM-02 models no physical move. It holds for any `ops` after which Repr holds, which is more general than \"the step's own sequence\". simulation_pinned instantiates it with assoc, and the CaseSim witness at line 4118 applies it, so it is not vacuous.\n\n**Axioms.** `#print axioms` gives only [propext, Quot.sound] for pinned_address_stable, simulation, simulation_pinned, r6_free, r6_enter, r6_exit, r6_alloc and freeSound_derived (gen_check.lean output).\n\n**Citations.** Every new rule-encoding declaration cites its clause or arbitrage, apart from GEN-3 and helper lemmas such as posIn_*, index_inj_of_lt, mem_transferPairs and decAlong_readOps.\n\n**Out of scope for this lens:** I did not judge the content of L4, L6 and L7, the arena cases, or whether the per-step simulation obligations make it vacuous. I did not re-run lake build.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bc272831-76c5-4757-9d4f-46aae1bbd79f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5681156d-328b-43de-a414-44ce3719e9f3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
