{"parentUuid":"3797c469-e852-4b30-8986-f559d7ce7868","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e8b5e291-8f60-4fc9-8d4e-2bfcd70fe451","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UoCfQMbNHjvLose7BZGTn3","type":"tool_result","content":"        rw [hpl]; exact hplc ho\n    exact (hR.leaked r hr hrt hu hf ho' l hl).of_dom hd fun a a' _ _ e _ _ h => e ▸ h\n\n/-- R6 for `transfer` (MM-03.3 §9.2, O4; L6: for each pair of corresponding leaves, a `ReadStep` of\nthe source range then a `WriteStep` of the destination range with the bytes read, provenance\nincluded; held authorities and owned storage give no step): under `WF3`, `SameSizeAlong` (spec 4),\n`dec` along the run and `stat` (K5), every read and write has the outcome `ok` and the arrival\nstates are in `Repr`. The source ranges stay initialised in MM-02; MM-03 makes them unreadable\n(`Moved`). -/\n----\n\n/-- L6, `ptrBytes`: the bytes of a pointer to the region `rg`. -/\ndef ptrBytes (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (rg : List Nat) :\n    Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat :=\n  pe.enc (regionAddr s2 L rg) (regionProv L rg)\n\n/-- L6 (`store a p`): one write of the range of the leaf `p` with the bytes of a pointer to the\nregion covered by `a`. -/\ndef storeOps (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (s3 : S3) (a p : Nat) : List Op2 :=\n  [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write p) (ptrBytes pe s2 L (s3.afp a))]\n\n/-- L6 (`issue`): one write of the range of the destination with the bytes of a pointer to the\nblock; `available` and `issued` are abstract state of the arena entry (library obligation). -/\ndef issueOps (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    List Op2 :=\n  [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (ptrBytes pe s2 L region)]\n\n/-- L6: the pointer to a region whose first leaf `l` is covered by an active authority is neither\nlost nor fabricated: its provenance is the allocation of `l`, which is live, and its address is\nthe address of `l`, within that allocation. -/\n----\n3283:/-- `simulation` (step 5): along every execution of MM-03 from `S3.init statics` within the\n3284-envelope of L1 and L2, translated with parameters `π` fixed once for the whole execution, whose\n3285-steps meet their obligations (`SimRun`), the MM-02 run starts with the run of `repr_init`, appends\n3286-at each step the sequence associated by K4 and L6, has only `ok` outcomes, reaches the state `s2`,\n3287-and is in `Repr` with the MM-03 state; the MM-03 state is reached, and the ghost `provOf` is empty\n3288-beyond the places. Since every prefix of a `SimRun` is a `SimRun`, this holds at each step. The\n3289-remaining hypotheses: `DDSound k` (L7: `ddSound_of_layout`); `stat` (K5); the obligation of the\n3290-placement and valid alignments (K2); the compatibility of the frame tokens (K2). -/\n3291-theorem simulation {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c0904e39-f0ba-466f-a84e-8e628a488dc6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:59:14.418Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"        rw [hpl]; exact hplc ho\n    exact (hR.leaked r hr hrt hu hf ho' l hl).of_dom hd fun a a' _ _ e _ _ h => e ▸ h\n\n/-- R6 for `transfer` (MM-03.3 §9.2, O4; L6: for each pair of corresponding leaves, a `ReadStep` of\nthe source range then a `WriteStep` of the destination range with the bytes read, provenance\nincluded; held authorities and owned storage give no step): under `WF3`, `SameSizeAlong` (spec 4),\n`dec` along the run and `stat` (K5), every read and write has the outcome `ok` and the arrival\nstates are in `Repr`. The source ranges stay initialised in MM-02; MM-03 makes them unreadable\n(`Moved`). -/\n----\n\n/-- L6, `ptrBytes`: the bytes of a pointer to the region `rg`. -/\ndef ptrBytes (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (rg : List Nat) :\n    Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat :=\n  pe.enc (regionAddr s2 L rg) (regionProv L rg)\n\n/-- L6 (`store a p`): one write of the range of the leaf `p` with the bytes of a pointer to the\nregion covered by `a`. -/\ndef storeOps (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (s3 : S3) (a p : Nat) : List Op2 :=\n  [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write p) (ptrBytes pe s2 L (s3.afp a))]\n\n/-- L6 (`issue`): one write of the range of the destination with the bytes of a pointer to the\nblock; `available` and `issued` are abstract state of the arena entry (library obligation). -/\ndef issueOps (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :\n    List Op2 :=\n  [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (ptrBytes pe s2 L region)]\n\n/-- L6: the pointer to a region whose first leaf `l` is covered by an active authority is neither\nlost nor fabricated: its provenance is the allocation of `l`, which is live, and its address is\nthe address of `l`, within that allocation. -/\n----\n3283:/-- `simulation` (step 5): along every execution of MM-03 from `S3.init statics` within the\n3284-envelope of L1 and L2, translated with parameters `π` fixed once for the whole execution, whose\n3285-steps meet their obligations (`SimRun`), the MM-02 run starts with the run of `repr_init`, appends\n3286-at each step the sequence associated by K4 and L6, has only `ok` outcomes, reaches the state `s2`,\n3287-and is in `Repr` with the MM-03 state; the MM-03 state is reached, and the ghost `provOf` is empty\n3288-beyond the places. Since every prefix of a `SimRun` is a `SimRun`, this holds at each step. The\n3289-remaining hypotheses: `DDSound k` (L7: `ddSound_of_layout`); `stat` (K5); the obligation of the\n3290-placement and valid alignments (K2); the compatibility of the frame tokens (K2). -/\n3291-theorem simulation {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b1c944eb-c716-4e38-ac26-89f3619cb5c9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3797c469-e852-4b30-8986-f559d7ce7868","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
