s `K1`…`K5`. The rules of the specifications are cited","-as `MM-02.x` (MM-02 v0.4) and `MM-03.3 …` (MM-03.3 v0.3 révisée). Out of scope: `transfer`,","-`store`, `issue`, concurrency, real `DDSound`, stability of pinned addresses, low-level translation.","-The decisions not dictated by the texts are listed in the report `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md`,","-section (c); the gaps between the drafts and their texts, section (f).","+machine of MM-02 (module `Ern.MM02`), refinement of every operation of MM-03 (R6), and simulation","+of an execution. Both modules are imported unchanged; a lemma they lack is proved here.","+","+The arbitrages of the task are cited as `K1`…`K5` (pass 1) and `L1`…`L8` (pass 2, which replace","+the K arbitrages where they say so). The rules of the specifications are cited as `MM-02.x`","+(MM-02 v0.4) and `MM-03.3 …` (MM-03.3 v0.3 révisée). Out of scope: concurrency, finite addresses,","+representation of the metadata of arenas, low-level translation. The decisions not dictated by the","+texts are listed in the reports `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1.md` (pass 1) and","+`formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md` (pass 2), section (c); the gaps between the drafts and their","+texts, section (f) of the pass-1 report."," -/"," "," namespace Ern.MM23"]},{"oldStart":2224,"oldLines":11,"newStart":2226,"newLines":13,"lines":["     exact (hR.leaked r hr hrt hu hf ho' l hl).of_dom hd fun a a' _ _ e _ _ h => e ▸ h"," "," /-- R6 for `transfer` (MM-03.3 §9.2, O4; L6: for each pair of corresponding leaves, a `ReadStep` of","-the source range then a `WriteStep` of the destination range with the bytes read, provenance","-included; held authorities and owned storage give no step): under `WF3`, `SameSizeAlong` (spec 4),","+the source range then a `WriteStep` of the destination range with the bytes of the source range","+(`bytesOf`), provenance included; held authorities and owned storage give no step): under `WF3`,"," `dec` along the run and `stat` (K5), every read and write has the outcome `ok` and the arrival","-states are in `Repr`. The source ranges stay initialised in MM-02; MM-03 makes them unreadable","-(`Moved`). -/","+states are in `Repr`. The theorem does not take `SameSizeAlong` (L6, spec 4): without it, the","+write is not the copy of the bytes read (it reads past the source range, or copies a part of it);","+`transfer_copies`, which takes it, states the copy. The source ranges stay initialised in MM-02;","+MM-03 makes them unreadable (`Moved`). -/"," theorem r6_transfer {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec}","     {k : K} {tok ptok : Nat → Nat} {provOf : Nat → Option Nat} {L : Layout} {s3 s3' : S3}","     {s2 : MM02.State} {src dst : Nat} (hwf : WF3 s3) (hR : Repr tok ptok provOf L s3 s2)"]},{"oldStart":2449,"oldLines":8,"newStart":2453,"newLines":9,"lines":[" def PtrEncAt (pe : PtrEnc) (addr : Nat) (prov : Option Nat) : Prop :=","   pe.decode (pe.enc addr prov) = addr ∧ ∀ i, (pe.enc addr prov i).2 = prov"," ","-/-- L6: address of the first byte of the region `rg`: base of the allocation of its first leaf plus","-the offset of that leaf. -/","+/-- L6 (\"base + off of first leaf\"): address of the pointer to the region `rg`: base of the","+allocation of the first leaf of the list plus the offset of that leaf. It is the first byte of the","+region when that leaf has the lowest offset; K1 fixes no order of fields (report, (e) 3). -/"," def regionAddr (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (rg : List Nat) : Nat :=","   match rg.head? with","   | some l => (((s2.allocs (L l).alloc).map (·.base)).getD 0) + (L l).off"]},{"oldStart":2470,"oldLines":11,"newStart":2475,"newLines":24,"lines":[" def storeOps (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (s3 : S3) (a p : Nat) : List Op2 :=","   [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write p) (ptrBytes pe s2 L (s3.afp a))]"," ","-/-- L6 (`issue`): one write of the range of the destination with the bytes of a pointer to the","-block; `available` and `issued` are abstract state of the arena entry (library obligation). -/","-def issueOps (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat) :","-    List Op2 :=","-  [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (ptrBytes pe s2 L region)]","+/-- L6 (`issue`, \"prov: allocation of arena storage\"): the provenance of a block of the arena entry","+`i` of `s3`: the allocation of the storage of the arena, read on its first leaf (as `rootAlloc`","+reads a root); none for a missing entry. -/","+def arenaProv (L : Layout) (s3 : S3) (i : Nat) : Option Nat :=","+  (s3.arenas[i]?).map fun ar => (L ((footprint s3.P ar.storage).headD ar.storage)).alloc","+","+/-- L6, the bytes of the pointer to the block `region` of the arena entry `i`: the address of the","+region (`regionAddr`) and the provenance of the storage of the arena (`arenaProv`). -/","+def issueBytes (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (s3 : S3) (i : Nat)","+    (region : List Nat) : Nat → UInt8 × Option Nat :=","+  pe.enc (regionAddr s2 L region) (arenaProv L s3 i)","+","+/-- L6 (`issue` on the arena entry `i`): one write of the range of the destination with the bytes of","+the pointer to the block; `available` and `issued` are abstract state of the arena entry (library","+obligation). -/","+def issueOps (pe : PtrEnc) (s2 : MM02.State) (L : Layout) (s3 : S3) (i : Nat) (region : List Nat)","+    (dst : Nat) : List Op2 :=","+  [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region)]"," "," /-- L6: the pointer to a region whose first leaf `l` is covered by an active authority is neither"," lost nor fabricated: its provenance is the allocation of `l`, which is live, and its address is"]},{"oldStart":2530,"oldLines":11,"newStart":2548,"newLines":12,"lines":["     {s2 : MM02.State} {pe : PtrEnc} {i via dst : Nat} {region : List Nat} (hwf : WF3 s3)","     (hR : Repr tok ptok provOf L s3 s2) (h : IssueAt k i via region dst s3 (.ok s3'))","     (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)","-    (hdec : ObW.dec s2 (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (ptrBytes pe s2 L region)) :","-    AllOk C ObR ObW s2 (issueOps pe s2 L region dst) ∧","-      Repr tok ptok provOf L s3' (exec s2 (issueOps pe s2 L region dst)) ∧","-      rangeBytes (exec s2 (issueOps pe s2 L region dst)) L dst = some ((List.range (L dst).len).map","-        fun i => .init (ptrBytes pe s2 L region i).1 (ptrBytes pe s2 L region i).2) := by","+    (hdec : ObW.dec s2 (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region)) :","+    AllOk C ObR ObW s2 (issueOps pe s2 L s3 i region dst) ∧","+      Repr tok ptok provOf L s3' (exec s2 (issueOps pe s2 L s3 i region dst)) ∧","+      rangeBytes (exec s2 (issueOps pe s2 L s3 i region dst)) L dst =","+        some ((List.range (L dst).len).map fun j =>","+          .init (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region j).1 (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region j).2) := by","   cases h with","   | ok har hst =>","     cases hst with"]},{"oldStart":2553,"oldLines":9,"newStart":2572,"newLines":12,"lines":["       · exact .inl hi"," "," /-- L6, `pointer_sound` for `store a p`: under the obligation of the encoding for the pointer","-written, the range of `p` holds bytes that decode to the address of the first leaf `l` of the","-region of `a` (base + offset) and that carry, each, the provenance of the allocation of `l`, which","-is live and contains the range of `l`: no address or provenance is lost or fabricated. -/","+written (`PtrEncAt`), the bytes of the pointer (`ptrBytes`) decode to the address of the first leaf","+`l` of the list of the region of `a` (base + offset), and each carries the provenance of the","+allocation of `l`, which is live and contains the range of `l`; the range of `p` receives the first","+`(L p).len` of these bytes. Whether they are enough to decode the address depends on the size of","+`p` (report, (e) 4); whether `l` holds the first byte of the region, on the layout (report,","+(e) 3). -/"," theorem pointer_sound_store {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}","     {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {tok ptok : Nat → Nat} {provOf : Nat → Option Nat} {L : Layout}","     {s3 s3' : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} {pe : PtrEnc} {a p : Nat} (hwf : WF3 s3)"]},{"oldStart":2578,"oldLines":37,"newStart":2600,"newLines":67,"lines":["   refine ⟨hpe.1, fun i => ?_, hta, hst⟩","   rw [← hprov]; exact hpe.2 i"," ","-/-- L6, `pointer_sound` for `issue`: under the obligation of the encoding for the pointer written,","-the range of the destination holds bytes that decode to the address of the first leaf `l` of the","-block and carry, each, the provenance of the allocation of `l` (the allocation of the storage of the","-arena), which is live and contains the range of `l`. -/","+/-- L6, provenance of `issue` (\"prov: allocation of arena storage\"): under `WF3`, `LayoutWF` and the","+invariant of the arenas of MM-03 (`ArenasInv`, true on the reached states), every leaf `l` of the","+block of an `ok` `issue` is in the allocation of every leaf of the storage of the arena, and","+`arenaProv` is that allocation. -/","+theorem issue_prov_storage {k : K} {L : Layout} {s3 s3' : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} {i via dst : Nat}","+    {region : List Nat} (hwf : WF3 s3) (hlw : LayoutWF L s3 s2) (hai : ArenasInv s3)","+    (h : IssueAt k i via region dst s3 (.ok s3')) {l : Nat} (hl : l ∈ region) :","+    arenaProv L s3 i = some (L l).alloc ∧ ∃ ar, s3.arenas[i]? = some ar ∧","+      ∀ l' ∈ footprint s3.P ar.storage, (L l').alloc = (L l).alloc := by","+  cases h with","+  | @ok ar _ _ har hst =>","+    cases hst with","+    | ok hstat _ _ _ =>","+      have hA := hai ar (List.mem_of_getElem? har) hstat.2.1","+      have hsl : ar.storage < s3.P.length := hA.2.2.2.2.2.1","+      obtain ⟨r, hr, hsr⟩ :=","+        exists_rootPlace hwf (ar.storage + 1) ar.storage (Nat.lt_succ_self _) hsl","+      have hlS : l ∈ footprint s3.P ar.storage := (hA.2.2.2.2.2.2.2 l).1 (hstat.2.2.1 l hl)","+      have key : ∀ l' ∈ footprint s3.P ar.storage, (L l').alloc = (L l).alloc := fun l' hl' =>","+        hlw.sameAlloc r hr.1 hr l' (footprint_sub hwf hsr hl') l (footprint_sub hwf hsr hlS)","+      refine ⟨?_, ar, har, key⟩","+      simp only [arenaProv, har, Option.map_some, key _ (headD_mem_footprint hwf hsl)]","+","+/-- L6, `pointer_sound` for `issue`: under the obligation of the encoding for the pointer written","+(`PtrEncAt`), the bytes of the pointer (`issueBytes`) decode to the address of the first leaf `l` of","+the list of the block (base + offset), and each carries the provenance of the storage of the arena","+(L6), the allocation of `l` and of every leaf of the storage, which is live and contains the range","+of `l`; the range of the destination receives the first `(L dst).len` of these bytes (report, (e) 3","+and (e) 4). -/"," theorem pointer_sound_issue {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec}","     {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec} {k : K} {tok ptok : Nat → Nat} {provOf : Nat → Option Nat}","     {L : Layout} {s3 s3' : S3} {s2 : MM02.State} {pe : PtrEnc} {i via dst : Nat}","     {region : List Nat} (hwf : WF3 s3) (hnd : NoDangling s3) (hfl : FpLeaves s3)","-    (hR : Repr tok ptok provOf L s3 s2) (h : IssueAt k i via region dst s3 (.ok s3'))","-    (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)","-    (hdec : ObW.dec s2 (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (ptrBytes pe s2 L region))","+    (hai : ArenasInv s3) (hR : Repr tok ptok provOf L s3 s2)","+    (h : IssueAt k i via region dst s3 (.ok s3')) (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)","+    (hdec : ObW.dec s2 (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region))","     {l : Nat} (hl : region.head? = some l)","-    (hpe : PtrEncAt pe (regionAddr s2 L region) (regionProv L region)) :","-    pe.decode (ptrBytes pe s2 L region) = regionAddr s2 L region ∧","-      (∀ i, (ptrBytes pe s2 L region i).2 = some (L l).alloc) ∧","+    (hpe : PtrEncAt pe (regionAddr s2 L region) (arenaProv L s3 i)) :","+    pe.decode (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region) = regionAddr s2 L region ∧","+      (∀ j, (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region j).2 = some (L l).alloc) ∧","+      (∃ ar, s3.arenas[i]? = some ar ∧","+        ∀ l' ∈ footprint s3.P ar.storage, (L l').alloc = (L l).alloc) ∧","       (∃ al, s2.allocs (L l).alloc = some al ∧ al.live = true ∧","         regionAddr s2 L region = al.base + (L l).off ∧ (L l).off + (L l).len ≤ al.size) ∧","-      rangeBytes (exec s2 (issueOps pe s2 L region dst)) L dst = some ((List.range (L dst).len).map","-        fun i => .init (ptrBytes pe s2 L region i).1 (ptrBytes pe s2 L region i).2) := by","+      rangeBytes (exec s2 (issueOps pe s2 L s3 i region dst)) L dst =","+        some ((List.range (L dst).len).map fun j =>","+          .init (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region j).1 (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region j).2) := by","   have hst := (r6_issue (C := C) (ObR := ObR) hwf hR h hstatW hdec).2.2","+  have hlm : l ∈ region :=","+    List.mem_of_getElem? (by rw [List.head?_eq_getElem?] at hl; exact hl)","+  obtain ⟨hprov, hsto⟩ := issue_prov_storage hwf hR.lwf hai h hlm","   cases h with","   | ok har hstep =>","     cases hstep with","     | ok hstat _ _ _ =>","-      have hact := hstat.2.1","-      obtain ⟨y, hy, ya⟩ := hact","+      obtain ⟨y, hy, ya⟩ := hstat.2.1","       have hrg : ∀ x ∈ region, x ∈ y.footprint := fun x hx => by","         have := hstat.2.2.1 x hx; simpa [S3.afp, hy] using this","-      obtain ⟨hprov, hta⟩ := ptr_target hwf hnd hfl hR.toReprB hy ya hrg hl","-      refine ⟨hpe.1, fun i => ?_, hta, hst⟩","-      rw [← hprov]; exact hpe.2 i","+      obtain ⟨-, hta⟩ := ptr_target hwf hnd hfl hR.toReprB hy ya hrg hl","+      refine ⟨hpe.1, fun j => ?_, hsto, hta, hst⟩","+      rw [← hprov]; exact hpe.2 j"," "," /-! ## Real `DDSound` (L7) -/"," "]},{"oldStart":3163,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3215,"newLines":7,"lines":["   | .writeShared _ ls w, _, s2 => writeOps s2 π.L w ls","   | .transfer src dst, s3, s2 => transferOps s2 π.L s3.P src dst","   | .store a p, s3, s2 => storeOps π.pe s2 π.L s3 a p","-  | .issue _ _ region dst, _, s2 => issueOps π.pe s2 π.L region dst","+  | .issue i _ region dst, s3, s2 => issueOps π.pe s2 π.L s3 i region dst","   | .alloc pr _ ls, s3, s2 =>","     allocOps π.pl (fun i => π.geom (s3.P.length + i)) (some (π.ptok pr)) s2 (rootIdx ls)","   | .enter _ ls, s3, s2 =>"]},{"oldStart":3287,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3339,"newLines":9,"lines":[" and is in `Repr` with the MM-03 state; the MM-03 state is reached, and the ghost `provOf` is empty"," beyond the places. Since every prefix of a `SimRun` is a `SimRun`, this holds at each step. The"," remaining hypotheses: `DDSound k` (L7: `ddSound_of_layout`); `stat` (K5); the obligation of the","-placement and valid alignments (K2); the compatibility of the frame tokens (K2). -/","+placement and valid alignments (K2); the compatibility of the frame tokens (K2). `SameSizeAlong`","+(L6) is not one: the outcomes and `Repr` hold without it; the copy of the bytes of a `transfer`","+holds under it (`transfer_copies`). -/"," theorem simulation {C : Nat → Nat → Prop} {ObR : MM02.ReadOblSpec} {ObW : MM02.WriteOblSpec}","     {k : K} {statics : Statics} {π : Params} (hdd : DDSound k)","     (hstatR : ∀ s ac, ObR.stat s ac) (hstatW : ∀ s ac w, ObW.stat s ac w)"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal/Ern/MM23.lean"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"30c81193-f546-44af-a41a-74e0b35f3410","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","platform":"macos"}},"sa