{"parentUuid":"f86ee9bd-f857-476d-b4e0-6e00434d1d82","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e8b5e291-8f60-4fc9-8d4e-2bfcd70fe451","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQqCWg8dCcDZD62uhH8BYF","type":"tool_result","content":"[(2668, 101), (4187, 107), (4198, 102)]\n    x10e.afp 10 = [] ∧ regionAddr n10 L (x10e.afp 10) = 0 ∧ regionProv L (x10e.afp 10) = none :=\n  ⟨.ok (by decide), .ok (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- Witness of question (e) 3 of the pass-2 report: `issue` of the region `[6, 5]` (the leaves of\n`[5, 6]`) is `ok`; the pointer has the address 112 of its first leaf 6, while the region begins at\n104, the address of 5. Under the layout `Lsw`, which swaps the two fields (K1 fixes no order of fields) and\nsatisfies `LayoutWF`, the region `[5, 6]` gives 112 while it begins at 104. -/\nexample : Step3 KS (.issue 0 5 [6, 5] 7) x9\n      (arenaSet (issueEff x9 arS [6, 5] 7).1 0 (issueEff x9 arS [6, 5] 7).2) ∧\n    regionAddr n9 L [6, 5] = 112 ∧ leafAddr n9 L 5 = 104 ∧ leafAddr n9 L 6 = 112 :=\n  ⟨.ok (ar := arS) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)),\n    by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\ndef Lsw : Layout := fun q => if q = 5 then ⟨4, 8, 8⟩ else if q = 6 then ⟨4, 0, 8⟩ else L q\nexample : LayoutWF Lsw x9 n9 ∧ regionAddr n9 Lsw [5, 6] = 112 ∧ leafAddr n9 Lsw 6 = 104 := by\n  decide\n\n/-- Witness of question (e) 4 of the pass-2 report: under the layout `L0`, where the leaf 8 has size 0\n(K1 (d)), `ReprB` holds before `store 5 8`, the pointer written decodes to 8 as before, and the\nrange of 8 receives no byte of it, while MM-03 makes 8 `Init` and lets it hold the authority 5. -/\ndef L0 : Layout := fun q => if q = 8 then ⟨6, 0, 0⟩ else L q\nexample : ReprB π.tok π.ptok pvA L0 x10 n10 ∧ pe.decode (ptrBytes pe n10 L0 (x10.afp 5)) = 8 ∧\n    rangeBytes (exec n10 (storeOps pe n10 L0 x10 5 8)) L0 8 = some [] ∧ x11.I 8 = .init ∧\n    (x11.A[5]?).map (·.holder) = some (.place 8) := by\n  decide","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4b573f36-684f-4bb6-a523-6744c89d3dfc","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:03:08.218Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"[(2668, 101), (4187, 107), (4198, 102)]\n    x10e.afp 10 = [] ∧ regionAddr n10 L (x10e.afp 10) = 0 ∧ regionProv L (x10e.afp 10) = none :=\n  ⟨.ok (by decide), .ok (by decide), by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- Witness of question (e) 3 of the pass-2 report: `issue` of the region `[6, 5]` (the leaves of\n`[5, 6]`) is `ok`; the pointer has the address 112 of its first leaf 6, while the region begins at\n104, the address of 5. Under the layout `Lsw`, which swaps the two fields (K1 fixes no order of fields) and\nsatisfies `LayoutWF`, the region `[5, 6]` gives 112 while it begins at 104. -/\nexample : Step3 KS (.issue 0 5 [6, 5] 7) x9\n      (arenaSet (issueEff x9 arS [6, 5] 7).1 0 (issueEff x9 arS [6, 5] 7).2) ∧\n    regionAddr n9 L [6, 5] = 112 ∧ leafAddr n9 L 5 = 104 ∧ leafAddr n9 L 6 = 112 :=\n  ⟨.ok (ar := arS) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)),\n    by decide, by decide, by decide⟩\ndef Lsw : Layout := fun q => if q = 5 then ⟨4, 8, 8⟩ else if q = 6 then ⟨4, 0, 8⟩ else L q\nexample : LayoutWF Lsw x9 n9 ∧ regionAddr n9 Lsw [5, 6] = 112 ∧ leafAddr n9 Lsw 6 = 104 := by\n  decide\n\n/-- Witness of question (e) 4 of the pass-2 report: under the layout `L0`, where the leaf 8 has size 0\n(K1 (d)), `ReprB` holds before `store 5 8`, the pointer written decodes to 8 as before, and the\nrange of 8 receives no byte of it, while MM-03 makes 8 `Init` and lets it hold the authority 5. -/\ndef L0 : Layout := fun q => if q = 8 then ⟨6, 0, 0⟩ else L q\nexample : ReprB π.tok π.ptok pvA L0 x10 n10 ∧ pe.decode (ptrBytes pe n10 L0 (x10.afp 5)) = 8 ∧\n    rangeBytes (exec n10 (storeOps pe n10 L0 x10 5 8)) L0 8 = some [] ∧ x11.I 8 = .init ∧\n    (x11.A[5]?).map (·.holder) = some (.place 8) := by\n  decide","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Use