essages.2.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HrJwrvQtyzkwEeYDgiyqmL":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/w9ztvw6fy.output'\ndata=json.load(open(p))['result']\nfor r in data:\n    v={x['id']:x for x in (r.get('verdicts') or [])}\n    print(\"=== LENS\", r['lens'], \"findings:\", len(r['review']['findings']))\n    for f in r['review']['findings']:\n        vv=v.get(f['id'])\n        print(f\"--- {f['id']} [{f['severity']}] verdict: {None if not vv else (vv['real'], vv['severity'])}\")\n        print(\"LOC:\", f['location'])\n        print(\"CLAIM:\", f['claim'])\n        if vv: print(\"VERIFIER:\", vv['reason'][:1200])\n        print()\n    if r['lens']!='FIX': print(\"CHECKED:\", r['review']['checked'][:2500]); print()\nEOF","description":"Extract second-check findings and verdicts"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1f295837-8620-4966-80d2-737f179e2223","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgbAwd5w5Q1DCm8e17Try","requestRef":"c35fd5ee-ef99-4e57-9cd9-6862137d47b4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d714e4e0-e321-4dd1-93aa-420f18a41baa","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:20:31.648Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"d714e4e0-e321-4dd1-93aa-420f18a41baa","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b5f18ae9-8acf-40c8-8b34-6556a60953e8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HrJwrvQtyzkwEeYDgiyqmL","type":"tool_result","content":"=== LENS FIX findings: 2\n--- FIX-1 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2543-2546 (docstring of r6_issue)\nCLAIM: fe0bd8c changed the statement of r6_issue from `ptrBytes` to `issueBytes` but did not update its docstring. The docstring still says the write is \"with `ptrBytes` of the block\". `ptrBytes pe s2 L region` carries provenance `regionProv L region`, while the statement writes `issueBytes`, whose provenance is `arenaProv`. The two differ on an `ok` issue: for the empty block, `ptrBytes` has no provenance and `issueBytes` has the storage allocation. So the docstring names bytes that the theorem does not write.\nVERIFIER: fe0bd8c changed r6_issue from `ptrBytes` to `issueBytes` (the report says so: \"`r6_issue` est inchangé hors du passage de `ptrBytes` à `issueBytes`\"). The docstring at formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2543-2544 was not updated and still names the Lean definition `ptrBytes`. `ptrBytes` takes provenance `regionProv L region`; the statement writes `issueBytes`, which takes `arenaProv L s3 i`. The brief's L6 text does say \"WriteStep of ptrBytes of the block on dst range (prov: allocation of arena storage)\", but the docstring leaves out the provenance qualifier, and that qualifier is exactly what the fix changed. The two byte functions differ on an `ok` issue of the empty block. The docstrings of issueOps and issueBytes are correct. Only the r6_issue docstring is stale, so this is documentation only and minor.\n\n--- FIX-2 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2456-2459 (docstring of regionAddr, added in fe0bd8c)\nCLAIM: The new sentence \"It is the first byte of the region when that leaf has the lowest offset\" is false when that leaf has size zero, which K1 (d) allows. The head leaf can have the lowest offset and an empty range. `regionAddr` then names an address that is no byte of the region, and the first byte of the region is higher. The report's question (e) 3 leaves this case open (\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\"), but the docstring states it as settled.\nVERIFIER: The sentence added to regionAddr in fe0bd8c, \"It is the first byte of the region when that leaf has the lowest offset\", states as settled a case that report (e) 3 leaves open (\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\"). The statement is false when the head leaf has the lowest offset but size zero, which K1 (d) allows and the module's LayoutWF accepts. A size-zero leaf contributes no byte, so regionAddr names an address that is no byte of the region, and the region's first byte is higher. The definition itself does what L6 says (\"base + off of first leaf\"). Only the docstring claim is wrong, so this is minor.\n\n=== LENS FACTS findings: 6\n--- FACTS-1 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:32-34 (Résultats principaux, item 2); formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2589-2590, 2601, 2641-2642, 2663\nCLAIM: Main result 2 says `pointer_sound_store` and `pointer_sound_issue` \"montrent que le pointeur écrit se décode en l'adresse de la première feuille de la région\" and does not mention `PtrEncAt`. The decode conjunct is not proved: it restates the hypothesis `hpe : PtrEncAt …`. The proofs close it with `hpe.1`, and `regionAddr` is base + off of the head leaf by definition. What the theorems do prove is that the head leaf's allocation exists and is live, plus the base + off form and the provenance identity. Sections (b) and (c) 10 do say \"sous PtrEncAt\". The main-results summary presents an assumption as a result.\nVERIFIER: Main result 2 of the report says `pointer_sound_store` and `pointer_sound_issue` \"montrent que le pointeur écrit se décode en l'adresse de la première feuille\" and does not name `PtrEncAt`. The decode conjunct is the hypothesis hpe.1 restated. Taking decode as a hypothesis is what the brief asks (L6: \"obligation decode (ptrBytes x) = address…\"), so the Lean is fine. The defect is only the summary wording. Sections (b) and (c) 10 do say \"sous PtrEncAt\", so the impact is small.\n\n--- FACTS-2 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:320 (table (f), alignment row) vs formal/Ern/MM23.lean:3349\nCLAIM: Table (f) gives the alignment hypothesis of `simulation` as \"alignements valides, `0 < align` et `Pow2 align`, pour chaque racine\". The statement actually requires valid alignment for every natural index `r`, including indices that are not root places of the run and are never read by `assoc` or `initOpsOf`. The hypothesis is stronger than the table says, so the theorem is weaker than reported. The (f) task is to check the table against the actual statement.\nVERIFIER: Table (f) says the alignment hypothesis applies \"pour chaque racine\". The statement quantifies over every natural r. Per the Params docstring, π.geom is only meaningful at root-place indices, and `assoc` reads it only at `s3.P.length + i` for roots i. So the hypothesis is stronger than the table states. The practical impact is nil: geom at unread indices can be set to a valid alignment without changing anything. Still, the table does not match the statement.\n\n--- FACTS-3 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:392-396 (\"Énoncés de la passe 2 changés par les corrections\")\nCLAIM: The list of pass-2 statements changed by the review-fix commit fe0bd8c names `issueOps`/`assoc`, `r6_issue` and `pointer_sound_issue`. It leaves out the theorem `CaseSim.inv`, whose conclusion gained `ArenasInv s3` in that commit.\nVERIFIER: The list \"Énoncés de la passe 2 changés par les corrections\" leaves out `CaseSim.inv`, whose conclusion gained `ArenasInv s3` in fe0bd8c. The change strengthens a witness helper, so no weakening is hidden. The list is still incomplete.\n\n--- FACTS-4 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:226-233 ((c) 15, \"Énoncés de la passe 1 modifiés\")\nCLAIM: (c) 15 lists the changed pass-1 statements as repr_init, r6_enter, r6_alloc, r6_free and Repr.change/shrink. The review summary cites it as the account of every allowed change (\"Aucun affaiblissement hors de ce que L3 et L4 imposent ((c) 15)\"). The list omits `repr_extend`, which gained the hypothesis `hprov` and moved from `Repr` to `ReprB`. It also omits `repr_writes`, `repr_of_nil`, `covered_live` and `repr_deallocs`, whose statements moved from `Repr` to `ReprB`.\nVERIFIER: (c) 15 lists the modified pass-1 statements and leaves some out. It omits `repr_extend`, which gained the hypothesis `hprov` and moved Repr→ReprB. It also omits `repr_writes`, `repr_of_nil`, `covered_live` and `repr_deallocs`, which moved Repr→ReprB in both hypothesis and conclusion. All of these follow L3 and L4, like the listed ones, so the claim \"aucun affaiblissement hors de L3/L4\" still holds. The list is incomplete, and the added hypothesis of repr_extend is undisclosed.\n\n--- FACTS-5 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:370-371 (Revue adverse, L7-1)\nCLAIM: The report summarizes L7-1 as \"confirmé, ramené à mineur : déjà signalé, mais la conséquence pour simulation manquait\". The verifier's verdict in the journal says the opposite about simulation: the draft's simulation-hypothesis table already linked DDSound to the non-empty-range condition and to (e) 1. The verifier names a different contribution: `inst_iff`, showing that hpos is exactly necessary, and the fact that ddSound_instance cannot hold together with LayoutWF on a state with a zero-size allocation. The report mentions neither.\nVERIFIER: The report says the simulation consequence of L7-1 was missing. The review record says otherwise. Both the L7 reviewer and the verifier state that the draft (f) table already tied DDSound to the non-empty-range condition and to (e) 1. The verifier named inst_iff as the finding's contribution, and the report never mentions it. The fix did make the table say explicitly \"non déchargée par L7 …\", so the misstatement is mild. It concerns the account of the review, not the formalization.\n\n--- FACTS-6 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:14-16 (État de vérification)\nCLAIM: \"Un script Lean parcourt les 333 constantes de type théorème du module\" understates the module's theorem constants. Ern.MM23 has 487 theorem constants. 333 is the count after excluding the 154 internal names (`_proof_N`, `_simp_…`), which matches the implementer's `!n.isInternal` filter. The axiom conclusion is not affected: all 487 stay within {propext, Quot.sound}.\nVERIFIER: \"les 333 constantes de type théorème du module\" is inaccurate. The module has 487 theorem constants, and 333 is the count of non-internal ones. The axiom conclusion holds for all 487, so only the stated count is wrong.\n\nCHECKED: I checked every factual claim of formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md at fe0bd8c without modifying the repo. Scratch files are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/facts/.\n\n**Counts and build.**\n- `grep -cE '^theorem '` gives 178 and `grep -c '^example'` gives 95, as the report says.\n- Count2.lean finds 487 theorem constants in Ern.MM23, 333 of them non-internal, and none outside {propext, Quot.sound} (FACTS-6).\n- ExAx.lean is a copy of fe0bd8c's MM23.lean with the 95 examples renamed to theorems in namespace Ern.MM23X. It compiles with no error or warning, and all 95 `#print axioms` lines give [propext, Quot.sound] (ExAx.out).\n- `lake env lean Ern/MM23.lean` prints nothing. The forbidden-word grep is empty, there is no `noncomputable`, and the working tree is clean.\n- `git diff 4e7cdbc fe0bd8c -- MM02.lean MM03.lean` is empty.\n\n**Commits.** Each of the six step commits touches only MM23.lean and has the subject the report gives. Theorem counts per commit: 97 at cd079be, 105, 130, 134, 142, 151, 177 at 579808d, 178 at fe0bd8c. `PtrEncOK` appears at cf09f12..10b837c only in its definition, and is replaced by `PtrEncAt` at 579808d. `arenaProv` and `issue_prov_storage` first appear at fe0bd8c.\n\n**Declarations.** Every declaration named in (a), (b) and (f) resolves (Names.lean). The hypotheses in the R6 table of (b) match the signatures of r6_read3, r6_alloc, r6_alloc_fail, r6_free, r6_enter, r6_exit, r6_transfer, r6_store, r6_issue and r6_noStep. R1, R2, R4, exclusive_bytes and the *_reachable variants are identical to pass 1 once Repr is renamed. The (c) 15 changes are confirmed for repr_init, r6_enter, r6_alloc and r6_free, but the list is incomplete (FACTS-4). FreeSound and exitOps are unchanged. The ReprB fields match (c) 1. Params, provStep and assoc match (c) 3 and (c) 14. r6_enter applies to CaseOwnedLocal (Owned.lean).\n\n**Witnesses.**\n- CaseSim has 18 steps, x1..x18, in the order the report lists.\n- `n18.next = 7` (Facts.lean), together with the module example `∀ i < 7, DeadAlloc n18 i`, supports \"les sept allocations sont mortes\".\n- In n9 the base of allocation 4 is 104, and `leafAddr n10 L 0 = 8`.\n- Leaf 1 is pinned at x11.\n- resetEff returns the same S3, so reset changes only `arenas`.\n- The (e) 2, 3 and 4 witnesses (x10e, [6,5], Lsw, L0) state what the report says.\n- `¬ReprB` with a wrong provider token holds in Cases.\n\n**(e) numbering.** Every \"pass-2 report, (e) N\" citati\n\n=== LENS COMPL findings: 3\n--- COMPL-1 [minor] verdict: (False, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:50 and :156 (section (a) row L1 and (c) 4); formal/Ern/MM23.lean (no declaration)\nCLAIM: Missing coverage: the third clause of L1, 'K.Deallocable false on statics', has no definition and no theorem. The report says so itself. In `simulation` the clause is only enforced indirectly: `FreeOblig` fails for a static because the ghost is `none` there. MM-03 itself allows a free of a static whenever K makes it Deallocable, so the clause is a real constraint and does not follow from MM-03.\nVERIFIER: The facts are accurate, but they show no defect. No declaration states L1's third clause, and the report says so in (a) and (c) 4. The clause only narrows the set of K. `simulation` and `r6_free` are proved for every K, so they hold in particular for every K with Deallocable false on statics. Leaving the clause out makes the theorems stronger, not weaker. Adding it would be an unneeded hypothesis. The checker's own Lean file also confirms the report's (c) 4 rather than contradicting it. Its K, KT [] [] [] [1] [(1,7)], violates L4, not only L1: L4 sets `FreeCompat p auth` to `Compatible auth (ptok (provOf p))`, and that is false for a static because a static has no provider. In a SimRun the ghost is `fun _ => none` at init, and `provStep` only sets indices from s3.P.length upward. So the run is excluded by the brief's own L4, which `FreeOblig` encodes. An ok free of a static needs `k.FreeCompat p auth`, so in a SimRun such a free also contradicts L4. The domain L1 intends is fully covered.\n\n--- COMPL-2 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:315-327 (section (f) table)\nCLAIM: Deliverable (f) asks for each hypothesis to be classed spec 4 / spec 11 / bibliothèque / ouverte. Three rows of the table use none of these classes: `ShapeOK` des statiques ('aucune'), the L1 envelope and the L2 envelope ('hors langage'). Separately, the `hg` row describes the alignment hypothesis as 'pour chaque racine', but `simulation` quantifies it over every index r. This is harmless, because only root indices are read, but the row does not describe the statement exactly.\nVERIFIER: Deliverable (f) asks for each simulation hypothesis to be classed spec 4 / spec 11 / bibliothèque / ouverte. Three rows of the report use labels outside these four: 'aucune' for ShapeOK, and 'hors langage' for the L1 and L2 envelopes. Section (e) asks no question about this. The `hg` row also describes the hypothesis as holding 'pour chaque racine', but the statement quantifies over every index r. Only root indices are read: repr_init, r6_enter and r6_alloc call hg at root indices. So this is harmless, but the table describes the hypothesis less strictly than it is stated. Both points concern the deliverable's form only; no theorem is affected.\n\n--- COMPL-3 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:226-233 ((c) 15); formal/Ern/MM23.lean:684-697 (repr_extend)\nCLAIM: (c) 15 lists the pass-1 statements changed under L3/L4 and reads as exhaustive, but it omits `repr_extend`. That pass-1 theorem gained a new hypothesis `hprov`, and its `hR`/conclusion changed from `Repr` to `ReprB`. The report never mentions `repr_extend`.\nVERIFIER: `repr_extend` is a public theorem from pass 1. Its statement changed beyond the switch to `Repr tok ptok provOf L` that report l.75 describes: it gained the hypothesis `hprov`, and its hR and conclusion moved from `Repr` to `ReprB`. Section (c) 15, 'Énoncés de la passe 1 modifiés', lists the other changed statements but leaves this one out. The change itself is allowed by L3 and L4: `hprov` is needed for the clause `provTokens` that the new conclusion adds, so this is not a weakening. The defect is only that the report's disclosure of changed statements is incomplete.\n\nCHECKED: Each part of the brief at task_mm23_p2.md, with the declarations that formalize it:\n- L1: NoOwner in Step3 (envelope). repr_init places no restriction on statics owned by statics; checked non-vacuous with review2/completeness/statics_owned.lean, where SimRun.init and ReprB hold by decide for a static owned by a static (no output). The 'Deallocable false on statics' clause has no declaration (COMPL-1).\n- L2: `∃ i, rootIdx ls = [i]` in Step3; hone in r6_alloc.\n- L3: Repr extends ReprB with wf2. Repr does not take k. The init clause concerns Init leaves only.\n- L4: ReprB.provTokens, provStep, FreeCompatInst (`∃ pr, provOf p = some pr ∧ C auth (ptok pr)`), FreeOblig. freeSound_derived is proved from ReprB, and r6_free uses it.\n- L5: deallocOps [rootAlloc ..] in r6_free; the leaked clause; exitOps and r6_exit.\n- L6: transferPairs, copyOps, bytesOf, SameSizeAlong, r6_transfer, transfer_copies; PtrEnc, PtrEncAt, regionAddr, regionProv, ptrBytes, storeOps, r6_store, pointer_sound_store; arenaProv, issueBytes, issueOps, r6_issue, issue_prov_storage, pointer_sound_issue; NoStep.reset.\n- L7: ByteDisjoint, ddSound_of_layout (extra hpos hypothesis, disclosed), ddSound_instance, ddSound_of_layout_needs_size, byteDisjoint_of_leaves.\n- L8: leafAddr and pinned_address_stable. Its docstring states that MM-02 models no physical move and covers static and dynamic pins.\n- Step 5: Op3 covers all 19 Reachable constructors. Step3, Exec3, Params, assoc, Trans, SimRun, Oblig, simulation.\n- Step 6: CaseSim has an 18-step run covering alloc, newArena, issue, store, transfer to caller, free and exit, plus per-op examples for issue, store, transfer and reset, and counterexamples L0, Lsw and x10e. The pass-1 case counts are kept: CaseInit 7/7, Cases 54/56, CaseOwnedLocal 9/9, DraftGaps 3/3.\n- One commit per step (git log cd079be..fe0bd8c).\n\nDeliverable:\n- (a): all of L1-L8 and steps 5-6 are present.\n- (b): R1, R2, R4 and R6 for every operation, plus ddSound_of_layout, pinned_address_stable, freeSound_derived and simulation. The hypotheses in the R6 table match the signatures. A statement diff confirms that R1, R2 and R4 changed only in their Repr signature.\n- (c), (d), (e) are present.\n- (f): every explicit argument of simulation, every SimRun premise and both Step3 envelope conditions are listed. Class problems are in COMPL-2.\n\nDocstrings: every pass-2 rule-encoding declaration cites its clause or arbitrage. Only helper lemmas have no docstring: Exec3.reachable, ReprB.provOf_congr, dec","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"98dc4eb7-406e-4a5b-bc30-d6759f1e50b0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:20:32.416Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== LENS FIX findings: 2\n--- FIX-1 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2543-2546 (docstring of r6_issue)\nCLAIM: fe0bd8c changed the statement of r6_issue from `ptrBytes` to `issueBytes` but did not update its docstring. The docstring still says the write is \"with `ptrBytes` of the block\". `ptrBytes pe s2 L region` carries provenance `regionProv L region`, while the statement writes `issueBytes`, whose provenance is `arenaProv`. The two differ on an `ok` issue: for the empty block, `ptrBytes` has no provenance and `issueBytes` has the storage allocation. So the docstring names bytes that the theorem does not write.\nVERIFIER: fe0bd8c changed r6_issue from `ptrBytes` to `issueBytes` (the report says so: \"`r6_issue` est inchangé hors du passage de `ptrBytes` à `issueBytes`\"). The docstring at formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2543-2544 was not updated and still names the Lean definition `ptrBytes`. `ptrBytes` takes provenance `regionProv L region`; the statement writes `issueBytes`, which takes `arenaProv L s3 i`. The brief's L6 text does say \"WriteStep of ptrBytes of the block on dst range (prov: allocation of arena storage)\", but the docstring leaves out the provenance qualifier, and that qualifier is exactly what the fix changed. The two byte functions differ on an `ok` issue of the empty block. The docstrings of issueOps and issueBytes are correct. Only the r6_issue docstring is stale, so this is documentation only and minor.\n\n--- FIX-2 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2456-2459 (docstring of regionAddr, added in fe0bd8c)\nCLAIM: The new sentence \"It is the first byte of the region when that leaf has the lowest offset\" is false when that leaf has size zero, which K1 (d) allows. The head leaf can have the lowest offset and an empty range. `regionAddr` then names an address that is no byte of the region, and the first byte of the region is higher. The report's question (e) 3 leaves this case open (\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\"), but the docstring states it as settled.\nVERIFIER: The sentence added to regionAddr in fe0bd8c, \"It is the first byte of the region when that leaf has the lowest offset\", states as settled a case that report (e) 3 leaves open (\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\"). The statement is false when the head leaf has the lowest offset but size zero, which K1 (d) allows and the module's LayoutWF accepts. A size-zero leaf contributes no byte, so regionAddr names an address that is no byte of the region, and the region's first byte is higher. The definition itself does what L6 says (\"base + off of first leaf\"). Only the docstring claim is wrong, so this is minor.\n\n=== LENS FACTS findings: 6\n--- FACTS-1 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:32-34 (Résultats principaux, item 2); formal/Ern/MM23.lean:2589-2590, 2601, 2641-2642, 2663\nCLAIM: Main result 2 says `pointer_sound_store` and `pointer_sound_issue` \"montrent que le pointeur écrit se décode en l'adresse de la première feuille de la région\" and does not mention `PtrEncAt`. The decode conjunct is not proved: it restates the hypothesis `hpe : PtrEncAt …`. The proofs close it with `hpe.1`, and `regionAddr` is base + off of the head leaf by definition. What the theorems do prove is that the head leaf's allocation exists and is live, plus the base + off form and the provenance identity. Sections (b) and (c) 10 do say \"sous PtrEncAt\". The main-results summary presents an assumption as a result.\nVERIFIER: Main result 2 of the report says `pointer_sound_store` and `pointer_sound_issue` \"montrent que le pointeur écrit se décode en l'adresse de la première feuille\" and does not name `PtrEncAt`. The decode conjunct is the hypothesis hpe.1 restated. Taking decode as a hypothesis is what the brief asks (L6: \"obligation decode (ptrBytes x) = address…\"), so the Lean is fine. The defect is only the summary wording. Sections (b) and (c) 10 do say \"sous PtrEncAt\", so the impact is small.\n\n--- FACTS-2 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:320 (table (f), alignment row) vs formal/Ern/MM23.lean:3349\nCLAIM: Table (f) gives the alignment hypothesis of `simulation` as \"alignements valides, `0 < align` et `Pow2 align`, pour chaque racine\". The statement actually requires valid alignment for every natural index `r`, including indices that are not root places of the run and are never read by `assoc` or `initOpsOf`. The hypothesis is stronger than the table says, so the theorem is weaker than reported. The (f) task is to check the table against the actual statement.\nVERIFIER: Table (f) says the alignment hypothesis applies \"pour chaque racine\". The statement quantifies over every natural r. Per the Params docstring, π.geom is only meaningful at root-place indices, and `assoc` reads it only at `s3.P.length + i` for roots i. So the hypothesis is stronger than the table states. The practical impact is nil: geom at unread indices can be set to a valid alignment without changing anything. Still, the table does not match the statement.\n\n--- FACTS-3 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:392-396 (\"Énoncés de la passe 2 changés par les corrections\")\nCLAIM: The list of pass-2 statements changed by the review-fix commit fe0bd8c names `issueOps`/`assoc`, `r6_issue` and `pointer_sound_issue`. It leaves out the theorem `CaseSim.inv`, whose conclusion gained `ArenasInv s3` in that commit.\nVERIFIER: The list \"Énoncés de la passe 2 changés par les corrections\" leaves out `CaseSim.inv`, whose conclusion gained `ArenasInv s3` in fe0bd8c. The change strengthens a witness helper, so no weakening is hidden. The list is still incomplete.\n\n--- FACTS-4 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:226-233 ((c) 15, \"Énoncés de la passe 1 modifiés\")\nCLAIM: (c) 15 lists the changed pass-1 statements as repr_init, r6_enter, r6_alloc, r6_free and Repr.change/shrink. The review summary cites it as the account of every allowed change (\"Aucun affaiblissement hors de ce que L3 et L4 imposent ((c) 15)\"). The list omits `repr_extend`, which gained the hypothesis `hprov` and moved from `Repr` to `ReprB`. It also omits `repr_writes`, `repr_of_nil`, `covered_live` and `repr_deallocs`, whose statements moved from `Repr` to `ReprB`.\nVERIFIER: (c) 15 lists the modified pass-1 statements and leaves some out. It omits `repr_extend`, which gained the hypothesis `hprov` and moved Repr→ReprB. It also omits `repr_writes`, `repr_of_nil`, `covered_live` and `repr_deallocs`, which moved Repr→ReprB in both hypothesis and conclusion. All of these follow L3 and L4, like the listed ones, so the claim \"aucun affaiblissement hors de L3/L4\" still holds. The list is incomplete, and the added hypothesis of repr_extend is undisclosed.\n\n--- FACTS-5 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:370-371 (Revue adverse, L7-1)\nCLAIM: The report summarizes L7-1 as \"confirmé, ramené à mineur : déjà signalé, mais la conséquence pour simulation manquait\". The verifier's verdict in the journal says the opposite about simulation: the draft's simulation-hypothesis table already linked DDSound to the non-empty-range condition and to (e) 1. The verifier names a different contribution: `inst_iff`, showing that hpos is exactly necessary, and the fact that ddSound_instance cannot hold together with LayoutWF on a state with a zero-size allocation. The report mentions neither.\nVERIFIER: The report says the simulation consequence of L7-1 was missing. The review record says otherwise. Both the L7 reviewer and the verifier state that the draft (f) table already tied DDSound to the non-empty-range condition and to (e) 1. The verifier named inst_iff as the finding's contribution, and the report never mentions it. The fix did make the table say explicitly \"non déchargée par L7 …\", so the misstatement is mild. It concerns the account of the review, not the formalization.\n\n--- FACTS-6 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:14-16 (État de vérification)\nCLAIM: \"Un script Lean parcourt les 333 constantes de type théorème du module\" understates the module's theorem constants. Ern.MM23 has 487 theorem constants. 333 is the count after excluding the 154 internal names (`_proof_N`, `_simp_…`), which matches the implementer's `!n.isInternal` filter. The axiom conclusion is not affected: all 487 stay within {propext, Quot.sound}.\nVERIFIER: \"les 333 constantes de type théorème du module\" is inaccurate. The module has 487 theorem constants, and 333 is the count of non-internal ones. The axiom conclusion holds for all 487, so only the stated count is wrong.\n\nCHECKED: I checked every factual claim of formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md at fe0bd8c without modifying the repo. Scratch files are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review2/facts/.\n\n**Counts and build.**\n- `grep -cE '^theorem '` gives 178 and `grep -c '^example'` gives 95, as the report says.\n- Count2.lean finds 487 theorem constants in Ern.MM23, 333 of them non-internal, and none outside {propext, Quot.sound} (FACTS-6).\n- ExAx.lean is a copy of fe0bd8c's MM23.lean with the 95 examples renamed to theorems in namespace Ern.MM23X. It compiles with no error or warning, and all 95 `#print axioms` lines give [propext, Quot.sound] (ExAx.out).\n- `lake env lean Ern/MM23.lean` prints nothing. The forbidden-word grep is empty, there is no `noncomputable`, and the working tree is clean.\n- `git diff 4e7cdbc fe0bd8c -- MM02.lean MM03.lean` is empty.\n\n**Commits.** Each of the six step commits touches only MM23.lean and has the subject the report gives. Theorem counts per commit: 97 at cd079be, 105, 130, 134, 142, 151, 177 at 579808d, 178 at fe0bd8c. `PtrEncOK` appears at cf09f12..10b837c only in its definition, and is replaced by `PtrEncAt` at 579808d. `arenaProv` and `issue_prov_storage` first appear at fe0bd8c.\n\n**Declarations.** Every declaration named in (a), (b) and (f) resolves (Names.lean). The hypotheses in the R6 table of (b) match the signatures of r6_read3, r6_alloc, r6_alloc_fail, r6_free, r6_enter, r6_exit, r6_transfer, r6_store, r6_issue and r6_noStep. R1, R2, R4, exclusive_bytes and the *_reachable variants are identical to pass 1 once Repr is renamed. The (c) 15 changes are confirmed for repr_init, r6_enter, r6_alloc and r6_free, but the list is incomplete (FACTS-4). FreeSound and exitOps are unchanged. The ReprB fields match (c) 1. Params, provStep and assoc match (c) 3 and (c) 14. r6_enter applies to CaseOwnedLocal (Owned.lean).\n\n**Witnesses.**\n- CaseSim has 18 steps, x1..x18, in the order the report lists.\n- `n18.next = 7` (Facts.lean), together with the module example `∀ i < 7, DeadAlloc n18 i`, supports \"les sept allocations sont mortes\".\n- In n9 the base of allocation 4 is 104, and `leafAddr n10 L 0 = 8`.\n- Leaf 1 is pinned at x11.\n- resetEff returns the same S3, so reset changes only `arenas`.\n- The (e) 2, 3 and 4 witnesses (x10e, [6,5], Lsw, L0) state what the report says.\n- `¬ReprB` with a wrong provider token holds in Cases.\n\n**(e) numbering.** Every \"pass-2 report, (e) N\" citati\n\n=== LENS COMPL findings: 3\n--- COMPL-1 [minor] verdict: (False, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:50 and :156 (section (a) row L1 and (c) 4); formal/Ern/MM23.lean (no declaration)\nCLAIM: Missing coverage: the third clause of L1, 'K.Deallocable false on statics', has no definition and no theorem. The report says so itself. In `simulation` the clause is only enforced indirectly: `FreeOblig` fails for a static because the ghost is `none` there. MM-03 itself allows a free of a static whenever K makes it Deallocable, so the clause is a real constraint and does not follow from MM-03.\nVERIFIER: The facts are accurate, but they show no defect. No declaration states L1's third clause, and the report says so in (a) and (c) 4. The clause only narrows the set of K. `simulation` and `r6_free` are proved for every K, so they hold in particular for every K with Deallocable false on statics. Leaving the clause out makes the theorems stronger, not weaker. Adding it would be an unneeded hypothesis. The checker's own Lean file also confirms the report's (c) 4 rather than contradicting it. Its K, KT [] [] [] [1] [(1,7)], violates L4, not only L1: L4 sets `FreeCompat p auth` to `Compatible auth (ptok (provOf p))`, and that is false for a static because a static has no provider. In a SimRun the ghost is `fun _ => none` at init, and `provStep` only sets indices from s3.P.length upward. So the run is excluded by the brief's own L4, which `FreeOblig` encodes. An ok free of a static needs `k.FreeCompat p auth`, so in a SimRun such a free also contradicts L4. The domain L1 intends is fully covered.\n\n--- COMPL-2 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:315-327 (section (f) table)\nCLAIM: Deliverable (f) asks for each hypothesis to be classed spec 4 / spec 11 / bibliothèque / ouverte. Three rows of the table use none of these classes: `ShapeOK` des statiques ('aucune'), the L1 envelope and the L2 envelope ('hors langage'). Separately, the `hg` row describes the alignment hypothesis as 'pour chaque racine', but `simulation` quantifies it over every index r. This is harmless, because only root indices are read, but the row does not describe the statement exactly.\nVERIFIER: Deliverable (f) asks for each simulation hypothesis to be classed spec 4 / spec 11 / bibliothèque / ouverte. Three rows of the report use labels outside these four: 'aucune' for ShapeOK, and 'hors langage' for the L1 and L2 envelopes. Section (e) asks no question about this. The `hg` row also describes the hypothesis as holding 'pour chaque racine', but the statement quantifies over every index r. Only root indices are read: repr_init, r6_enter and r6_alloc call hg at root indices. So this is harmless, but the table describes the hypothesis less strictly than it is stated. Both points concern the deliverable's form only; no theorem is affected.\n\n--- COMPL-3 [minor] verdict: (True, 'minor')\nLOC: formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:226-233 ((c) 15); formal/Ern/MM23.lean:684-697 (repr_extend)\nCLAIM: (c) 15 lists the pass-1 statements changed under L3/L4 and reads as exhaustive, but it omits `repr_extend`. That pass-1 theorem gained a new hypothesis `hprov`, and its `hR`/conclusion changed from `Repr` to `ReprB`. The report never mentions `repr_extend`.\nVERIFIER: `repr_extend` is a public theorem from pass 1. Its statement changed beyond the switch to `Repr tok ptok provOf L` that report l.75 describes: it gained the hypothesis `hprov`, and its hR and conclusion moved from `Repr` to `ReprB`. Section (c) 15, 'Énoncés de la passe 1 modifiés', lists the other changed statements but leaves this one out. The change itself is allowed by L3 and L4: `hprov` is needed for the clause `provTokens` that the new conclusion adds, so this is not a weakening. The defect is only that the report's disclosure of changed statements is incomplete.\n\nCHECKED: Each part of the brief at task_mm23_p2.md, with the declarations that formalize it:\n- L1: NoOwner in Step3 (envelope). repr_init places no restriction on statics owned by statics; checked non-vacuous with review2/completeness/statics_owned.lean, where SimRun.init and ReprB hold by decide for a static owned by a static (no output). The 'Deallocable false on statics' clause has no declaration (COMPL-1).\n- L2: `∃ i, rootIdx ls = [i]` in Step3; hone in r6_alloc.\n- L3: Repr extends ReprB with wf2. Repr does not take k. The init clause concerns Init leaves only.\n- L4: ReprB.provTokens, provStep, FreeCompatInst (`∃ pr, provOf p = some pr ∧ C auth (ptok pr)`), FreeOblig. freeSound_derived is proved from ReprB, and r6_free uses it.\n- L5: deallocOps [rootAlloc ..] in r6_free; the leaked clause; exitOps and r6_exit.\n- L6: transferPairs, copyOps, bytesOf, SameSizeAlong, r6_transfer, transfer_copies; PtrEnc, PtrEncAt, regionAddr, regionProv, ptrBytes, storeOps, r6_store, pointer_sound_store; arenaProv, issueBytes, issueOps, r6_issue, issue_prov_storage, pointer_sound_issue; NoStep.reset.\n- L7: ByteDisjoint, ddSound_of_layout (extra hpos hypothesis, disclosed), ddSound_instance, ddSound_of_layout_needs_size, byteDisjoint_of_leaves.\n- L8: leafAddr and pinned_address_stable. Its docstring states that MM-02 models no physical move and covers static and dynamic pins.\n- Step 5: Op3 covers all 19 Reachable constructors. Step3, Exec3, Params, assoc, Trans, SimRun, Oblig, simulation.\n- Step 6: CaseSim has an 18-step run covering alloc, newArena, issue, store, transfer to caller, free and exit, plus per-op examples for issue, store, transfer and reset, and counterexamples L0, Lsw and x10e. The pass-1 case counts are kept: CaseInit 7/7, Cases 54/56, CaseOwnedLocal 9/9, DraftGaps 3/3.\n- One commit per step (git log cd079be..fe0bd8c).\n\nDeliverable:\n- (a): all of L1-L8 and steps 5-6 are present.\n- (b): R1, R2, R4 and R6 for every operation, plus ddSound_of_layout, pinned_address_stable, freeSound_derived and simulation. The hypotheses in the R6 table match the signatures. A statement diff confirms that R1, R2 and R4 changed only in their Repr signature.\n- (c), (d), (e) are present.\n- (f): every explicit argument of simulation, every SimRun premise and both Step3 envelope conditions are listed. Class problems are in COMPL-2.\n\nDocstrings: every pass-2 rule-encoding declaration cites its clause or arbitrage. Only helper lemmas have no docstring: Exec3.reachable, ReprB.provOf_congr, dec","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1f295837-8620-4966-80d2-737f179e2223","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d714e4e0-e321-4dd1-93aa-420f18a41baa","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
