{"parentUuid":"921507c2-a8b7-4bc7-8998-73b1e90660b7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"db6ff477-9c41-43e9-8c29-33ca29113377","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wsa69ea4a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01PPPMp62EpyCgfSYv2EQgPC</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wsa69ea4a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Check that the second-check fixes of MM23 pass 2 are applied and introduce no new false claim\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"review\":{\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"R3-1\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:187-189 ((c) 10, bullet Adresse)\",\"claim\":\"FIX-2 is fixed only in the docstring. Report (c) 10 still carries the false sentence that the diff removed from `regionAddr`: \\\"C'est le premier octet de la région si cette feuille a le plus petit décalage, ce que rien ne garantit\\\". The sentence is false when the head leaf has the lowest offset and size zero. That is the case (e) 3 leaves open, and the report's own account of the second check says it was corrected (\\\"celle de `regionAddr` affirmait un cas que (e) 3 laisse ouvert\\\").\",\"evidence\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review3/p2fix/C10.lean compiles with exit 0 and no output. With `Lz := fun q =&gt; if q = 5 then ⟨4, 0, 0⟩ else L q` in CaseSim, all of these hold by `decide`: `LayoutWF Lz x9 n9 ∧ ReprB π.tok π.ptok pvA Lz x9 n9`; `(Lz 5).off &lt; (Lz 6).off ∧ (Lz 5).len = 0 ∧ regionAddr n9 Lz [5, 6] = 104`; and the bytes of [5, 6] are exactly 112..119. `Step3 KS (.issue 0 5 [5, 6] 7) x9 …` is also ok. Negative control C10neg.lean: `regionAddr n9 Lz [5, 6] = 112 := by decide` fails with \\\"Tactic `decide` proved that the proposition … is false\\\".\"},{\"id\":\"R3-2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:383-384 (Revue adverse, L7-1)\",\"claim\":\"FACTS-5 is not fully fixed. The new text says \\\"Le vérificateur ajoute, sur un fichier d'essai, que l'hypothèse des plages non vides est exactement nécessaire\\\". In the first review, the L7 reviewer (relecteur) produced `inst_iff` and its test file. The verifier only rechecked it and called it what \\\"the finding adds\\\". So the account still misattributes who added what.\",\"evidence\":\"journal wf_ad77d6e4-e1d. The review:L7 agent a38f059e5e8cd95c9, finding L7-1, has this evidence: \\\"(2) `inst_iff : DDSound {k with DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint L} ↔ ∀ l, 0 &lt; (L l).len` is proved … Checked in …/review/L7/L7check.lean\\\". The verify:L7 agent a1a993ceb56c8dbd4 says: \\\"What the finding adds is evidence that sharpens (e) 1: inst_iff shows hpos is exactly necessary\\\". Its own evidence is \\\"Rechecked with `lake env lean`\\\".\"},{\"id\":\"R3-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:237-238 ((c) 15)\",\"claim\":\"The bullet added for COMPL-3/FACTS-4 says that `repr_writes`, `repr_of_nil`, `covered_live` and `repr_deallocs` go from `Repr` to `ReprB` \\\"en hypothèse et en conclusion\\\". That is false for two of them. `repr_of_nil` has no `Repr` hypothesis; only its conclusion changed. `covered_live` has no `Repr` in its conclusion; only its hypothesis changed.\",\"evidence\":\"Statements extracted from `git show cd079be:formal/Ern/MM23.lean` and from the working tree (/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review3/p2fix/show.py). repr_of_nil goes from `(h : s3.P.length = 0) : Repr tok L s3 s2` to `(h : s3.P.length = 0) : ReprB tok ptok provOf L s3 s2`. covered_live goes from `(hR : Repr tok L s3 s2) … : l &lt; s3.P.length ∧ isLeaf s3.P l ∧ LiveAlloc s2 (L l).alloc` to `(hR : ReprB tok ptok provOf L s3 s2) … : l &lt; s3.P.length ∧ isLeaf s3.P l ∧ LiveAlloc s2 (L l).alloc`.\"},{\"id\":\"R3-4\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:240-241 ((c) 15, last bullet)\",\"claim\":\"The new closing bullet says that every other pass-1 theorem keeps its text (\\\"les autres théorèmes (R1, R2, R4, … exclusive_bytes…) gardent leur texte\\\"). Two pass-1 theorems do not. `Cases.wf2 : ∀ ops, MM02.WF (exec MM02.State.empty ops)` was removed, and nothing replaces it with that statement. `Cases.wfm8` was renamed `Cases.wf_m8`. (c) 15 accounts only for the other two removals, `Repr.change` and `Repr.shrink`.\",\"evidence\":\"`python3 -I review2/facts/stmtdiff.py p1.lean cur.lean` (p1.lean = cd079be MM23.lean, cur.lean = working tree) prints `removed ['Repr.change', 'Repr.shrink', 'Cases.wf2', 'Cases.wfm8']`. `grep -n 'theorem wf2\\\\|theorem wfm8'` matches only p1.lean:1957-1958. The working tree has `theorem wf_m8 : MM02.WF m8` (line 3600) and no theorem stating `MM02.WF (exec MM02.State.empty ops)` for all ops.\"},{\"id\":\"R3-5\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:14-16 (État de vérification)\",\"claim\":\"The FACTS-6 fix says the 154 non-public theorem constants are \\\"des constantes internes générées (`_proof_N`, `_simp_…`)\\\". The two families listed cover only 105 of the 154. The other 49 are match equation lemmas under `_private` (43) and `_sparseCasesOn_N.else_eq` lemmas (6). The axiom result is unaffected.\",\"evidence\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review3/p2fix/Count.lean prints `all thm constants of Ern.MM23: 487; non-internal: 333; internal: 154`, `internal kinds: [(_sparseCasesOn_, 6), (_proof__, 50), (_simp__, 18), (_proof_, 37), (_private, 43)]` and `outside propext, Quot.sound (all): #[]`. Priv.lean lists these names, for example `_private.Ern.MM23.0.Ern.MM23.assoc.match_1.eq_1` and `Ern.MM23.assoc._sparseCasesOn_1.else_eq`.\"},{\"id\":\"R3-6\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2