utput. With `Lz := fun q =&gt; if q = 5 then ⟨4, 0, 0⟩ else L q` in CaseSim, all of these hold by `decide`: `LayoutWF Lz x9 n9 ∧ ReprB π.tok π.ptok pvA Lz x9 n9`; `(Lz 5).off &lt; (Lz 6).off ∧ (Lz 5).len = 0 ∧ regionAddr n9 Lz [5, 6] = 104`; and the bytes of [5, 6] are exactly 112..119. `Step3 KS (.issue 0 5 [5, 6] 7) x9 …` is also ok. Negative control C10neg.lean: `regionAddr n9 Lz [5, 6] = 112 := by decide` fails with \\\"Tactic `decide` proved that the proposition … is false\\\".\"},{\"id\":\"R3-2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:383-384 (Revue adverse, L7-1)\",\"claim\":\"FACTS-5 is not fully fixed. The new text says \\\"Le vérificateur ajoute, sur un fichier d'essai, que l'hypothèse des plages non vides est exactement nécessaire\\\". In the first review, the L7 reviewer (relecteur) produced `inst_iff` and its test file. The verifier only rechecked it and called it what \\\"the finding adds\\\". So the account still misattributes who added what.\",\"evidence\":\"journal wf_ad77d6e4-e1d. The review:L7 agent a38f059e5e8cd95c9, finding L7-1, has this evidence: \\\"(2) `inst_iff : DDSound {k with DeclaredDisjoint := ByteDisjoint L} ↔ ∀ l, 0 &lt; (L l).len` is proved … Checked in …/review/L7/L7check.lean\\\". The verify:L7 agent a1a993ceb56c8dbd4 says: \\\"What the finding adds is evidence that sharpens (e) 1: inst_iff shows hpos is exactly necessary\\\". Its own evidence is \\\"Rechecked with `lake env lean`\\\".\"},{\"id\":\"R3-3\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:237-238 ((c) 15)\",\"claim\":\"The bullet added for COMPL-3/FACTS-4 says that `repr_writes`, `repr_of_nil`, `covered_live` and `repr_deallocs` go from `Repr` to `ReprB` \\\"en hypothèse et en conclusion\\\". That is false for two of them. `repr_of_nil` has no `Repr` hypothesis; only its conclusion changed. `covered_live` has no `Repr` in its conclusion; only its hypothesis changed.\",\"evidence\":\"Statements extracted from `git show cd079be:formal/Ern/MM23.lean` and from the working tree (/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review3/p2fix/show.py). repr_of_nil goes from `(h : s3.P.length = 0) : Repr tok L s3 s2` to `(h : s3.P.length = 0) : ReprB tok ptok provOf L s3 s2`. covered_live goes from `(hR : Repr tok L s3 s2) … : l &lt; s3.P.length ∧ isLeaf s3.P l ∧ LiveAlloc s2 (L l).alloc` to `(hR : ReprB tok ptok provOf L s3 s2) … : l &lt; s3.P.length ∧ isLeaf s3.P l ∧ LiveAlloc s2 (L l).alloc`.\"},{\"id\":\"R3-4\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:240-241 ((c) 15, last bullet)\",\"claim\":\"The new closing bullet says that every other pass-1 theorem keeps its text (\\\"les autres théorèmes (R1, R2, R4, … exclusive_bytes…) gardent leur texte\\\"). Two pass-1 theorems do not. `Cases.wf2 : ∀ ops, MM02.WF (exec MM02.State.empty ops)` was removed, and nothing replaces it with that statement. `Cases.wfm8` was renamed `Cases.wf_m8`. (c) 15 accounts only for the other two removals, `Repr.change` and `Repr.shrink`.\",\"evidence\":\"`python3 -I review2/facts/stmtdiff.py p1.lean cur.lean` (p1.lean = cd079be MM23.lean, cur.lean = working tree) prints `removed ['Repr.change', 'Repr.shrink', 'Cases.wf2', 'Cases.wfm8']`. `grep -n 'theorem wf2\\\\|theorem wfm8'` matches only p1.lean:1957-1958. The working tree has `theorem wf_m8 : MM02.WF m8` (line 3600) and no theorem stating `MM02.WF (exec MM02.State.empty ops)` for all ops.\"},{\"id\":\"R3-5\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:14-16 (État de vérification)\",\"claim\":\"The FACTS-6 fix says the 154 non-public theorem constants are \\\"des constantes internes générées (`_proof_N`, `_simp_…`)\\\". The two families listed cover only 105 of the 154. The other 49 are match equation lemmas under `_private` (43) and `_sparseCasesOn_N.else_eq` lemmas (6). The axiom result is unaffected.\",\"evidence\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review3/p2fix/Count.lean prints `all thm constants of Ern.MM23: 487; non-internal: 333; internal: 154`, `internal kinds: [(_sparseCasesOn_, 6), (_proof__, 50), (_simp__, 18), (_proof_, 37), (_private, 43)]` and `outside propext, Quot.sound (all): #[]`. Priv.lean lists these names, for example `_private.Ern.MM23.0.Ern.MM23.assoc.match_1.eq_1` and `Ern.MM23.assoc._sparseCasesOn_1.else_eq`.\"},{\"id\":\"R3-6\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:334-340 vs 318-321 ((f))\",\"claim\":\"The COMPL-2 fix takes the three conditions out of the table as \\\"sans être des hypothèses à classer\\\" and says \\\"L1 et L2 mettent ces deux formes hors du langage\\\". This has two problems. (1) The unchanged (f) introduction still counts the Step3 domain among the hypotheses to be classed (\\\"Les hypothèses de `simulation` sont de trois sortes : … le domaine de `Step3`, fixé par L1 et L2. Classement demandé : …\\\"), so the section now contradicts itself. (2) L2 does not say that a multi-root alloc is out of the language; it calls the condition a hypothesis of the statements. Deliverable (f) asks for every hypothesis to be classed. So the L2 condition is exempted from classification by a reading that no text supports, and (e) raises no question about it.\",\"evidence\":\"Brief: \\\"L2. `alloc` : la forme a exactement une racine (hypothèse des énoncés).\\\" By contrast, L1 says: \\\"une forme d'`enterFrame` portant un élément propriétaire est hors du langage\\\". Deliverable: \\\"(f) liste finale des hypothèses de `simulation`, chacune classée : obligation de la spec 4 (types), de la spec 11 (ABI), de la bibliothèque, ou ouverte\\\". Report l.318-320: \\\"Les hypothèses de `simulation` sont de trois sortes : celles de l'énoncé, globales ; les prémisses de `SimRun`, … ; le domaine de `Step3`, fixé par L1 et L2\\\". Report l.334: \\\"Trois conditions restreignent le domaine de `simulation` sans être des hypothèses à classer\\\". The (a) table, l.53, itself calls it \\\"hypothèse `hone` de `r6_alloc`\\\".\"},{\"id\":\"R3-7\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"location\":\"formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md:32-35 (Résultats principaux, item 2)\",\"claim\":\"FACTS-1 is only partly fixed. The new text describes `PtrEncAt` only as \\\"`decode` rend l'adresse écrite\\\", then lists among what the theorems show \\\"que chaque octet porte la provenance de cette allocation\\\". `PtrEncAt` also assumes that every byte carries the given provenance. For `store`, the per-byte provenance conclusion follows from that second conjunct alone, through the definitions of `ptrBytes` and `regionProv`. The summary therefore still presents part of the hypothesis as a result. (For `issue`, identifying `arenaProv` with the allocation of `l` is genuinely proved, by `issue_prov_storage`.)\",\"evidence\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/review3/p2fix/C10.lean compiles with exit 0. It proves `(hl : rg.head? = some l) (hpe : PtrEncAt pe (regionAddr s2 L rg) (regionProv L rg)) : ∀ i, (ptrBytes pe s2 L rg i).2 = some (L l).alloc` with no WF3, Repr or step hypothesis, by `have := hpe.2 i; simp … ; simpa [ptrBytes, regionProv, hl] using this`. Negative control in C10neg.lean, which compiles with no error at that example:\n... (truncated 10648 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wsa69ea4a.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/subagents/workflows/wf_3af303ed-b18/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/workflows/scripts/mm23-p2-third-check-wf_3af303ed-b18.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_3af303ed-b18'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>2</agent_count><agents_done>2</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>351521</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>61</tool_uses><duration_ms>754163</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
