{"parentUuid":"d8d070d0-2b13-4dde-9601-77b7e447a242","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbC2BzLJxUAgW6ZPkMUf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SVuDsZG6KD1tcMA3ne5E2a","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wsa69ea4a.output'\nd=json.load(open(p))['result']\nv={x['id']:x for x in (d.get('verdicts') or [])}\nfor f in d['review']['findings']:\n    vv=v.get(f['id'])\n    print(f\"--- {f['id']} verdict real={None if not vv else vv['real']}\")\n    if f['id'] in ('R3-7','R3-8','R3-9','R3-10'): print(\"CLAIM:\", f['claim'])\n    if vv: print(\"VERIFIER:\", vv['reason'][:900])\n    print()\nEOF","description":"Extract third-check verdicts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4786,"cache_read_input_tokens":486174,"output_tokens":350,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4786,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":486174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4786},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SVuDsZG6KD1tcMA3ne5E2a":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/tasks/wsa69ea4a.output'\nd=json.load(open(p))['result']\nv={x['id']:x for x in (d.get('verdicts') or [])}\nfor f in d['review']['findings']:\n    vv=v.get(f['id'])\n    print(f\"--- {f['id']} verdict real={None if not vv else vv['real']}\")\n    if f['id'] in ('R3-7','R3-8','R3-9','R3-10'): print(\"CLAIM:\", f['claim'])\n    if vv: print(\"VERIFIER:\", vv['reason'][:900])\n    print()\nEOF","description":"Extract third-check verdicts"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"73ebc9a5-02ff-4151-82e3-8361aefdcd22","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgbC2BdFMNgMLwBeSzyan","requestRef":"adcf69b0-02d0-4f29-9fbc-0b6f5ff65d22","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15ca3457-7b3e-481b-a7b0-be3a458c0562","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:34:39.849Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"15ca3457-7b3e-481b-a7b0-be3a458c0562","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"db6ff477-9c41-43e9-8c29-33ca29113377","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SVuDsZG6KD1tcMA3ne5E2a","type":"tool_result","content":"--- R3-1 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: The finding holds. The diff changed only the `regionAddr` docstring. Report (c) 10, lines 188-189, still says: \"C'est le premier octet de la région si cette feuille a le plus petit décalage, ce que rien ne garantit\". That is the same claim FIX-2 found false. It fails when the head leaf has the lowest offset and size zero, which is the case (e) 3 leaves open (\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\"). The report's own account of the second check says this was corrected, but the report text was not.\n\n--- R3-2 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: The new text says \"Le vérificateur ajoute, sur un fichier d'essai, que l'hypothèse des plages non vides est exactement nécessaire\". In the first review, the L7 reviewer (relecteur) proved `inst_iff` and wrote the test file. The verifier only rechecked that same file and called it what \"the finding adds\". So the account still credits the wrong agent.\n\n--- R3-3 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: The bullet says the four lemmas pass from `Repr` to `ReprB` \"en hypothèse et en conclusion\". That holds for `repr_writes` and `repr_deallocs` only. `repr_of_nil` has no Repr-type hypothesis; only its conclusion changed. `covered_live` concludes on `LiveAlloc`; only its hypothesis `hR` changed. The wording is copied from the FACTS-4 verdict, which was already wrong on this point.\n\n--- R3-4 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: (c) 15 ends with \"les autres théorèmes (…) gardent leur texte\" and names only `Repr.change` and `Repr.shrink` as removed. `Cases.wf2 : ∀ ops, MM02.WF (exec MM02.State.empty ops)` no longer exists. `Cases.wfm8` is now `Cases.wf_m8`: same statement text, new name. The (Revue adverse) section mentions \"4 retirés et remplacés\" without names, so (c) 15 also disagrees with the report's own count. Impact is small: wf2 is a trivial corollary of `exec_wf`, which remains, and wf_m0…wf_mF take over its role in Cases.\n\n--- R3-5 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: The counts hold. Of the 154 internal theorem constants, 105 are `_proof_N`/`_simp_` and 49 are not: 43 private match equation lemmas and 6 `_sparseCasesOn_N.else_eq`. The report's parenthetical \"(`_proof_N`, `_simp_…`)\" reads as an enumeration, and it misses those 49. The defect is cosmetic: \"constantes internes générées\" is true of all 154, and the axiom result is unaffected.\n\n--- R3-6 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: (1) The (f) introduction is unchanged. It still counts \"le domaine de `Step3`, fixé par L1 et L2\" among the hypotheses of `simulation` and is followed by \"Classement demandé\". The new paragraph then says these conditions, and `ShapeOK`, a `SimRun` premise, are \"sans être des hypothèses à classer\". The section contradicts itself. (2) The French brief's L2 reads \"`alloc` : la forme a exactement une racine (hypothèse des énoncés)\". Only L1 says \"hors du langage\". So the L2 condition is by the brief's own words a hypothesis of the statements, and deliverable (f) requires every hypothesis to be classed. The fix leaves it unclassed and raises no (e) question, which is the defect COMPL-2 confirmed, reshaped.\n\n--- R3-7 verdict real=True\nCLAIM: FACTS-1 is only partly fixed. The new text describes `PtrEncAt` only as \"`decode` rend l'adresse écrite\", then lists among what the theorems show \"que chaque octet porte la provenance de cette allocation\". `PtrEncAt` also assumes that every byte carries the given provenance. For `store`, the per-byte provenance conclusion follows from that second conjunct alone, through the definitions of `ptrBytes` and `regionProv`. The summary therefore still presents part of the hypothesis as a result. (For `issue`, identifying `arenaProv` with the allocation of `l` is genuinely proved, by `issue_prov_storage`.)\nVERIFIER: Main result 2 now glosses `PtrEncAt` only as \"`decode` rend l'adresse écrite\". It then lists \"que chaque octet porte la provenance de cette allocation\" among what the theorems show. `PtrEncAt` also assumes that every byte carries `prov`. For `store`, prov = `regionProv L rg`, which is the allocation of the head leaf by definition. So the per-byte provenance conjunct of `pointer_sound_store` is the hypothesis's second half unfolded, which is the same pattern FACTS-1 found for decode. For `issue`, the identification of `arenaProv` with the allocation of `l` is genuinely proved, by `issue_prov_storage`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"05b977b5-0c7c-47cc-ad23-c875397bf258","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:34:40.687Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"--- R3-1 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: The finding holds. The diff changed only the `regionAddr` docstring. Report (c) 10, lines 188-189, still says: \"C'est le premier octet de la région si cette feuille a le plus petit décalage, ce que rien ne garantit\". That is the same claim FIX-2 found false. It fails when the head leaf has the lowest offset and size zero, which is the case (e) 3 leaves open (\"Et que faire d'une feuille de taille nulle placée avant les autres ?\"). The report's own account of the second check says this was corrected, but the report text was not.\n\n--- R3-2 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: The new text says \"Le vérificateur ajoute, sur un fichier d'essai, que l'hypothèse des plages non vides est exactement nécessaire\". In the first review, the L7 reviewer (relecteur) proved `inst_iff` and wrote the test file. The verifier only rechecked that same file and called it what \"the finding adds\". So the account still credits the wrong agent.\n\n--- R3-3 verdict real=True\nVERIFIER: The bullet says the four lemmas pass from `Repr` to `ReprB` \"en hypothèse et en conclusion\". That holds for `repr_writes` and `repr_deallocs` only. `repr_of_nil` has no Repr-type hypothes