fixed. The new text describes `PtrEncAt` only as \"`decode` rend l'adresse écrite\", then lists among what the theorems show \"que chaque octet porte la provenance de cette allocation\". `PtrEncAt` also assumes that every byte carries the given provenance. For `store`, the per-byte provenance conclusion follows from that second conjunct alone, through the definitions of `ptrBytes` and `regionProv`. The summary therefore still presents part of the hypothesis as a result. (For `issue`, identifying `arenaProv` with the allocation of `l` is genuinely proved, by `issue_prov_storage`.)\nVERIFIER: Main result 2 now glosses `PtrEncAt` only as \"`decode` rend l'adresse écrite\". It then lists \"que chaque octet porte la provenance de cette allocation\" among what the theorems show. `PtrEncAt` also assumes that every byte carries `prov`. For `store`, prov = `regionProv L rg`, which is the allocation of the head leaf by definition. So the per-byte provenance conjunct of `pointer_sound_store` is the hypothesis's second half unfolded, which is the same pattern FACTS-1 found for decode. For `issue`, the identification of `arenaProv` with the allocation of `l` is genuinely proved, by `issue_prov_storage`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"73ebc9a5-02ff-4151-82e3-8361aefdcd22","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/