{"parentUuid":"d996333f-1abf-4b52-a0cd-815d0f8af3d8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"db6ff477-9c41-43e9-8c29-33ca29113377","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HAC3e42cwk1p5Kmg59tgnF","type":"tool_result","content":"# ub-mode log — MM23 pass 2\n\n19. Saved the pass-2 brief summary to task_mm23_p2.md; stayed on formal/refinement_0.1. Why: brief §Git (\"même branche, à la suite\").\n20. Step 1 (9c08116): split Repr into decidable ReprB + Repr (WF clause, L3); added provTokens and the ghost provOf (L4); freeSound_derived replaces the FreeSound hypothesis of r6_free. Why: L3, L4. Found r6_enter needs no L1, so L1/L2 became an envelope of Step3 rather than hypotheses.\n21. Step 2 (cf09f12): transfer/store/issue sequences (L6), r6_transfer/r6_store/r6_issue, transfer_copies. Found r6_transfer holds without SameSizeAlong; only transfer_copies needs it, so it stays off r6_transfer and simulation (stronger statements).\n22. Step 3 (837a192): ddSound_of_layout. Found L7 literally false with zero-size leaves (K1 (d)); kept the counterexample with a LayoutWF witness; added the non-empty-range hypothesis and a report question.\n23. Step 4 (5fd6d8a): pinned_address_stable via PinnedLive on reached states and exec_keeps_base.\n24. Step 5 (10b837c): first draft quantified obligations over all translations (vacuity risk caught by self-review); rewrote as SimRun with per-run Oblig premises and Params fixed once; proved simulation and simulation_pinned.\n25. Step 6 (579808d): 18-step CaseSim run (alloc, arena, issue, store, transfer to caller, free, exits) as SimRun prefixes with an explicit ghost; witnesses for each new operation; negative Repr checks. Found PtrEncOK (universal) unsatisfiable by a finite decode; replaced by per-pointer PtrEncAt and added pointer_sound_store/issue for the L6 obligation. An unquoted heredoc once expanded backticks in docstrings: reverted the insertion and redid it with a quoted heredoc.\n26. Verified: build clean, 331 theorem constants and all 90 examples (renamed to theorems in a scratch copy) within {propext, Quot.sound}; forbidden-word grep empty.\n27. Adversarial review workflow launched: 5 lenses (L4, L6, L7, simulation, general) + one refuter per lens with findings. Why: brief §Règles and memory lesson (one reviewer per lens).\n28. Review result: 11 findings, 9 confirmed (3 duplicates on the r6_transfer docstring), 2 refuted. L4: none. Fixed: issue provenance now arenaProv (L6 says \"allocation of arena storage\"; the empty block had none) with issue_prov_storage proved under ArenasInv; docstrings (r6_transfer, simulation, pointer_sound_*, regionAddr, module header). Why not change regionAddr: \"first byte\" vs \"first leaf\" is ambiguous in L6, so AGENTS says report, not pick; added witnesses and question (e) 3.\n29. Added witnesses for the new questions: store after split into [] (e) 2, region [6, 5] and swapped layout (e) 3, target leaf of size 0 (e) 4. Made pass-2 report citations explicit in docstrings (two reports now).\n30. Verified and committed fe0bd8c: build clean; 333 theorem constants and all 95 examples within {propext, Quot.sound}; no new line over 100 characters (counted in characters, not bytes).\n31. Second targeted check launched on fe0bd8c: fixes, report facts, completeness, one refuter per lens. Why: memory lesson (fixes can introduce new errors; report claims need witnesses).\n32. Second check: 11 minor findings, 10 confirmed (2 duplicates), 1 refuted. Fixed: r6_issue and regionAddr docstrings; report summary (decoding is the PtrEncAt hypothesis), (f) alignment row and domain conditions set apart from the four classes, (c) 15 completed (repr_extend and four lemmas), CaseSim.inv in the changed list, L7-1 account, constant count 487 (333 non-internal), verified with a Lean script.\n33. Third check launched on the uncommitted wording fixes (one checker plus refuter). Why: fixes can introduce new false claims.\n34. Third check: 7 minor findings, all confirmed (a sentence fixed in a docstring but left in the report; per-byte provenance also comes from PtrEncAt; (c) 15 side of change and two Cases renames; internal-constant families; (f) contradicted itself and L2 says \"hypothèse des énoncés\", so the envelopes are now classed \"ouverte\"; L7-1 credit). Fixed in the report only.\n35. Committed 278a42d after a final build, 487-constant axiom sweep, grep, and MM02/MM03 diff check. Not pushed, no merge, no PR: the brief says \"Pas de merge, pas de PR\", which overrides ub-mode's push step.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e1d1f5ff-9e6a-47ae-8e44-8cc22b8bfb2e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:36:39.839Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# ub-mode log — MM23 pass 2\n\n19. Saved the pass-2 brief summary to task_mm23_p2.md; stayed on formal/refinement_0.1. Why: brief §Git (\"même branche, à la suite\").\n20. Step 1 (9c08116): split Repr into decidable ReprB + Repr (WF clause, L3); added provTokens and the ghost provOf (L4); freeSound_derived replaces the FreeSound hypothesis of r6_free. Why: L3, L4. Found r6_enter needs no L1, so L1/L2 became an envelope of Step3 rather than hypotheses.\n21. Step 2 (cf09f12): transfer/store/issue sequences (L6), r6_transfer/r6_store/r6_issue, transfer_copies. Found r6_transfer holds without SameSizeAlong; only transfer_copies needs it, so it stays off r6_transfer and simulation (stronger statements).\n22. Step 3 (837a192): ddSound_of_layout. Found L7 literally false with zero-size leaves (K1 (d)); kept the counterexample with a LayoutWF witness; added the non-empty-range hypothesis and a report question.\n23. Step 4 (5fd6d8a): pinned_address_stable via PinnedLive on reached states and exec_keeps_base.\n24. Step 5 (10b837c): first draft quantified obligations over all translations (vacuity risk caught by self-review); rewrote as SimRun with per-run Oblig premises and Params fixed once; proved simulation and simulation_pinned.\n25. Step 6 (579808d): 18-step CaseSim run (alloc, arena, issue, store, transfer to caller, free, exits) as SimRun prefixes with an explicit ghost; witnesses for each new operation; negative Repr checks. Found PtrEncOK (universal) unsatisfiable by a finite decode; replaced by per-pointer PtrEncAt and added pointer_sound_store/issue for the L6 obligation. An unquoted heredoc once expanded backticks in docstrings: reverted the insertion and redid it with a quoted heredoc.\n26. Verified: build clean, 331 theorem constants and all 90 examples (renamed to theorems in a scratch copy) within {propext, Quot.sound}; forbidden-word grep empty.\n27. Adversarial review workflow launched: 5 lenses (L4, L6, L7, simulation, general) + one refuter per lens with findings. Why: brief §Règles and memory lesson (one reviewer per lens).\n28. Review result: 11 findings, 9 confirmed (3 duplicates on the r6_transfer docstring), 2 refuted. L4: none. Fixed: issue provenance now arenaProv (L6 says \"allocation of arena storage\"; the empty block had none) with issue_prov_storage proved under ArenasInv; docstrings (r6_transfer, simulation, pointer_sound_*, regionAddr, module header). Why not change regionAddr: \"first byte\" vs \"first leaf\" is ambiguous in L6, so AGENTS says report, not pick; added witnesses and question (e) 3.\n29. Added witnesses for the new questions: store after split into [] (e) 2, region [6, 5] and swapped layout (e) 3, target leaf of size 0 (e) 4. Made pass-2 report citations explicit in docstrings (two reports now).\n30. Verified and committed fe0bd8c: build clean; 333 theorem constants and all 95 examples within {propext, Quot.sound}; no new line over 100 characters (counted in characters, not bytes).\n31. Second targeted check launched on fe0bd8c: fixes, report facts, completeness, one refuter per lens. Why: memory lesson (fixes can introduce new errors; report claims need witnesses).\n32. Second check: 11 minor findings, 10 confirmed (2 duplicates), 1 refuted. Fixed: r6_issue and regionAddr docstrings; report summary (decoding is the PtrEncAt hypothesis), (f) alignment row and domain conditions set apart from the four classes, (c) 15 completed (repr_extend and four lemmas), CaseSim.inv in the changed list, L7-1 account, constant count 487 (333 non-internal), verified with a Lean script.\n33. Third check launched on the uncommitted wording fixes (one checker plus refuter). Why: fixes can introduce new false claims.\n34. Third check: 7 minor findings, all confirmed (a sentence fixed in a docstring but left in the report; per-byte provenance also comes from PtrEncAt; (c) 15 side of change and two Cases renames; internal-constant families; (f) contradicted itself and L2 says \"hypothèse des énoncés\", so the envelopes are now classed \"ouverte\"; L7-1 credit). Fixed in the report only.\n35. Committed 278a42d after a final build, 487-constant axiom sweep, grep, and MM02/MM03 diff check. Not pushed, no merge, no PR: the brief says \"Pas de merge, pas de PR\", which overrides ub-mode's push step.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fbabc8cf-6d99-4e87-8ce0-ff81f591b597","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/refinement_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d996333f-1abf-4b52-a0cd-815d0f8af3d8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-deskt