{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","id":"e362d49a-c8d3-4407-8a45-05bb0c11ef11","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:36:42.955Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"d1aa6c2254c890b11835611a868b353c28b0e75545aafd34fb8d8155d691dfb1","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"ad8290ee-3576-46f5-82cb-778008378546","keep":251,"tail":["e340d7b0563e429c56213102d0331536ec37221447557b9d807d7a15f17cecf6","afed5839d7048b0511827e7a0d37a91164268b9f36c9c7ded5f3315e08250cb4"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",252,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8828ebfaba77d41f436ac0e3abb14345fae367ed4004ccc7fd60ede45c32eb30"}
{"parentUuid":"c6cef499-d777-4bf6-87b8-ae4d271f5f26","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbCBYJT5FJGGpyF5sMGf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass 2 is done and committed on `formal/refinement_0.1`, with no merge, no PR and nothing pushed. The build is clean with no warnings. All 487 theorem constants and all 95 examples use only `propext` and `Quot.sound`. `MM02.lean` and `MM03.lean` are unchanged.\n\n**What was proved**\n- **`simulation`:** an MM-03 execution has an MM-02 translation whose operations are all `ok` and which stays in `Repr` at every step, starting from the initial state of `repr_init`. This holds when:\n  - the execution starts from `S3.init statics` and stays within L1 and L2;\n  - the layout, placement, tokens and pointer encoding are fixed once for the whole run;\n  - every step meets its obligations.\n\n  The witness `CaseSim` is an 18-step run covering allocation, arena, `issue`, `store`, `transfer` to the caller, `free` and both frame exits.\n- **R6 for every operation:** `transfer`, `store` and `issue` are now covered (L6), and `reset` maps to no MM-02 step. `transfer_copies` shows the copy keeps every byte and its provenance. For `issue`, the pointer's provenance is the allocation of the arena storage, as L6 states (`issue_prov_storage`).\n- **`freeSound_derived` (L4):** it follows from the token clause of `Repr`, which every step preserves, so the derivation is not circular.\n- **`pinned_address_stable` (L8):** a pinned leaf keeps a live allocation and the same address.\n- **`ddSound_of_layout` (L7):** proved only with one extra hypothesis, that leaves of declared regions are non-empty. L7 as written is false when a leaf has size zero; the counterexample is kept in the module.\n\n**Decisions for you** (report section (e), each with a Lean witness):\n1. L7 with zero-size leaves.\n2. Which address (and, for `store`, which provenance) a pointer to an empty region should get. MM-03 accepts both `issue []` and `store` after `split` into `[]`.\n3. Whether L6's \"premier octet / première feuille\" means the lowest address or the first leaf in the region's list. They differ when the list order or the field order changes: region `[6, 5]` gives 112 instead of 104.\n4. Whether to require that a leaf receiving a reference has the size of a pointer. With size 0, the leaf receives no byte of the pointer.\n5. Whether `SameShape` should also compare the `kind` field, so that same sizes follow from types.\n6. Whether stating the remaining obligations per execution, rather than for every `Reachable` execution, is the intended form of `simulation`.\n\n**Not proved:** that every execution admits parameters meeting its obligations. `dec` and `FreeCompat` belong to MM-02 and to the library, so they can't be discharged in general.\n\n**Review:** three rounds, each finding re-checked by an agent trying to refute it.\n- First review (5 lenses): 11 findings, 9 confirmed, none blocking. The fix for one of them changed how `issue` pointer bytes are defined.\n- Second check: 11 minor findings, 10 confirmed.\n- Third check: 7 minor findings, all confirmed.\n\n**ub-mode log, pass 2** (entries 19 to 35):\n- **Step 1, 9c08116:** `Repr` split into a decidable part `ReprB` plus `MM02.WF`; ghost `provOf` and `freeSound_derived`. L1 and L2 became restrictions on the allowed steps, because `r6_enter` needs no L1.\n- **Step 2, cf09f12:** `transfer`, `store` and `issue`. `r6_transfer` turned out not to need `SameSizeAlong`; only the byte-copy theorem does.\n- **Step 3, 837a192:** found L7 false with zero-size leaves; counterexample kept, and the question goes in the report.\n- **Step 4, 5fd6d8a:** `pinned_address_stable`.\n- **Step 5, 10b837c:** my first draft quantified the obligations over every translation, which risked making the theorem vacuous. I rewrote it so the obligations are premises on the given run, with the parameters fixed once.\n- **Step 6, 579808d:** the 18-step run. The universal pointer-encoding obligation could not be met by any finite `decode`, so it now applies per pointer, and two pointer theorems were added.\n- **Review fixes, fe0bd8c:** `issue` provenance now follows L6; docstrings corrected; witnesses added for the questions.\n- **Check fixes, 278a42d:** wording only, in two docstrings and the report.\n- **Not pushed:** the brief's \"Pas de merge, pas de PR\" overrides ub-mode's push step.\n\nThe report is at [MM23_v0.1_p2.md](formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":511671,"output_tokens":1641,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1641,"cache_read_input_tokens":511671,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"378f8e4a-9462-46fe-bf69-b89f22747e76","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgbCBY4KFXFoSSs6p7bFu","requestRef":"e362d49a-c8d3-4407-8a45-05bb0c11ef11","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"ee149a53-76ae-463f-943e-2b48434e49b7","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:36:57.999Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
