{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"c040b4d3-da8e-4846-ae0a-33ebe748d3da","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"auto","preTokens":521482,"postTokens":35054,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":7845353,"durationMs":13,"precomputed":true,"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"ee149a53-76ae-463f-943e-2b48434e49b7","anchorUuid":"42d985ed-be40-46cc-b938-f137b63ff549","tailUuid":"c040b4d3-da8e-4846-ae0a-33ebe748d3da"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"42d985ed-be40-46cc-b938-f137b63ff549","uuids":["ee149a53-76ae-463f-943e-2b48434e49b7","32268143-f2d7-4691-9d4b-6d844ee11195","7eafe96c-3b3c-4b36-b770-1b007ce8e182","c040b4d3-da8e-4846-ae0a-33ebe748d3da"],"allUuids":["ee149a53-76ae-463f-943e-2b48434e49b7","84cbff99-6dc0-48a3-9fa6-b8786ebd7a80","44dee18f-e0ab-4547-8358-5d0877cd85ed","d9f3377e-1e8c-4b76-ae14-8f00cf03b7de","32268143-f2d7-4691-9d4b-6d844ee11195","7eafe96c-3b3c-4b36-b770-1b007ce8e182","c040b4d3-da8e-4846-ae0a-33ebe748d3da"]},"runningTurnSends":{"uuids":[],"openerUuid":"7eafe96c-3b3c-4b36-b770-1b007ce8e182","summarisedOnly":["7eafe96c-3b3c-4b36-b770-1b007ce8e182"]}},"uuid":"ef52eaf5-fc77-41d6-b17e-68e0d804bda3","timestamp":"2026-11-01T17:17:28.213Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"ef52eaf5-fc77-41d6-b17e-68e0d804bda3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"@AGENTS.md\n\n## Claude Code\n\nYou implement. The Review section applies to you only when asked.\nBefore coding, list the spec passages the task covers and read them in full."},{"path":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nClaude Code implements. Codex reviews. Both follow this file.\n\n## Source of truth\n\n- `specs/` is normative and the only source of semantics. Before acting, read the spec text the task depends on. Never rely on memory, summaries, comments or earlier sessions.\n- Never restate spec content in code comments or agent files. Point to its location.\n- Spec beats code. If the spec is ambiguous, contradictory or silent on something the task needs: stop and report the exact passage with a concrete example of the problem. Never pick an interpretation yourself.\n- Representation choices (structure or inductive type, function or relation) are yours when they change no accepted program and no behavior. A choice that does is a semantic question: stop and report.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Do exactly the task. No unrequested features, generalization, refactoring or \"robustness\" additions. Put suggestions in the report.\n- Do not edit `specs/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` or `formal/DESIGN.md` unless the task says so.\n\n## Lean\n\n- The Lake project is in `formal/`. `formal/DESIGN.md` governs how to formalize, never what the semantics is. Propose design decisions it does not settle in your report; never take them silently.\n- Every definition or theorem that encodes a spec rule cites the rule's location in its docstring.\n- A definition says what its rule says. Never make a definition more permissive, add an unjustified hypothesis or narrow a theorem's domain to obtain a proof.\n- Never change a theorem statement, or a definition it depends on, to make a proof go through. If stuck, stop and report the goal state.\n- Never use `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` or `native_decide`.\n- Every `.lean` file under `formal/` is part of the build target.\n- Done means:\n  - `lake build` (in `formal/`) succeeds;\n  - this prints nothing: `grep -rnE '\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\b|^\\s*axiom\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake .`\n  - for each theorem completed by the task, `#print axioms` lists nothing beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.\n\n## Report\n\nSpec passages implemented (by location), what changed, what is unproven or open, spec problems found.\n\n## Review (Codex)\n\nAdversarial and read-only. For each change, check:\n\n- It says exactly what the spec says: not stronger, not weaker. Read definitions, hypotheses and quantifiers, not only proofs. A theorem that holds because a definition is too permissive or its hypotheses are unsatisfiable is blocking.\n- Each formalized rule cites its spec location.\n- No theorem statement or dependency was changed without the task allowing it.\n- No interpretation was chosen silently where the spec is unclear.\n- Nothing outside the task was added.\n\nWhen a milestone is declared complete, compare the rules in its announced scope with the spec locations cited in `formal/`, and list every rule left without a definition or theorem.\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a spec quote, a counterexample or command output. No evidence, no finding. Never ask for additions beyond the task.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity, location, cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence."},{"path":"/Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem","content":"- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23 branches, reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule, no-weakening diff"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"72c52f96-56a4-4efa-aa8e-e71dacac70ba","timestamp":"2026-11-01T17:17:28.212Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/CLAUDE.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n@AGENTS.md\n\n## Claude Code\n\nYou implement. The Review section applies to you only when asked.\nBefore coding, list the spec passages the task covers and read them in full.\n\nContents of /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/AGENTS.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# AGENTS.md\n\nClaude Code implements. Codex reviews. Both follow this file.\n\n## Source of truth\n\n- `specs/` is normative and the only source of semantics. Before acting, read the spec text the task depends on. Never rely on memory, summaries, comments or earlier sessions.\n- Never restate spec content in code comments or agent files. Point to its location.\n- Spec beats code. If the spec is ambiguous, contradictory or silent on something the task needs: stop and report the exact passage with a concrete example of the problem. Never pick an interpretation yourself.\n- Representation choices (structure or inductive type, function or relation) are yours when they change no accepted program and no behavior. A choice that does is a semantic question: stop and report.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Do exactly the task. No unrequested features, generalization, refactoring or \"robustness\" additions. Put suggestions in the report.\n- Do not edit `specs/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` or `formal/DESIGN.md` unless the task says so.\n\n## Lean\n\n- The Lake project is in `formal/`. `formal/DESIGN.md` governs how to formalize, never what the semantics is. Propose design decisions it does not settle in your report; never take them silently.\n- Every definition or theorem that encodes a spec rule cites the rule's location in its docstring.\n- A definition says what its rule says. Never make a definition more permissive, add an unjustified hypothesis or narrow a theorem's domain to obtain a proof.\n- Never change a theorem statement, or a definition it depends on, to make a proof go through. If stuck, stop and report the goal state.\n- Never use `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom` or `native_decide`.\n- Every `.lean` file under `formal/` is part of the build target.\n- Done means:\n  - `lake build` (in `formal/`) succeeds;\n  - this prints nothing: `grep -rnE '\\b(sorry|admit|native_decide)\\b|^\\s*axiom\\b' --include='*.lean' --exclude-dir=.lake .`\n  - for each theorem completed by the task, `#print axioms` lists nothing beyond `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.\n\n## Report\n\nSpec passages implemented (by location), what changed, what is unproven or open, spec problems found.\n\n## Review (Codex)\n\nAdversarial and read-only. For each change, check:\n\n- It says exactly what the spec says: not stronger, not weaker. Read definitions, hypotheses and quantifiers, not only proofs. A theorem that holds because a definition is too permissive or its hypotheses are unsatisfiable is blocking.\n- Each formalized rule cites its spec location.\n- No theorem statement or dependency was changed without the task allowing it.\n- No interpretation was chosen silently where the spec is unclear.\n- Nothing outside the task was added.\n\nWhen a milestone is declared complete, compare the rules in its announced scope with the spec locations cited in `formal/`, and list every rule left without a definition or theorem.\n\nEvery finding needs evidence: a spec quote, a counterexample or command output. No evidence, no finding. Never ask for additions beyond the task.\n\nOutput: verdict (block / changes / ok), then each finding with severity, location, cause (formalization error, missing coverage or spec defect) and evidence.\n\nContents of /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n- [ERN formal exploratory passes](ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md) — French briefs, MM-02/MM-03/MM-23 branches, reports/ never merged, spec in ~/Downloads, axiom rule, no-weakening diff\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
