{"parentUuid":"037c42cc-3717-4acf-a726-4473c81a63d5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d8867bcf-fa69-4463-9401-ce9d6d53950a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Read, Skill, Workflow, Write, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up, mcp__terminal__read_terminal</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **ub-mode (invoked earlier).** Work \"make it work → make it right → practice\", keep a log of every action and its reason, and report that log at completion. The briefs' « Pas de merge, pas de PR » overrides ub-mode's push to main.\n   - **Pass-2 brief** (pasted in French, summarized in `$SP/task_mm23_p2.md`): « Tâche : jalon 2, passe 2 — raffinement MM-03 → MM-02 (transfer, store, issue, DDSound, épinglage, simulation) ».\n     - Git, verbatim: « Même branche `formal/refinement_0.1`, à la suite. Pas de merge, pas de PR. Tout sous `formal/`. `Ern/MM02.lean` et `Ern/MM03.lean` inchangés ; tout ajout va dans `Ern/MM23.lean` ou un module voisin. »\n     - Language: code, docstrings, comments and commits in English; the report in French.\n     - Arbitrages L1–L8 font foi.\n     - Steps, one commit each: 1 (L1–L5), 2 (L6), 3 (L7), 4 (L8), 5 (simulation), 6 (cases: one witness per new operation, plus a full execution with allocation, arena, emission, store, transfer to the caller, free and frame exit).\n     - Rules: zero sorry; axioms ⊆ {propext, Quot.sound}; no noncomputable; a build without warnings; docstrings cite clause or arbitrage; nothing invented; no statement weakened; counterexamples kept; adversarial review on L4, L6, L7 and simulation vacuity.\n     - Deliverable: `formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md` with sections (a) to (f).\n   - **AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md rules:**\n     - The spec is the only source of semantics.\n     - If the spec is ambiguous, stop and report with an example; never pick an interpretation.\n     - Never weaken a definition or theorem.\n     - Do not edit `specs/`, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md or `formal/DESIGN.md`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Toolchain.** Lean 4 core v4.35, no Mathlib.\n     - Build with `~/.elan/bin/lake build` in `formal/`; scratch checks with `~/.elan/bin/lake env lean <file>`. `lake env lean` uses the last built olean.\n     - `SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad`.\n     - Axiom scripts: `$SP/mm23/axcheck.lean` checks non-internal theorem constants; `$SP/mm23/axcheck_all.lean` checks all 487 (333 non-internal).\n     - Example axioms are checked by renaming `example` to `theorem` in a scratch copy (`$SP/p2work/ax_all_examples.lean`).\n   - **Relation.**\n     - `ReprB` is decidable (fields lwf, inj, tokens, provTokens, live, init, freed, exited, leaked); `Repr` extends it with `wf2 : MM02.WF`.\n     - The ghost `provOf` is updated by `provStep`.\n   - **Simulation.** `SimRun`, `Oblig` (= `LayoutObl` ∧ `DecAlong` ∧ `FreeOblig`), `Params` fixed once, `Step3` envelope (L1 `NoOwner`, L2 one root).\n   - **L6 pointers.**\n     - `PtrEnc`, `PtrEncAt` (per pointer).\n     - `regionAddr`: head of the list, base + off.\n     - Provenance: `regionProv` for store; `arenaProv` for issue (allocation of the arena storage).\n     - `ArenasInv` is true on reached states via `reachable_access_invariant_underDD`.\n   - **Pitfalls.**\n     - Unquoted heredocs expand backticks: use `<<'EOF'` and pass paths through environment variables.\n     - `awk length` counts bytes.\n     - Anonymous constructors need explicit grouping for ∃.\n     - macOS `head` does not accept negative counts.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`formal/Ern/MM23.lean`** (about 4220 lines; 178 theorem declarations, 95 examples, 487 theorem constants of which 333 are non-internal, all within {propext, Quot.sound}).\n     - Module header updated to \"passes 1 and 2\", L1–L8, with both reports cited.\n     - `PtrEncAt pe addr prov := pe.decode (pe.enc addr prov) = addr ∧ ∀ i, (pe.enc addr prov i).2 = prov`.\n     - New issue definitions:\n       ```lean\n       def arenaProv (L : Layout) (s3 : S3) (i : Nat) : Option Nat :=\n         (s3.arenas[i]?).map fun ar => (L ((footprint s3.P ar.storage).headD ar.storage)).alloc\n       def issueBytes (pe) (s2) (L) (s3) (i) (region) := pe.enc (regionAddr s2 L region) (arenaProv L s3 i)\n       def issueOps (pe) (s2) (L) (s3) (i) (region) (dst) : List Op2 :=\n         [.write (leafAcc s2 L .write dst) (issueBytes pe s2 L s3 i region)]\n       ```\n       `assoc` now reads `| .issue i _ region dst, s3, s2 => issueOps π.pe s2 π.L s3 i region dst`.\n     - `issue_prov_storage` takes `(hwf : WF3 s3) (hlw : LayoutWF L s3 s2) (hai : ArenasInv s3) (h : IssueAt k i via region dst s3 (.ok s3')) (hl : l ∈ region)` and concludes `arenaProv L s3 i = some (L l).alloc ∧ ∃ ar, s3.arenas[i]? = some ar ∧ ∀ l' ∈ footprint s3.P ar.storage, (L l').alloc = (L l).alloc`. Proof: `exists_rootPlace`, `footprint_sub`, `hlw.sameAlloc`, `headD_mem_footprint`.\n     - `pointer_sound_store`:\n       - hypotheses: hwf, hnd, hfl, hR, a StoreStep, hstatW, hdec, `hl : head? = some l`, `hpe : PtrEncAt`;\n       - conclusion: decode, per-byte provenance, live allocation with `regionAddr` = base + off, and `rangeBytes`.\n     - `pointer_sound_issue`: the same, plus hypothesis `hai : ArenasInv s3` and the storage conclusion.\n     - `r6_issue` now uses `issueBytes` and `issueOps … s3 i …`.\n     - Docstrings fixed:\n       - `r6_transfer` (no `SameSizeAlong`);\n       - `simulation` (`SameSizeAlong` is not a hypothesis);\n       - `regionAddr` (\"need not be the first byte… pass-2 report, (e) 3\");\n       - `r6_issue` (`issueBytes`);\n       - `pointer_sound_*` (the range receives the first `(L p).len` bytes);\n       - all pass-2 citations now read \"pass-2 report, (e) N\".\n     - Instances added: `Decidable (NoOwner ls)` and `Decidable (LayoutObl π op s3 s3' s2)`.\n     - `namespace CaseSim` (at the end):\n       - Setup: `KS := KT [0] [] [1] [4] [(4, 7)]`; states x0..x18 (enter, write 1, alloc 1 0 lsA, write 0, newArena 4 4, derive 0 0 obs, derive 2 2 mod, pin 1, enter [5,6] lsE, issue 0 5 [5] 7, store 5 8, transfer 7 2, exit, endUse 2, reset 0 0, unpin 1, free 4 7, exit).\n       - Parameters: layout `L` (8-byte leaves, storage 4 with parts 5 at off 0 and 6 at off 8); `pe` (little-endian over 8 bytes); `π`; `pv0`, `pvA`; MM-02 states n0..n18; `Run`, `run0..run18`, `step10`, `step12`, `ob12`, `sim`, `inv` (whose conclusion now includes `ArenasInv`).\n       - Witnesses: issue decodes to 104 with provenance 4 (the storage); store decodes to 8 with provenance 0; `transfer_copies`; reset; holder of block 9; negative `ReprB`; `simulation_pinned`; empty-region issue (address 0, provenance 4); `x10e := splitEff x10 6 [[]]` then store 10 8 (address 0, provenance none); issue [6,5] → 112 versus 104, and `Lsw`; `L0` with leaf 8 of size 0 (`rangeBytes` = `some []`).\n   - **`formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md`** (French): verification state, main results, (a) to (f), and the \"Revue adverse\" section covering the first review plus the second and third checks.\n     - (e) has six questions:\n       1. L7 with zero-size leaves;\n       2. pointer of an empty region (issue, and store after split);\n       3. first leaf versus first byte;\n       4. size of the pointer target;\n       5. `SameSizeAlong` and kinds;\n       6. the form of `simulation`.\n     - (f) table: the L1 and L2 envelopes are classed « ouverte »; `ShapeOK` is not a remaining hypothesis.\n   - **Scratch and memory:**\n     - Log `$SP/mm23/log.md` has entries 19–35 for pass 2.\n     - The memory file `ern-formal-mm02-exploration.md` gained a pass-2 entry and lessons.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Unquoted heredoc** ran backticks in docstrings as shell commands. Fix: removed the damaged block and redid it with `<<'EOF'` and an environment-variable path.\n   - **`head -n -3` failed on macOS:** used Python instead.\n   - **`MM02` not resolved in scratch files:** added `open Ern`.\n   - **Missing decidability for `NoOwner` and `Oblig`:** added instances; `Oblig` is proved as `⟨by decide, by decide, trivial⟩`.\n   - **`UnpinPre` false:** added `ExternalDone 1` to `KS`.\n   - **Stale olean** (`pointer_sound_*` unknown in scratch): rebuilt the module.\n   - **`r6_issue` needed `(ObW := obW)`:** passed it explicitly.\n   - **Anonymous-constructor grouping for ∃:** wrote `⟨arS, h3, rfl, h3'⟩` explicitly.\n   - **Long lines:** reflowed, and verified line lengths in Python (characters, not bytes).\n   - **Review findings:** each round's wording errors were fixed (details in section 5).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **First review** (579808d): 11 findings, 9 confirmed, 2 refuted (L7-2, GEN-3). Fixed in fe0bd8c.\n     - L6-1: the provenance of an empty issue block. `issueOps` now uses `arenaProv`, as L6 states.\n     - L6-2: \"first leaf\" versus \"first byte\" is ambiguous, so it was reported as (e) 3 without changing the definition.\n     - L6-3: overclaiming docstrings fixed; question (e) 4 added.\n     - L6-4/SIM-1/GEN-1: the `r6_transfer` docstring no longer lists `SameSizeAlong`.\n     - L6-5: `issue_prov_storage` proved.\n     - L7-1: (e) 1 and (f) sharpened.\n     - GEN-2: module header updated.\n   - **Second check:** 11 findings, 10 confirmed; fixes went into docstrings and the report.\n   - **Third check:** 7 confirmed; fixes went into the report.\n   - **Final state at 278a42d:**\n     - `lake build` is clean, with no warnings.\n     - All 487 theorem constants are within {propext, Quot.sound}.\n     - The forbidden-word grep is empty.\n     - MM02 and MM03 are unchanged since 4e7cdbc.\n     - The working tree is clean.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Earlier (before the compactions): `/ub-mode`, the pass-1 brief and the pass-2 brief (pasted in French). Git rule verbatim: « Même branche `formal/refinement_0.1`, à la suite. Pas de merge, pas de PR. Tout sous `formal/`. `Ern/MM02.lean` et `Ern/MM03.lean` inchangés ; tout ajout va dans `Ern/MM23.lean` ou un module voisin. »\n   - No new user messages in this session. Every later turn was a system or task notification (workflow completions) or a system reminder, which are not user input.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Only the closing message to the user remains (`wrap_up` was already called and returned \"write it now\"). It should:\n     - report the ub-mode log (pass-2 entries 19–35);\n     - summarize the results and the six questions in (e);\n     - state that nothing was pushed, merged or opened as a PR.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Just committed 278a42d \"MM23 pass 2: second and third check fixes\", updated the log and the memory, and called `mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up`. Its recap: \"Pass 2 is complete on formal/refinement_0.1. All six steps, the review fixes and the report MM23_v0.1_p2.md are committed (last commit 278a42d). The build is clean and all theorems use only propext and Quot.sound. Six questions in report section (e) await arbitration; nothing was pushed or merged.\"\n   - The tool answered: \"Nothing is pending, so the app draws no box; the recap is the session's status. Your closing message is your answer to the user: write it now, as the last thing you say this turn.\"\n   - Commit chain: 9c08116 (1), cf09f12 (2), 837a192 (3), 5fd6d8a (4), 10b837c (5), 579808d (6), fe0bd8c (review fixes and report), 278a42d (second and third check fixes).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Write the final closing message, in English, to the user:\n     - point to the report [formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md](formal/reports/MM23_v0.1_p2.md);\n     - give the headline results: `simulation` proved with an 18-step witness; R6 covers every operation; `freeSound_derived`; `ddSound_of_layout` under a non-empty-range hypothesis because L7 is literally false; `pinned_address_stable`;\n     - list the six questions in (e);\n     - give the review rounds (11/9, 11/10, 7/7 confirmed);\n     - report the ub-mode log entries 19–35;\n     - note that nothing was pushed or merged, per « Pas de merge, pas de PR ».\n   - No further tool calls are needed.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/guygouri/.claude/projects/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"42d985ed-be40-46cc-b938-f137b63ff549","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:31:32.821Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":20,"turnIndex":54},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["7eafe96c-3b3c-4b36-b770-1b007ce8e182"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/refinement_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
