{"parentUuid":"9b77c2c8-1a14-425c-826f-48eace2239ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcbvRr9KwPP6HWimBW77","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018oqV1Evr38LQLdLmJACR4T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad; cat > $SP/j3/log.md <<'EOF'\n# Jalon 3 log (ub-mode)\n\n1. Created branch formal/validation_0.1 from formal/refinement_0.1 (brief: new draft branch).\n2. Read MM-03.3 v0.3 révisée in full, the jalon-3 material v2, and the kernel API of MM03.lean\n   (derive, split, release, transfer, store, enter/exit, endUse, free, alloc, arenas, Reachable)\n   to build the pool on kernel operations only.\n3. Design of HandlePool: pool entries outside S3 (kernel unchanged); slots = children of the\n   storage (kids), first free slot for allocSlot; resolve = derive companion (whole storage) +\n   derive entry; resolveMany = derive companion + split; unresolve = releases; freeSlot = endUse;\n   right check = companion's DerivePre (so H31a rejects whatever the handles). Extension PReach =\n   all kernel steps + pool ops, so pool ops are kernel step chains (PReach -> Reachable).\n4. Finding while designing: PoolInv clauses 2-3 are not preserved when the program can use the\n   companion (kernel derive from it onto a free entry) or through exitFrame re-anchoring.\nEOF\ncd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && grep -n 'theorem exitEff_eq\\|theorem exitG_active\\|theorem enter_lt\\|theorem addAuth_lt\\|theorem addAuth_self\\|theorem mem_descModes\\|theorem releaseEff_eq\\|theorem endUseS_get' Ern/MM03.lean","description":"Start the log and locate helper lemma names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4457,"cache_read_input_tokens":303767,"output_tokens":1306,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":552},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4457,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1306,"cache_read_input_tokens":303767,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4457},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018oqV1Evr38LQLdLmJACR4T":{"command":"SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad; cat > $SP/j3/log.md <<'EOF'\n# Jalon 3 log (ub-mode)\n\n1. Created branch formal/validation_0.1 from formal/refinement_0.1 (brief: new draft branch).\n2. Read MM-03.3 v0.3 révisée in full, the jalon-3 material v2, and the kernel API of MM03.lean\n   (derive, split, release, transfer, store, enter/exit, endUse, free, alloc, arenas, Reachable)\n   to build the pool on kernel operations only.\n3. Design of HandlePool: pool entries outside S3 (kernel unchanged); slots = children of the\n   storage (kids), first free slot for allocSlot; resolve = derive companion (whole storage) +\n   derive entry; resolveMany = derive companion + split; unresolve = releases; freeSlot = endUse;\n   right check = companion's DerivePre (so H31a rejects whatever the handles). Extension PReach =\n   all kernel steps + pool ops, so pool ops are kernel step chains (PReach -> Reachable).\n4. Finding while designing: PoolInv clauses 2-3 are not preserved when the program can use the\n   companion (kernel derive from it onto a free entry) or through exitFrame re-anchoring.\nEOF\ncd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && grep -n 'theorem exitEff_eq\\|theorem exitG_active\\|theorem enter_lt\\|theorem addAuth_lt\\|theorem addAuth_self\\|theorem mem_descModes\\|theorem releaseEff_eq\\|theorem endUseS_get' Ern/MM03.lean","description":"Start the log and locate helper lemma names"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5808e204-2a46-4ce2-a40d-a8ae90ffb74c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgcbvRa2kGQN7pABdsGZU","requestRef":"011e7528-6099-40ad-85f2-e412587a6bf9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6aa4607d-5c20-4018-b6ab-524112dab5f1","timestamp":"2026-11-01T17:28:50.542Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
