{"parentUuid":"560fb5b2-f30a-4dcb-bdea-434dd1d62970","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgcd2B3ggapacVdw2jxpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"HandlePool's theorems all compile—stale access, companion exclusivity, disjoint entries, atomicity, distinctness, fail lemmas, and the `Reachable` integration are all verified. Next I'll add an executable runner for building reached states, then work on the `PoolInv` counterexample.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":429971,"output_tokens":5252,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":101},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5252,"cache_read_input_tokens":429971,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"dda0afa3-feb3-4ca1-aa3a-11d5666fdc4e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgcd2AnZCP687CbaCrZsS","requestRef":"87111731-0c6e-49df-98e3-ed4d4fd21d36","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8724ead1-ae6b-4dfe-b95b-d39ac642bbff","timestamp":"2026-11-01T17:43:05.320Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"8724ead1-ae6b-4dfe-b95b-d39ac642bbff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgcd2B3ggapacVdw2jxpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q5KiXDFLa5gCWsW3SeSz6c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/HandlePool.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd=r'''\n/-! ## Executable steps\n\nA decidable step function for the extended machine, used by the case files to build reached\nstates: `prun` runs a list of operations and returns the final state when every step is `ok`\n(`prun_reach`). -/\n\n/-- An operation of the extended machine with its arguments: the steps of `Reachable`\n(MM-03.3 §3–6) and the pool operations (material §4). -/\ninductive Op where\n  | derive (src q : Nat) (m : Mode)\n  | split (src : Nat) (rs : List (List Nat))\n  | release (a : Nat)\n  | transfer (src dst : Nat)\n  | depend (q x : Nat)\n  | enter (ps : List Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n  | exit\n  | read (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n  | write (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n  | writeShared (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n  | pin (p : Nat)\n  | unpin (p : Nat)\n  | endUse (p : Nat)\n  | free (p auth : Nat)\n  | alloc (pr ow : Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n  | store (a p : Nat)\n  | newArena (st i : Nat)\n  | issue (i via : Nat) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat)\n  | reset (i via : Nat)\n  | newPool (st i : Nat)\n  | allocSlot (j via dst : Nat)\n  | resolve (j : Nat) (h : Handle) (m : Mode)\n  | resolveMany (j : Nat) (hs : List Handle) (m : Mode)\n  | unresolve (c : Nat)\n  | freeSlot (j via : Nat) (h : Handle)\n\nsection Exec\nvariable (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- `ok` outcome of a step of `Reachable` (MM-03.3 §3–6), `none` otherwise. -/\ndef kexec (s : S3) : Op → Option S3\n  | .derive src q m => if DerivePre s src q m then some (deriveEff s src q m) else none\n  | .split src rs => if SplitPre k s src rs then some (splitEff s src rs) else none\n  | .release a => if ReleasePre s a then some (releaseEff s a) else none\n  | .transfer src dst => if TransferPre k s src dst then some (transferEff s src dst) else none\n  | .depend q x => if DependPre s q x then some (dependEff s q x) else none\n  | .enter ps ls => if EnterPre s ps ls then some (enterEff s ps ls) else none\n  | .exit => if ExitPre k s then some (exitEff s) else none\n  | .read a ls => if canRead3 s a ls then some s else none\n  | .write a ls => if canWrite3 s a ls then some (write3Eff s ls) else none\n  | .writeShared a ls => if WriteSharedPre k s a ls then some (write3Eff s ls) else none\n  | .pin p => if PinPre s p then some (pinEff s p true) else none\n  | .unpin p => if UnpinPre k s p then some (pinEff s p false) else none\n  | .endUse p => if EndUsePre k s p then some (endUseEff s p) else none\n  | .free p auth => if FreePre k s p auth then some (freeEff s p) else none\n  | .alloc pr ow ls =>\n    if AllocStatic k s pr ow ls ∧ k.Satisfiable pr ls s then some (allocEff s pr ow ls) else none\n  | .store a p => if StorePre s a p then some (storeEff s a p) else none\n  | .newArena st i => if NewArenaPre s st i then some (newArenaEff s st i) else none\n  | .issue i via region dst =>\n    match s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar =>\n      if IssueStatic k s ar via region dst ∧ Avail ar region ∧ IssueRight s ar region ∧\n          AnchorOrderHeld (issueEff s ar region dst).1 then\n        some (arenaSet (issueEff s ar region dst).1 i (issueEff s ar region dst).2)\n      else none\n    | none => none\n  | .reset i via => if ResetAtPre k s i via then some (resetAtEff s i) else none\n  | _ => none\n\n/-- `ok` outcome of a step of the extended machine, `none` otherwise. -/\ndef pexec (ps : PS) : Op → Option PS\n  | .newPool st i => if NewPoolPre ps.s st i then some (newPoolEff ps st i) else none\n  | .allocSlot j via dst =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      if AllocSlotStatic k ps.s pl via dst then\n        match firstFree pl with\n        | some i => (pl.slots[i]?).map fun sl => allocSlotEff ps j pl i sl dst\n        | none => none\n      else none\n    | none => none\n  | .resolve j h m =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      match pl.slots[h.slot]? with\n      | some sl =>\n        if ResolveRight ps.s pl m ∧ HandleOK pl h ∧\n            DerivePre (deriveEff ps.s pl.internal pl.storage m) ps.s.A.length sl.place m then\n          some { ps with\n            s := resolveS ps.s pl sl.place m\n            res := ps.res ++ [⟨pl.id, pl.internal, ps.s.A.length, m,\n              [(ps.s.A.length + 1, h.slot, h.gen)]⟩] }\n        else none\n      | none => none\n    | none => none\n  | .resolveMany j hs m =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      if ResolveRight ps.s pl m ∧ BatchOK pl hs ∧\n          SplitPre k (deriveEff ps.s pl.internal pl.storage m) ps.s.A.length\n            (batchRegions ps.s pl hs) then\n        some { ps with\n          s := resolveManyS ps.s pl hs m\n          res := ps.res ++ [⟨pl.id, pl.internal, ps.s.A.length, m,\n            batchEntries ps.s.A.length hs⟩] }\n      else none\n    | none => none\n  | .unresolve c =>\n    match findRes ps c with\n    | some r => (releaseAll ps.s (r.entries.map (·.1) ++ [r.comp])).map fun s' => { ps with s := s' }\n    | none => none\n  | .freeSlot j via h =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      match pl.slots[h.slot]? with\n      | some sl =>\n        if PoolRight k ps.s pl via ∧ HandleCur pl h ∧ ¬ EntryBorrowed ps.s pl sl.place ∧\n            EndUsePre k ps.s sl.place then\n          some (freeSlotEff ps j pl h.slot sl)\n        else none\n      | none => none\n    | none => none\n  | o => (kexec k ps.s o).map fun s' => { ps with s := s' }\n\n/-- Runs a list of operations; `some` of the final state when every step is `ok`. -/\ndef prun (ps : PS) : List Op → Option PS\n  | [] => some ps\n  | o :: os => (pexec k ps o).bind fun ps' => prun ps' os\n\nend Exec\n\nsection ExecSound\nvariable {k : K} [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\ntheorem kexec_step {s s' : S3} {o : Op} (h : kexec k s o = some s') : Step k s s' := by\n  cases o <;> simp only [kexec] at h\n  all_goals first\n    | (split at h\n       · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n         first\n           | exact .kernel (.derive (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.split (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.release (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.transfer (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.depend (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.enter (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.exit (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.read (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.write (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.writeShared (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.pin (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.unpin (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.endUse (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.free (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.alloc (.ok hp.1 hp.2))\n           | exact .kernel (.store (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .newArena (Guarded.ok hp)\n           | exact .reset (Guarded.ok hp)\n       · cases h)\n    | cases h\n    | (split at h\n       · rename_i ar har\n         split at h\n         · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n           exact .issue (.ok har (.ok hp.1 hp.2.1 hp.2.2.1 hp.2.2.2))\n         · cases h\n       · cases h)\n\ntheorem pexec_step {ps ps' : PS} {o : Op} (h : pexec k ps o = some ps') : PStep k ps ps' := by\n  cases o\n  case newPool st i =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h; split at h\n    · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h; exact .newPool (Guarded.ok hp)\n    · cases h\n  case allocSlot j via dst =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i hst\n        split at h\n        · rename_i i hi\n          cases hsl : pl.slots[i]? with\n          | none => rw [hsl] at h; cases h\n          | some sl =>\n            rw [hsl] at h; simp only [Option.map_some, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n            exact .allocSlot (.ok hpl hst hi hsl)\n        · cases h\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  case resolve j hd m =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i sl hsl\n        split at h\n        · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n          exact .resolve (.ok hpl hp.1 hp.2.1 hsl hp.2.2)\n        · cases h\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  case resolveMany j hs m =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n        exact .resolveMany (.ok hpl hp.1 hp.2.1 hp.2.2)\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  case unresolve c =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i r hr\n      cases hs : releaseAll ps.s (r.entries.map (·.1) ++ [r.comp]) with\n      | none => rw [hs] at h; cases h\n      | some s' =>\n        rw [hs] at h; simp only [Option.map_some, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n        exact .unresolve (.ok hr hs)\n    · cases h\n  case freeSlot j via hd =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i sl hsl\n        split at h\n        · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n          exact .freeSlot (.ok hpl hp.1 hp.2.1 hsl hp.2.2.1 hp.2.2.2)\n        · cases h\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  all_goals\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    cases hk : kexec k ps.s _ with\n    | none => rw [hk] at h; cases h\n    | some s' =>\n      rw [hk] at h; simp only [Option.map_some, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n      exact .kernel (kexec_step hk)\n\ntheorem prun_reach {statics : Statics} : ∀ {ps ps' : PS} {os : List Op}, PReach k statics ps →\n    prun k ps os = some ps' → PReach k statics ps'\n  | _, _, [], hr, h => by simp only [prun, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h; exact hr\n  | ps, ps', o :: os, hr, h => by\n    simp only [prun] at h\n    cases he : pexec k ps o with\n    | none => rw [he] at h; cases h\n    | some ps₁ => rw [he] at h; exact prun_reach (.step hr (pexec_step he)) h\n\n/-- A run from the initial state that succeeds reaches its final state. -/\ntheorem prun_init {statics : Statics} {os : List Op} {ps' : PS}\n    (hsh : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1))) (h : prun k (PS.init statics) os = some ps') :\n    PReach k statics ps' :=\n  prun_reach (.init hsh) h\n\nend ExecSound\n\n'''\ns=s.replace('\\nend Ern.HandlePool\\n', add+'end Ern.HandlePool\\n')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ntime ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/HandlePool.lean 2>&1 | grep -v '^\\s' | head -30","description":"Add executable runner with soundness proofs","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":429971,"output_tokens":5252,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":101},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5252,"cache_read_input_tokens":429971,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":454},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Q5KiXDFLa5gCWsW3SeSz6c":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='Ern/HandlePool.lean'\ns=open(p).read()\nadd=r'''\n/-! ## Executable steps\n\nA decidable step function for the extended machine, used by the case files to build reached\nstates: `prun` runs a list of operations and returns the final state when every step is `ok`\n(`prun_reach`). -/\n\n/-- An operation of the extended machine with its arguments: the steps of `Reachable`\n(MM-03.3 §3–6) and the pool operations (material §4). -/\ninductive Op where\n  | derive (src q : Nat) (m : Mode)\n  | split (src : Nat) (rs : List (List Nat))\n  | release (a : Nat)\n  | transfer (src dst : Nat)\n  | depend (q x : Nat)\n  | enter (ps : List Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n  | exit\n  | read (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n  | write (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n  | writeShared (a : Nat) (ls : List Nat)\n  | pin (p : Nat)\n  | unpin (p : Nat)\n  | endUse (p : Nat)\n  | free (p auth : Nat)\n  | alloc (pr ow : Nat) (ls : List (Option Nat × Option Nat × Nat))\n  | store (a p : Nat)\n  | newArena (st i : Nat)\n  | issue (i via : Nat) (region : List Nat) (dst : Nat)\n  | reset (i via : Nat)\n  | newPool (st i : Nat)\n  | allocSlot (j via dst : Nat)\n  | resolve (j : Nat) (h : Handle) (m : Mode)\n  | resolveMany (j : Nat) (hs : List Handle) (m : Mode)\n  | unresolve (c : Nat)\n  | freeSlot (j via : Nat) (h : Handle)\n\nsection Exec\nvariable (k : K) [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\n/-- `ok` outcome of a step of `Reachable` (MM-03.3 §3–6), `none` otherwise. -/\ndef kexec (s : S3) : Op → Option S3\n  | .derive src q m => if DerivePre s src q m then some (deriveEff s src q m) else none\n  | .split src rs => if SplitPre k s src rs then some (splitEff s src rs) else none\n  | .release a => if ReleasePre s a then some (releaseEff s a) else none\n  | .transfer src dst => if TransferPre k s src dst then some (transferEff s src dst) else none\n  | .depend q x => if DependPre s q x then some (dependEff s q x) else none\n  | .enter ps ls => if EnterPre s ps ls then some (enterEff s ps ls) else none\n  | .exit => if ExitPre k s then some (exitEff s) else none\n  | .read a ls => if canRead3 s a ls then some s else none\n  | .write a ls => if canWrite3 s a ls then some (write3Eff s ls) else none\n  | .writeShared a ls => if WriteSharedPre k s a ls then some (write3Eff s ls) else none\n  | .pin p => if PinPre s p then some (pinEff s p true) else none\n  | .unpin p => if UnpinPre k s p then some (pinEff s p false) else none\n  | .endUse p => if EndUsePre k s p then some (endUseEff s p) else none\n  | .free p auth => if FreePre k s p auth then some (freeEff s p) else none\n  | .alloc pr ow ls =>\n    if AllocStatic k s pr ow ls ∧ k.Satisfiable pr ls s then some (allocEff s pr ow ls) else none\n  | .store a p => if StorePre s a p then some (storeEff s a p) else none\n  | .newArena st i => if NewArenaPre s st i then some (newArenaEff s st i) else none\n  | .issue i via region dst =>\n    match s.arenas[i]? with\n    | some ar =>\n      if IssueStatic k s ar via region dst ∧ Avail ar region ∧ IssueRight s ar region ∧\n          AnchorOrderHeld (issueEff s ar region dst).1 then\n        some (arenaSet (issueEff s ar region dst).1 i (issueEff s ar region dst).2)\n      else none\n    | none => none\n  | .reset i via => if ResetAtPre k s i via then some (resetAtEff s i) else none\n  | _ => none\n\n/-- `ok` outcome of a step of the extended machine, `none` otherwise. -/\ndef pexec (ps : PS) : Op → Option PS\n  | .newPool st i => if NewPoolPre ps.s st i then some (newPoolEff ps st i) else none\n  | .allocSlot j via dst =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      if AllocSlotStatic k ps.s pl via dst then\n        match firstFree pl with\n        | some i => (pl.slots[i]?).map fun sl => allocSlotEff ps j pl i sl dst\n        | none => none\n      else none\n    | none => none\n  | .resolve j h m =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      match pl.slots[h.slot]? with\n      | some sl =>\n        if ResolveRight ps.s pl m ∧ HandleOK pl h ∧\n            DerivePre (deriveEff ps.s pl.internal pl.storage m) ps.s.A.length sl.place m then\n          some { ps with\n            s := resolveS ps.s pl sl.place m\n            res := ps.res ++ [⟨pl.id, pl.internal, ps.s.A.length, m,\n              [(ps.s.A.length + 1, h.slot, h.gen)]⟩] }\n        else none\n      | none => none\n    | none => none\n  | .resolveMany j hs m =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      if ResolveRight ps.s pl m ∧ BatchOK pl hs ∧\n          SplitPre k (deriveEff ps.s pl.internal pl.storage m) ps.s.A.length\n            (batchRegions ps.s pl hs) then\n        some { ps with\n          s := resolveManyS ps.s pl hs m\n          res := ps.res ++ [⟨pl.id, pl.internal, ps.s.A.length, m,\n            batchEntries ps.s.A.length hs⟩] }\n      else none\n    | none => none\n  | .unresolve c =>\n    match findRes ps c with\n    | some r => (releaseAll ps.s (r.entries.map (·.1) ++ [r.comp])).map fun s' => { ps with s := s' }\n    | none => none\n  | .freeSlot j via h =>\n    match ps.pools[j]? with\n    | some pl =>\n      match pl.slots[h.slot]? with\n      | some sl =>\n        if PoolRight k ps.s pl via ∧ HandleCur pl h ∧ ¬ EntryBorrowed ps.s pl sl.place ∧\n            EndUsePre k ps.s sl.place then\n          some (freeSlotEff ps j pl h.slot sl)\n        else none\n      | none => none\n    | none => none\n  | o => (kexec k ps.s o).map fun s' => { ps with s := s' }\n\n/-- Runs a list of operations; `some` of the final state when every step is `ok`. -/\ndef prun (ps : PS) : List Op → Option PS\n  | [] => some ps\n  | o :: os => (pexec k ps o).bind fun ps' => prun ps' os\n\nend Exec\n\nsection ExecSound\nvariable {k : K} [∀ r r', Decidable (k.DeclaredDisjoint r r')] [DecidablePred k.SharedMutable]\n  [DecidablePred k.Pinned] [DecidablePred k.ExternalDone] [DecidablePred k.Deallocable]\n  [∀ p a, Decidable (k.FreeCompat p a)] [∀ p ls s, Decidable (k.Satisfiable p ls s)]\n\ntheorem kexec_step {s s' : S3} {o : Op} (h : kexec k s o = some s') : Step k s s' := by\n  cases o <;> simp only [kexec] at h\n  all_goals first\n    | (split at h\n       · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n         first\n           | exact .kernel (.derive (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.split (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.release (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.transfer (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.depend (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.enter (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.exit (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.read (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.write (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.writeShared (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.pin (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.unpin (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.endUse (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.free (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .kernel (.alloc (.ok hp.1 hp.2))\n           | exact .kernel (.store (Guarded.ok hp))\n           | exact .newArena (Guarded.ok hp)\n           | exact .reset (Guarded.ok hp)\n       · cases h)\n    | cases h\n    | (split at h\n       · rename_i ar har\n         split at h\n         · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n           exact .issue (.ok har (.ok hp.1 hp.2.1 hp.2.2.1 hp.2.2.2))\n         · cases h\n       · cases h)\n\ntheorem pexec_step {ps ps' : PS} {o : Op} (h : pexec k ps o = some ps') : PStep k ps ps' := by\n  cases o\n  case newPool st i =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h; split at h\n    · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h; exact .newPool (Guarded.ok hp)\n    · cases h\n  case allocSlot j via dst =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i hst\n        split at h\n        · rename_i i hi\n          cases hsl : pl.slots[i]? with\n          | none => rw [hsl] at h; cases h\n          | some sl =>\n            rw [hsl] at h; simp only [Option.map_some, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n            exact .allocSlot (.ok hpl hst hi hsl)\n        · cases h\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  case resolve j hd m =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i sl hsl\n        split at h\n        · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n          exact .resolve (.ok hpl hp.1 hp.2.1 hsl hp.2.2)\n        · cases h\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  case resolveMany j hs m =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n        exact .resolveMany (.ok hpl hp.1 hp.2.1 hp.2.2)\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  case unresolve c =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i r hr\n      cases hs : releaseAll ps.s (r.entries.map (·.1) ++ [r.comp]) with\n      | none => rw [hs] at h; cases h\n      | some s' =>\n        rw [hs] at h; simp only [Option.map_some, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n        exact .unresolve (.ok hr hs)\n    · cases h\n  case freeSlot j via hd =>\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    split at h\n    · rename_i pl hpl\n      split at h\n      · rename_i sl hsl\n        split at h\n        · rename_i hp; simp only [Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n          exact .freeSlot (.ok hpl hp.1 hp.2.1 hsl hp.2.2.1 hp.2.2.2)\n        · cases h\n      · cases h\n    · cases h\n  all_goals\n    simp only [pexec] at h\n    cases hk : kexec k ps.s _ with\n    | none => rw [hk] at h; cases h\n    | some s' =>\n      rw [hk] at h; simp only [Option.map_some, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h\n      exact .kernel (kexec_step hk)\n\ntheorem prun_reach {statics : Statics} : ∀ {ps ps' : PS} {os : List Op}, PReach k statics ps →\n    prun k ps os = some ps' → PReach k statics ps'\n  | _, _, [], hr, h => by simp only [prun, Option.some.injEq] at h; subst h; exact hr\n  | ps, ps', o :: os, hr, h => by\n    simp only [prun] at h\n    cases he : pexec k ps o with\n    | none => rw [he] at h; cases h\n    | some ps₁ => rw [he] at h; exact prun_reach (.step hr (pexec_step he)) h\n\n/-- A run from the initial state that succeeds reaches its final state. -/\ntheorem prun_init {statics : Statics} {os : List Op} {ps' : PS}\n    (hsh : ShapeOK 0 (statics.map (·.1))) (h : prun k (PS.init statics) os = some ps') :\n    PReach k statics ps' :=\n  prun_reach (.init hsh) h\n\nend ExecSound\n\n'''\ns=s.replace('\\nend Ern.HandlePool\\n', add+'end Ern.HandlePool\\n')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ntime ~/.elan/bin/lake env lean Ern/HandlePool.lean 2>&1 | grep -v '^\\s' | head -30","description":"Add executable runner with soundness proofs","timeout":600000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Q5KiXDFLa5gCWsW3SeSz6c":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dda0afa3-feb3-4ca1-aa3a-11d5666fdc4e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgcd2AnZCP687CbaCrZsS","requestRef":"87111731-0c6e-49df-98e3-ed4d4fd21d36","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fa9d98d-686d-4128-be8a-f22dc80d1108","timestamp":"2026-11-01T17:43:38.082Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern/formal","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
