{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","hash":"651fb92d14f5f03ed3fdf43db9f4587f9cea846a985768380d935f55effa96a7","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017K5DzWoqpajWziXKZ9pbaB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern && git status --short && git add formal/Ern/HandlePool.lean && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nJ3 step 1: handle pool built on kernel operations\n\nWhy: jalon-3 material §4 asks for a handle pool whose exclusivity follows\nfrom the kernel rules (I1, O3.2), integrated with Reachable without\nchanging the kernel.\n\nWhat: new module Ern.HandlePool. Pool entries live beside S3; newPool\nreuses the newArena preconditions; resolve is derive (companion on the\nwhole storage) then derive (entry), resolveMany is derive then split,\nunresolve a sequence of release, freeSlot an endUse of the entry, and\nallocSlot a write3 of the handle. PReach extends Reachable with these\nsteps; every pool step is a chain of kernel steps (pReach_reachable).\nProved on every reached state under DDSound: pool_no_stale_access,\npool_resolve_modify_exclusive (whatever the sequence of steps),\npool_entries_disjoint; and pool_resolve_stale_fails,\npool_resolve_other_pool_fails, pool_resolveMany_atomic,\npool_resolveMany_distinct, pool_freeSlot_ends_content. PoolInv read\nliterally is not preserved: pool_inv_not_preserved (derive from the\ncompanion onto a free entry) and pool_inv_cex_entry (derive from the\nentry authority; re-anchoring at exitFrame), kept as counterexamples.\nAn executable runner (prun) with soundness proofs builds reached states\nfor the case files.\n\nProof: lake build succeeds without warnings; all 734 constants of the\nmodule depend only on propext and Quot.sound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit step 1 (HandlePool)","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
