","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
{"parentUuid":"140dde0a-42cc-49cc-b5f7-a8641ddb1c14","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d8867bcf-fa69-4463-9401-ce9d6d53950a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HDucsQnjKHaRGdhPBqRQvs","type":"tool_result","content":"/-- `alloc`, `process`, `free` at the end of the frame (`defer`), then `endUse` (expected:\n`ok`); `free` during an active access, without a compatible deallocation authority, or of an\narena block (expected: reject). Frame 1: 0 box value, 1 allocator value; in the middle of the\nframe, `alloc` with provider 1 and owner 0 creates the storage 2, owned by 0, with root 2 (B5). -/\nabbrev KF : K := KT [] [] [] [2] [(2, 7)]\ndef n6e : S3 := enter1 [(none, none, 0), (none, none, 0)]\ndef n6a : S3 := write3Eff (allocEff (write3Eff n6e [1]) 1 0 [(none, none, 0)]) [2]\nexample : Write3Step 1 [1] n6e (.ok (write3Eff n6e [1])) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : AllocStep KF 1 0 [(none, none, 0)] (write3Eff n6e [1]) (.ok (allocEff (write3Eff n6e [1]) 1 0 [(none, none, 0)])) :=\n  .ok (by decide) (by decide)\nexample : Write3Step 2 [2] (allocEff (write3Eff n6e [1]) 1 0 [(none, none, 0)]) (.ok n6a) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep KF 2 7 n6a (.ok (freeEff n6a 2)) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : EndUseStep KF 0 (freeEff n6a 2) (.ok (endUseEff (freeEff n6a 2) 0)) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep KF 2 7 (deriveEff n6a 2 2 .observe) .reject := .reject (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep KF 2 8 n6a .reject := .reject (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep (KT [0] [] [] [1] [(2, 7)]) 2 7 c6b.1 .reject := .reject (by decide)\n\n/-- `endUse` of a value whose owned storage was not freed (expected: `ok`, reported as a leak):\nthe storage is logically dead and not freed. -/\nexample : EndUseStep KF 0 n6a (.ok (endUseEff n6a 0)) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : (endUseEff n6a 0).dead 2 = true ∧ (endUseEff n6a 0).freed 2 = false := by decide\n\n/-- Two incompatible ordinary `Modify` authorities on a `SharedMutable` leaf (expected: reject);\ntwo observations and a `writeShared` within the contract (expected: `ok`). -/\nexample : DeriveStep 0 0 .modify (deriveEff (enter1 [(none, none, 0)]) 0 0 .modify) .reject :=\n  .reject (by decide)\nexample : WriteSharedStep KA 1 [0] c1c (.ok (write3Eff c1c [0])) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : WriteSharedStep K0 1 [0] c1c .reject := .reject (by decide)\n\n/-- Return of a value anchored on a derivation of a derivation of a parameter (expected: `ok`).\nCallee of case 8: 5 derived from parameter 2, 6 derived from 5; the value depends on 6. -/\n\n/-- Twin of `lb5_escape_rejected` (G4): the arena of case 16, whose storage is owned by the\ncaller's value 0; the callee issues the block 7 to its local 6, then transfers 6 to the caller's\nbuffer 2 and exits (expected and obtained: `ok` at each step). -/\ntheorem lb5_twin : TransferStep KA 6 2 a7 (.ok a8) ∧ ExitStep KA a8 (.ok a9) ∧ Reachable KA [] a11 :=\n  ⟨.ok (by decide), .ok (by decide), case16_reachable.1⟩\n\n/-- `issue` of a block of the callee's local arena to a value of the caller (G4). Frame 1: 0 the\nresult; it derives 1, `Modify` on 0, and calls with `[1]`. Frame 2: 1 arena value, 2 allocator\nvalue, 3 a local; `alloc` gives the storage 4, with the part 5, owned by 1, of root 5;\n`newArena 4 5`. The `issue` of `[5]` to the caller's value 0 is rejected (expected and\nobtained: reject) by the clause of arrival of G4 alone: the block would be held by a place of\nframe 1, its effective anchor, the root 5, being of frame 2. The same `issue` to the local 3 is\naccepted (twin, `ok`). -/\ndef ci0 : S3 := enterEff (deriveEff (enter1 [(none, none, 0)]) 0 0 .modify) [1]\n  [(none, none, 0), (none, none, 0), (none, none, 0)]\ndef ci1 : S3 := allocEff (write3Eff ci0 [2]) 2 1 [(none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)]\n/-- J1: the arena value is written before `newArena`. -/\ndef ci1w : S3 := write3Eff ci1 [1]\ndef ci2 : S3 := newArenaEff ci1w 4 5\ndef arCi : Arena := ⟨4, 5, [5], []⟩\ntheorem callee_issue_to_caller :\n    Reachable K0 [] ci2 ∧ ci2.arenas = [arCi] ∧ IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 0 ci2 .reject ∧\n      IssueStatic K0 ci2 arCi 0 [5] 0 ∧ Avail arCi [5] ∧ IssueRight ci2 arCi [5] ∧\n      ¬ AnchorOrderHeld (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 0).1 ∧\n      IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 3 ci2 (.ok (arenaSet (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).1 0\n        (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2)) := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] ci0 := .enter (.derive (.enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide)))\n    (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] ci1 := .alloc (.write r0 (show Write3Step 3 [2] ci0 (.ok _) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show AllocStep K0 2 1 [(none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)] _ (.ok ci1) from\n      .ok (by decide) trivial)\n  have r2 : Reachable K0 [] ci2 := .newArena (.write r1 (show Write3Step 2 [1] ci1 (.ok ci1w) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show NewArenaStep 4 5 ci1w (.ok ci2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  exact ⟨r2, by decide, .reject (ar := arCi) (by decide)\n    (.noAnchor (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)), by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    by decide, .ok (ar := arCi) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide))⟩\n\n/-- G4 is checked on the arrival state of an `issue` that succeeds only (MM-03.3 §6; A10): after\nthe block on `[5]` is issued to the local 3, the same `issue` to the caller's value 0 finds the\nregion unavailable and fails, the state unchanged, as in pass 6, although its arrival state would\nbreak `AnchorOrderHeld`. -/\ndef ci3 : S3 := arenaSet (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).1 0 (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2\ntheorem callee_issue_unavailable_fails :\n    Reachable K0 [] ci3 ∧ IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 0 ci3 (.fail ci3) ∧\n      ¬ AnchorOrderHeld (issueEff ci3 (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2 [5] 0).1 := by\n  have r2 := callee_issue_to_caller.1\n  exact ⟨.issue r2 callee_issue_to_caller.2.2.2.2.2.2.2,\n    .fail (ar := (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2) (by decide) (.fail (by decide) (by decide)), by decide⟩\n\n/-! ### Held authorities that no frame can exercise (G3) -/\n\n/-- No authority is held by the base frame 0 (G3 witnesses): with the stack `[1, 0]`, only the\ncurrent frame can exercise anything. -/\ndef NothingAtFrame0 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun y => y.holder ≠ .frame 0) True\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (NothingAtFrame0 s) := by unfold NothingAtFrame0; infer_instance\n\n\n/-- `NoOrphan` (G3) holds on every reached state, but it does not make a held authority\nexercisable: `transfer` builds an active authority held by the place it covers, which no frame\ncan exercise. Frame 1: structure 0 with the field 1, structure 2 with the field 3; roots 0 (on 1)\nand 1 (on 3). The frame derives 2, `Modify` on 3, stores it into the field 1 (`ok`), then transfers\n0 into 2 (`ok`): by J1, 2 passes to the corresponding field 3, which it covers. Its origin, the root\n1, has no effective mode on 3, so 2 is exercisable at no mode, the frame has no `Modify` on the\nstructure 2 nor on its field 3, and `release` of 2 and `endUse` of 2 are rejected; the exit of\nframe 1 releases 2. The chain of G3 is the root 1, held by frame 1, then 2. Pass 7 transferred into\na leaf, which J1 rejects (shape). -/\ndef hu0 : S3 := storeEff (deriveEff (enter1 [(none, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0), (none, none, 0),\n  (some 2, none, 0)]) 1 2 .modify) 2 1\ndef hu1 : S3 := transferEff hu0 0 2\ntheorem held_unexercisable_by_transfer :\n    Reachable K0 [] hu1 ∧ (hu1.A[2]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder, y.footprint)) =\n      some (true, .place 3, [3]) ∧ ¬ hu1.ExercisableAt 2 .observe ∧ ¬ HasRight hu1 .modify 2 ∧\n      ¬ HasRight hu1 .modify 3 ∧\n      ReleaseStep 2 hu1 .reject ∧ EndUseStep K0 2 hu1 .reject ∧ NoOrphan hu1 ∧\n      ExitStep K0 hu1 (.ok (exitEff hu1)) ∧ ¬ (exitEff hu1).Active 2 ∧ NothingAtFrame0 hu1 := by\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] hu1 := .transfer (.store (.derive (.enter (.init (by decide))\n    (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))\n  exact ⟨r, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), .reject (by decide),\n    reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r, .ok (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- The same through `issue` (G3; A10): from `fa2` (arena value 0, storage 4 with the nodes 5 and\n6, `internal` 4 held by 0), the block on the node 5 is issued to the node 5 itself (`ok`): the block\nis held by the place it covers, its origin `internal` 4 has no effective mode there, and the\nblock is exercisable at no mode. -/\ndef iu1 : S3 := arenaSet (issueEff fa2 arFa [5] 5).1 0 (issueEff fa2 arFa [5] 5).2\ntheorem held_unexercisable_by_issue :\n    Reachable K0 [] iu1 ∧ (iu1.A[5]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder, y.footprint)) =\n      some (true, .place 5, [5]) ∧ ¬ iu1.ExercisableAt 5 .observe ∧ NoOrphan iu1 ∧\n      NothingAtFrame0 iu1 := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] fa0 := .enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] fa1 := .alloc (.write r0 (show Write3Step 1 [1] fa0 (.ok _) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show AllocStep K0 1 0 [(none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)]\n      _ (.ok fa1) from .ok (by decide) trivial)\n  have r2 : Reachable K0 [] fa2 := .newArena (.write r1 (show Write3Step 0 [0] fa1 (.ok fa1w) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show NewArenaStep 4 4 fa1w (.ok fa2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] iu1 := .issue r2 (show IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 5 fa2 (.ok iu1) from\n    .ok (ar := arFa) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)))\n  exact ⟨r, by decide, by decide, reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ### Leaves made `Init` without a write (G2; review of pass 7; J1) -/\n\n/-- Pass 7 reached, through `transfer`, the configuration G2 rejects for `store`: a reference held\nby a whole structure, whose `length` field becomes `Init` without a write. J1 rejects that\ntransfer: the destination has another shape than the source. Frame 1: structure 0 with the fields\n1 (`ptr`) and 2 (`length`), the buffer 3, the leaves 4 and 5. The frame derives 4, `Modify` on 3,\nand stores it into the leaf 4. The transfer of 4 into the structure 0 is rejected (J1, shape).\nTwin: the transfer of 4 into the leaf 5, of the same shape, is accepted, 4 passing to 5, which is\nthen read. -/","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2ecffd14-84eb-4e93-8a68-67cdb85b8bd9","timestamp":"2026-11-01T17:49:45.770Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/-- `alloc`, `process`, `free` at the end of the frame (`defer`), then `endUse` (expected:\n`ok`); `free` during an active access, without a compatible deallocation authority, or of an\narena block (expected: reject). Frame 1: 0 box value, 1 allocator value; in the middle of the\nframe, `alloc` with provider 1 and owner 0 creates the storage 2, owned by 0, with root 2 (B5). -/\nabbrev KF : K := KT [] [] [] [2] [(2, 7)]\ndef n6e : S3 := enter1 [(none, none, 0), (none, none, 0)]\ndef n6a : S3 := write3Eff (allocEff (write3Eff n6e [1]) 1 0 [(none, none, 0)]) [2]\nexample : Write3Step 1 [1] n6e (.ok (write3Eff n6e [1])) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : AllocStep KF 1 0 [(none, none, 0)] (write3Eff n6e [1]) (.ok (allocEff (write3Eff n6e [1]) 1 0 [(none, none, 0)])) :=\n  .ok (by decide) (by decide)\nexample : Write3Step 2 [2] (allocEff (write3Eff n6e [1]) 1 0 [(none, none, 0)]) (.ok n6a) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep KF 2 7 n6a (.ok (freeEff n6a 2)) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : EndUseStep KF 0 (freeEff n6a 2) (.ok (endUseEff (freeEff n6a 2) 0)) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep KF 2 7 (deriveEff n6a 2 2 .observe) .reject := .reject (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep KF 2 8 n6a .reject := .reject (by decide)\nexample : FreeStep (KT [0] [] [] [1] [(2, 7)]) 2 7 c6b.1 .reject := .reject (by decide)\n\n/-- `endUse` of a value whose owned storage was not freed (expected: `ok`, reported as a leak):\nthe storage is logically dead and not freed. -/\nexample : EndUseStep KF 0 n6a (.ok (endUseEff n6a 0)) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : (endUseEff n6a 0).dead 2 = true ∧ (endUseEff n6a 0).freed 2 = false := by decide\n\n/-- Two incompatible ordinary `Modify` authorities on a `SharedMutable` leaf (expected: reject);\ntwo observations and a `writeShared` within the contract (expected: `ok`). -/\nexample : DeriveStep 0 0 .modify (deriveEff (enter1 [(none, none, 0)]) 0 0 .modify) .reject :=\n  .reject (by decide)\nexample : WriteSharedStep KA 1 [0] c1c (.ok (write3Eff c1c [0])) := .ok (by decide)\nexample : WriteSharedStep K0 1 [0] c1c .reject := .reject (by decide)\n\n/-- Return of a value anchored on a derivation of a derivation of a parameter (expected: `ok`).\nCallee of case 8: 5 derived from parameter 2, 6 derived from 5; the value depends on 6. -/\n\n/-- Twin of `lb5_escape_rejected` (G4): the arena of case 16, whose storage is owned by the\ncaller's value 0; the callee issues the block 7 to its local 6, then transfers 6 to the caller's\nbuffer 2 and exits (expected and obtained: `ok` at each step). -/\ntheorem lb5_twin : TransferStep KA 6 2 a7 (.ok a8) ∧ ExitStep KA a8 (.ok a9) ∧ Reachable KA [] a11 :=\n  ⟨.ok (by decide), .ok (by decide), case16_reachable.1⟩\n\n/-- `issue` of a block of the callee's local arena to a value of the caller (G4). Frame 1: 0 the\nresult; it derives 1, `Modify` on 0, and calls with `[1]`. Frame 2: 1 arena value, 2 allocator\nvalue, 3 a local; `alloc` gives the storage 4, with the part 5, owned by 1, of root 5;\n`newArena 4 5`. The `issue` of `[5]` to the caller's value 0 is rejected (expected and\nobtained: reject) by the clause of arrival of G4 alone: the block would be held by a place of\nframe 1, its effective anchor, the root 5, being of frame 2. The same `issue` to the local 3 is\naccepted (twin, `ok`). -/\ndef ci0 : S3 := enterEff (deriveEff (enter1 [(none, none, 0)]) 0 0 .modify) [1]\n  [(none, none, 0), (none, none, 0), (none, none, 0)]\ndef ci1 : S3 := allocEff (write3Eff ci0 [2]) 2 1 [(none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)]\n/-- J1: the arena value is written before `newArena`. -/\ndef ci1w : S3 := write3Eff ci1 [1]\ndef ci2 : S3 := newArenaEff ci1w 4 5\ndef arCi : Arena := ⟨4, 5, [5], []⟩\ntheorem callee_issue_to_caller :\n    Reachable K0 [] ci2 ∧ ci2.arenas = [arCi] ∧ IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 0 ci2 .reject ∧\n      IssueStatic K0 ci2 arCi 0 [5] 0 ∧ Avail arCi [5] ∧ IssueRight ci2 arCi [5] ∧\n      ¬ AnchorOrderHeld (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 0).1 ∧\n      IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 3 ci2 (.ok (arenaSet (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).1 0\n        (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2)) := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] ci0 := .enter (.derive (.enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide)))\n    (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] ci1 := .alloc (.write r0 (show Write3Step 3 [2] ci0 (.ok _) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show AllocStep K0 2 1 [(none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)] _ (.ok ci1) from\n      .ok (by decide) trivial)\n  have r2 : Reachable K0 [] ci2 := .newArena (.write r1 (show Write3Step 2 [1] ci1 (.ok ci1w) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show NewArenaStep 4 5 ci1w (.ok ci2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  exact ⟨r2, by decide, .reject (ar := arCi) (by decide)\n    (.noAnchor (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)), by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    by decide, .ok (ar := arCi) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide))⟩\n\n/-- G4 is checked on the arrival state of an `issue` that succeeds only (MM-03.3 §6; A10): after\nthe block on `[5]` is issued to the local 3, the same `issue` to the caller's value 0 finds the\nregion unavailable and fails, the state unchanged, as in pass 6, although its arrival state would\nbreak `AnchorOrderHeld`. -/\ndef ci3 : S3 := arenaSet (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).1 0 (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2\ntheorem callee_issue_unavailable_fails :\n    Reachable K0 [] ci3 ∧ IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 0 ci3 (.fail ci3) ∧\n      ¬ AnchorOrderHeld (issueEff ci3 (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2 [5] 0).1 := by\n  have r2 := callee_issue_to_caller.1\n  exact ⟨.issue r2 callee_issue_to_caller.2.2.2.2.2.2.2,\n    .fail (ar := (issueEff ci2 arCi [5] 3).2) (by decide) (.fail (by decide) (by decide)), by decide⟩\n\n/-! ### Held authorities that no frame can exercise (G3) -/\n\n/-- No authority is held by the base frame 0 (G3 witnesses): with the stack `[1, 0]`, only the\ncurrent frame can exercise anything. -/\ndef NothingAtFrame0 (s : S3) : Prop :=\n  ∀ j ∈ List.range s.A.length, OptP (s.A[j]?) (fun y => y.holder ≠ .frame 0) True\n\ninstance (s : S3) : Decidable (NothingAtFrame0 s) := by unfold NothingAtFrame0; infer_instance\n\n\n/-- `NoOrphan` (G3) holds on every reached state, but it does not make a held authority\nexercisable: `transfer` builds an active authority held by the place it covers, which no frame\ncan exercise. Frame 1: structure 0 with the field 1, structure 2 with the field 3; roots 0 (on 1)\nand 1 (on 3). The frame derives 2, `Modify` on 3, stores it into the field 1 (`ok`), then transfers\n0 into 2 (`ok`): by J1, 2 passes to the corresponding field 3, which it covers. Its origin, the root\n1, has no effective mode on 3, so 2 is exercisable at no mode, the frame has no `Modify` on the\nstructure 2 nor on its field 3, and `release` of 2 and `endUse` of 2 are rejected; the exit of\nframe 1 releases 2. The chain of G3 is the root 1, held by frame 1, then 2. Pass 7 transferred into\na leaf, which J1 rejects (shape). -/\ndef hu0 : S3 := storeEff (deriveEff (enter1 [(none, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0), (none, none, 0),\n  (some 2, none, 0)]) 1 2 .modify) 2 1\ndef hu1 : S3 := transferEff hu0 0 2\ntheorem held_unexercisable_by_transfer :\n    Reachable K0 [] hu1 ∧ (hu1.A[2]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder, y.footprint)) =\n      some (true, .place 3, [3]) ∧ ¬ hu1.ExercisableAt 2 .observe ∧ ¬ HasRight hu1 .modify 2 ∧\n      ¬ HasRight hu1 .modify 3 ∧\n      ReleaseStep 2 hu1 .reject ∧ EndUseStep K0 2 hu1 .reject ∧ NoOrphan hu1 ∧\n      ExitStep K0 hu1 (.ok (exitEff hu1)) ∧ ¬ (exitEff hu1).Active 2 ∧ NothingAtFrame0 hu1 := by\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] hu1 := .transfer (.store (.derive (.enter (.init (by decide))\n    (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))) (.ok (by decide))\n  exact ⟨r, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, .reject (by decide), .reject (by decide),\n    reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r, .ok (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- The same through `issue` (G3; A10): from `fa2` (arena value 0, storage 4 with the nodes 5 and\n6, `internal` 4 held by 0), the block on the node 5 is issued to the node 5 itself (`ok`): the block\nis held by the place it covers, its origin `internal` 4 has no effective mode there, and the\nblock is exercisable at no mode. -/\ndef iu1 : S3 := arenaSet (issueEff fa2 arFa [5] 5).1 0 (issueEff fa2 arFa [5] 5).2\ntheorem held_unexercisable_by_issue :\n    Reachable K0 [] iu1 ∧ (iu1.A[5]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder, y.footprint)) =\n      some (true, .place 5, [5]) ∧ ¬ iu1.ExercisableAt 5 .observe ∧ NoOrphan iu1 ∧\n      NothingAtFrame0 iu1 := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] fa0 := .enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] fa1 := .alloc (.write r0 (show Write3Step 1 [1] fa0 (.ok _) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show AllocStep K0 1 0 [(none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)]\n      _ (.ok fa1) from .ok (by decide) trivial)\n  have r2 : Reachable K0 [] fa2 := .newArena (.write r1 (show Write3Step 0 [0] fa1 (.ok fa1w) from\n    .ok (by decide))) (show NewArenaStep 4 4 fa1w (.ok fa2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] iu1 := .issue r2 (show IssueAt K0 0 0 [5] 5 fa2 (.ok iu1) from\n    .ok (ar := arFa) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)))\n  exact ⟨r, by decide, by decide, reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ### Leaves made `Init` without a write (G2; review of pass 7; J1) -/\n\n/-- Pass 7 reached, through `transfer`, the configuration G2 rejects for `store`: a reference held\nby a whole structure, whose `length` field becomes `Init` without a write. J1 rejects that\ntransfer: the destination has another shape than the source. Frame 1: structure 0 with the fields\n1 (`ptr`) and 2 (`length`), the buffer 3, the leaves 4 and 5. The frame derives 4, `Modify` on 3,\nand stores it into the leaf 4. The transfer of 4 into the structure 0 is rejected (J1, shape).\nTwin: the transfer of 4 into the leaf 5, of the same shape, is accepted, 4 passing to 5, which is\nthen read. -/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ea17b992-6e48-439c-9db0-0bf47bb10e0e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"140dde0a-42cc-49cc-b5f7-a8641ddb1c14","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"formal/validation_0.1","slug":"effervescent-gathering-wind"}
