{"parentUuid":"09c367f2-2415-4a30-82ae-92cb6231288e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d8867bcf-fa69-4463-9401-ce9d6d53950a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VTSynKRbq6s5ARBQUybQP6","type":"tool_result","content":"fields 1 and 2; the place `S` (3), owned by `q`, of root 1 held by `q` (A4, A5); a structure `w` (4)\nwith the fields 5 and 6; roots 0 (on 1 and 2) and 2 (on 5 and 6). The caller derives 3, `Modify` on\n`S`, from the root 1, then 4 from the root 0 on `q`, 5 and 6 from 4 on the fields 1 and 2, 7 from\nthe root 2 on `w`, stores 5 into 5 and 6 into 6, and calls with `[3, 4, 7]`. At the entry, the\nroot 1 is exercisable at no mode: 4 has no effective mode on `q`, and 5 and 6, exercisable through\n7, each cover one field of `q`; the call is accepted (G1) and `CallProtects` holds. The callee\nreleases 3: 1 is still hidden. It releases 5 and 6, held by the fields of `w` on which 7 gives\n`Modify` (C4): 4 regains effective `Modify` on `q`, so the root 1 is exercisable, covers the leaf 3\nof 3, and is its origin. The callee then writes the leaf 3 through 1. Pass 7 built the same\nsituation with a transfer of a leaf into the structure `q`, which J1 rejects. -/\ndef ub0 : S3 := enter1 [(none, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0), (none, some 0, 0),\n  (none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)]\ndef ub1 : S3 := deriveEff ub0 1 3 .modify\ndef ub2 : S3 := deriveEff ub1 0 0 .modify\ndef ub3 : S3 := deriveEff ub2 4 1 .modify\ndef ub4 : S3 := deriveEff ub3 4 2 .modify\ndef ub5 : S3 := deriveEff ub4 2 4 .modify\ndef ub6 : S3 := storeEff ub5 5 5\ndef ub7 : S3 := storeEff ub6 6 6\ndef ub8 : S3 := enterEff ub7 [3, 4, 7] []\ndef ub9 : S3 := releaseEff ub8 3\ndef ub10 : S3 := releaseEff ub9 5\ndef ub11 : S3 := releaseEff ub10 6\ntheorem call_protects_params_safe_fails_unblock :\n    Reachable K0 [] ub11 ∧ EnterStep [3, 4, 7] [] ub7 (.ok ub8) ∧ CallProtects ub8 ∧\n      ¬ ub8.ExercisableAt 1 .observe ∧ ¬ ub9.ExercisableAt 1 .observe ∧\n      ub11.ExercisableAt 1 .modify ∧ ¬ CallProtects ub11 ∧\n      Write3Step 1 [3] ub11 (.ok (write3Eff ub11 [3])) := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] ub0 := .enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] ub1 := .derive r0 (show DeriveStep 1 3 .modify ub0 (.ok ub1) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n/-- The witness `ub` without the release of the parameter (G1, targeted search): from the entry\n`ub8`, the callee releases only 5 and 6; the parameter 3 is still active, and its direct origin, the\nroot 1, is exercisable at `Modify`, without effective mode on the leaf 3 while 3 is active. -/\ndef ua1 : S3 := releaseEff ub8 5\ndef ua2 : S3 := releaseEff ua1 6\ntheorem call_protects_params_safe_fails_unblock_active :\n    Reachable K0 [] ua2 ∧ ReleaseStep 5 ub8 (.ok ua1) ∧ ReleaseStep 6 ua1 (.ok ua2) ∧\n      ua2.Active 3 ∧ ua2.ExercisableAt 1 .modify ∧ effective ua2 1 3 = none ∧\n      ¬ CallProtects ua2 ∧ ua2.callParams 2 = [3, 4, 7] ∧ ua2.org 3 = some 1 := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] ub0 := .enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] ub1 := .derive r0 (show DeriveStep 1 3 .modify ub0 (.ok ub1) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r2 : Reachable K0 [] ub2 := .derive r1 (show DeriveStep 0 0 .modify ub1 (.ok ub2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r3 : Reachable K0 [] ub3 := .derive r2 (show DeriveStep 4 1 .modify ub2 (.ok ub3) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r4 : Reachable K0 [] ub4 := .derive r3 (show DeriveStep 4 2 .modify ub3 (.ok ub4) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r5 : Reachable K0 [] ub5 := .derive r4 (show DeriveStep 2 4 .modify ub4 (.ok ub5) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r6 : Reachable K0 [] ub6 := .store r5 (show StoreStep 5 5 ub5 (.ok ub6) from .ok (by decide))\n    .ok (by decide))) (show NewArenaStep 5 3 it1w (.ok it2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have hi : IssueAt K0 0 0 [6] 3 it2 (.ok it3) :=\n    .ok (ar := arIt) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide))\n  exact ⟨.issue r2 hi, .reject (by decide), .reject (ar := arIt) (by decide) (.reject (by decide)),\n    by decide, hi, by decide, by decide, .ok (by decide), .reject (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ### Cycles of holders closed after the stores (G2, G3; review of pass 7) -/\n\n/-- The clause of arrival of G2 guards `store` only: the cycle of F7 (a), rejected at the second\n`store` (`progress_cycle_whole_nodes`), is built anyway with a helper. From `fa7`, the frame derives\n9, `Modify` on B from 7; `store 8 6` is then accepted, the helper keeping B exercisable; `release 9`\ncloses the cycle. The authorities 7 and 8 are then as after the rejected store: no frame can\nexercise them nor observe A or B, while `NoOrphan` holds (G3). -/\ndef fh0 : S3 := deriveEff fa7 7 6 .modify\ndef fh1 : S3 := storeEff fh0 8 6\ndef fh2 : S3 := releaseEff fh1 9\ntheorem f7a_cycle_by_release :\n    Reachable K0 [] fh2 ∧ StoreStep 8 6 fa7 .reject ∧\n      StoreStep 8 6 fh0 (.ok fh1) ∧ ReleaseStep 9 fh1 (.ok fh2) ∧\n      fh1.ExercisableAt 7 .modify ∧ fh1.ExercisableAt 8 .modify ∧\n      (fh2.A[7]?, fh2.A[8]?) = ((storeEff fa7 8 6).A[7]?, (storeEff fa7 8 6).A[8]?) ∧\n      ¬ fh2.ExercisableAt 7 .observe ∧ ¬ fh2.ExercisableAt 8 .observe ∧\n      ¬ HasRight fh2 .observe 5 ∧ ¬ HasRight fh2 .observe 6 ∧\n      fh2.F = [1, 0] ∧ NothingAtFrame0 fh2 ∧ NoOrphan fh2 ∧\n      (fh2.A[7]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder)) = some (true, .place 5) ∧\n      (fh2.A[8]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder)) = some (true, .place 6) := by\n  have r7 : Reachable K0 [] fa7 := progress_cycle_whole_nodes.1\n  have d : DeriveStep 7 6 .modify fa7 (.ok fh0) := .ok (by decide)\n  have st : StoreStep 8 6 fh0 (.ok fh1) := .ok (by decide)\n  have rl : ReleaseStep 9 fh1 (.ok fh2) := .ok (by decide)\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] fh2 := .release (.store (.derive r7 d) st) rl\n  exact ⟨r, progress_cycle_whole_nodes.2.2.2.1, st, rl, by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- The same pattern on the three-node cycle (G2): from `tc8`, where `store 11 8` is rejected, the\nframe derives the helper 12, `Modify` on C from 10; `store 11 8` is then accepted; `release 12`\ncloses the cycle, with 9, 10 and 11 as after the rejected store. -/\ndef tn0 : S3 := deriveEff tc8 10 8 .modify\ndef tn1 : S3 := storeEff tn0 11 8\ndef tn2 : S3 := releaseEff tn1 12\ntheorem three_node_cycle_by_release :\n    Reachable K0 [] tn2 ∧ StoreStep 11 8 tc8 .reject ∧ StoreStep 11 8 tn0 (.ok tn1) ∧\n      ReleaseStep 12 tn1 (.ok tn2) ∧\n      (tn2.A[9]?, tn2.A[10]?, tn2.A[11]?) =\n        ((storeEff tc8 11 8).A[9]?, (storeEff tc8 11 8).A[10]?, (storeEff tc8 11 8).A[11]?) ∧\n      ¬ tn2.ExercisableAt 9 .observe ∧ ¬ tn2.ExercisableAt 10 .observe ∧\n      ¬ tn2.ExercisableAt 11 .observe ∧ NothingAtFrame0 tn2 ∧ NoOrphan tn2 := by\n  have r8 : Reachable K0 [] tc8 := progress_cycle_three_nodes.1\n  have d : DeriveStep 10 8 .modify tc8 (.ok tn0) := .ok (by decide)\n  have st : StoreStep 11 8 tn0 (.ok tn1) := .ok (by decide)\n  have rl : ReleaseStep 12 tn1 (.ok tn2) := .ok (by decide)\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] tn2 := .release (.store (.derive r8 d) st) rl\n  exact ⟨r, progress_cycle_three_nodes.2.2.2.1, st, rl, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    by decide, reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r⟩\n\n/-- The same pattern on two leaves of the frame (G2): frame 1 has the leaves 0, 1 and 2, of roots\n0, 1 and 2. It derives 3, `Modify` on 1, and stores it into 0; derives the helper 4, `Modify` on 1\nfrom 3, then 5, `Modify` on 0, and stores 5 into 1, which the helper makes acceptable; without the\nhelper, that store is rejected. -/","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7be4180d-ef68-4cff-abe6-1fa84cbdacb9","timestamp":"2026-11-01T17:49:48.850Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"fields 1 and 2; the place `S` (3), owned by `q`, of root 1 held by `q` (A4, A5); a structure `w` (4)\nwith the fields 5 and 6; roots 0 (on 1 and 2) and 2 (on 5 and 6). The caller derives 3, `Modify` on\n`S`, from the root 1, then 4 from the root 0 on `q`, 5 and 6 from 4 on the fields 1 and 2, 7 from\nthe root 2 on `w`, stores 5 into 5 and 6 into 6, and calls with `[3, 4, 7]`. At the entry, the\nroot 1 is exercisable at no mode: 4 has no effective mode on `q`, and 5 and 6, exercisable through\n7, each cover one field of `q`; the call is accepted (G1) and `CallProtects` holds. The callee\nreleases 3: 1 is still hidden. It releases 5 and 6, held by the fields of `w` on which 7 gives\n`Modify` (C4): 4 regains effective `Modify` on `q`, so the root 1 is exercisable, covers the leaf 3\nof 3, and is its origin. The callee then writes the leaf 3 through 1. Pass 7 built the same\nsituation with a transfer of a leaf into the structure `q`, which J1 rejects. -/\ndef ub0 : S3 := enter1 [(none, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0), (some 0, none, 0), (none, some 0, 0),\n  (none, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0), (some 4, none, 0)]\ndef ub1 : S3 := deriveEff ub0 1 3 .modify\ndef ub2 : S3 := deriveEff ub1 0 0 .modify\ndef ub3 : S3 := deriveEff ub2 4 1 .modify\ndef ub4 : S3 := deriveEff ub3 4 2 .modify\ndef ub5 : S3 := deriveEff ub4 2 4 .modify\ndef ub6 : S3 := storeEff ub5 5 5\ndef ub7 : S3 := storeEff ub6 6 6\ndef ub8 : S3 := enterEff ub7 [3, 4, 7] []\ndef ub9 : S3 := releaseEff ub8 3\ndef ub10 : S3 := releaseEff ub9 5\ndef ub11 : S3 := releaseEff ub10 6\ntheorem call_protects_params_safe_fails_unblock :\n    Reachable K0 [] ub11 ∧ EnterStep [3, 4, 7] [] ub7 (.ok ub8) ∧ CallProtects ub8 ∧\n      ¬ ub8.ExercisableAt 1 .observe ∧ ¬ ub9.ExercisableAt 1 .observe ∧\n      ub11.ExercisableAt 1 .modify ∧ ¬ CallProtects ub11 ∧\n      Write3Step 1 [3] ub11 (.ok (write3Eff ub11 [3])) := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] ub0 := .enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] ub1 := .derive r0 (show DeriveStep 1 3 .modify ub0 (.ok ub1) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n/-- The witness `ub` without the release of the parameter (G1, targeted search): from the entry\n`ub8`, the callee releases only 5 and 6; the parameter 3 is still active, and its direct origin, the\nroot 1, is exercisable at `Modify`, without effective mode on the leaf 3 while 3 is active. -/\ndef ua1 : S3 := releaseEff ub8 5\ndef ua2 : S3 := releaseEff ua1 6\ntheorem call_protects_params_safe_fails_unblock_active :\n    Reachable K0 [] ua2 ∧ ReleaseStep 5 ub8 (.ok ua1) ∧ ReleaseStep 6 ua1 (.ok ua2) ∧\n      ua2.Active 3 ∧ ua2.ExercisableAt 1 .modify ∧ effective ua2 1 3 = none ∧\n      ¬ CallProtects ua2 ∧ ua2.callParams 2 = [3, 4, 7] ∧ ua2.org 3 = some 1 := by\n  have r0 : Reachable K0 [] ub0 := .enter (.init (by decide)) (.ok (by decide))\n  have r1 : Reachable K0 [] ub1 := .derive r0 (show DeriveStep 1 3 .modify ub0 (.ok ub1) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r2 : Reachable K0 [] ub2 := .derive r1 (show DeriveStep 0 0 .modify ub1 (.ok ub2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r3 : Reachable K0 [] ub3 := .derive r2 (show DeriveStep 4 1 .modify ub2 (.ok ub3) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r4 : Reachable K0 [] ub4 := .derive r3 (show DeriveStep 4 2 .modify ub3 (.ok ub4) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r5 : Reachable K0 [] ub5 := .derive r4 (show DeriveStep 2 4 .modify ub4 (.ok ub5) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have r6 : Reachable K0 [] ub6 := .store r5 (show StoreStep 5 5 ub5 (.ok ub6) from .ok (by decide))\n    .ok (by decide))) (show NewArenaStep 5 3 it1w (.ok it2) from\n    .ok (by decide))\n  have hi : IssueAt K0 0 0 [6] 3 it2 (.ok it3) :=\n    .ok (ar := arIt) (by decide) (.ok (by decide) (by decide) (by decide) (by decide))\n  exact ⟨.issue r2 hi, .reject (by decide), .reject (ar := arIt) (by decide) (.reject (by decide)),\n    by decide, hi, by decide, by decide, .ok (by decide), .reject (by decide), by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-! ### Cycles of holders closed after the stores (G2, G3; review of pass 7) -/\n\n/-- The clause of arrival of G2 guards `store` only: the cycle of F7 (a), rejected at the second\n`store` (`progress_cycle_whole_nodes`), is built anyway with a helper. From `fa7`, the frame derives\n9, `Modify` on B from 7; `store 8 6` is then accepted, the helper keeping B exercisable; `release 9`\ncloses the cycle. The authorities 7 and 8 are then as after the rejected store: no frame can\nexercise them nor observe A or B, while `NoOrphan` holds (G3). -/\ndef fh0 : S3 := deriveEff fa7 7 6 .modify\ndef fh1 : S3 := storeEff fh0 8 6\ndef fh2 : S3 := releaseEff fh1 9\ntheorem f7a_cycle_by_release :\n    Reachable K0 [] fh2 ∧ StoreStep 8 6 fa7 .reject ∧\n      StoreStep 8 6 fh0 (.ok fh1) ∧ ReleaseStep 9 fh1 (.ok fh2) ∧\n      fh1.ExercisableAt 7 .modify ∧ fh1.ExercisableAt 8 .modify ∧\n      (fh2.A[7]?, fh2.A[8]?) = ((storeEff fa7 8 6).A[7]?, (storeEff fa7 8 6).A[8]?) ∧\n      ¬ fh2.ExercisableAt 7 .observe ∧ ¬ fh2.ExercisableAt 8 .observe ∧\n      ¬ HasRight fh2 .observe 5 ∧ ¬ HasRight fh2 .observe 6 ∧\n      fh2.F = [1, 0] ∧ NothingAtFrame0 fh2 ∧ NoOrphan fh2 ∧\n      (fh2.A[7]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder)) = some (true, .place 5) ∧\n      (fh2.A[8]?).map (fun y => (y.active, y.holder)) = some (true, .place 6) := by\n  have r7 : Reachable K0 [] fa7 := progress_cycle_whole_nodes.1\n  have d : DeriveStep 7 6 .modify fa7 (.ok fh0) := .ok (by decide)\n  have st : StoreStep 8 6 fh0 (.ok fh1) := .ok (by decide)\n  have rl : ReleaseStep 9 fh1 (.ok fh2) := .ok (by decide)\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] fh2 := .release (.store (.derive r7 d) st) rl\n  exact ⟨r, progress_cycle_whole_nodes.2.2.2.1, st, rl, by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r, by decide, by decide⟩\n\n/-- The same pattern on the three-node cycle (G2): from `tc8`, where `store 11 8` is rejected, the\nframe derives the helper 12, `Modify` on C from 10; `store 11 8` is then accepted; `release 12`\ncloses the cycle, with 9, 10 and 11 as after the rejected store. -/\ndef tn0 : S3 := deriveEff tc8 10 8 .modify\ndef tn1 : S3 := storeEff tn0 11 8\ndef tn2 : S3 := releaseEff tn1 12\ntheorem three_node_cycle_by_release :\n    Reachable K0 [] tn2 ∧ StoreStep 11 8 tc8 .reject ∧ StoreStep 11 8 tn0 (.ok tn1) ∧\n      ReleaseStep 12 tn1 (.ok tn2) ∧\n      (tn2.A[9]?, tn2.A[10]?, tn2.A[11]?) =\n        ((storeEff tc8 11 8).A[9]?, (storeEff tc8 11 8).A[10]?, (storeEff tc8 11 8).A[11]?) ∧\n      ¬ tn2.ExercisableAt 9 .observe ∧ ¬ tn2.ExercisableAt 10 .observe ∧\n      ¬ tn2.ExercisableAt 11 .observe ∧ NothingAtFrame0 tn2 ∧ NoOrphan tn2 := by\n  have r8 : Reachable K0 [] tc8 := progress_cycle_three_nodes.1\n  have d : DeriveStep 10 8 .modify tc8 (.ok tn0) := .ok (by decide)\n  have st : StoreStep 11 8 tn0 (.ok tn1) := .ok (by decide)\n  have rl : ReleaseStep 12 tn1 (.ok tn2) := .ok (by decide)\n  have r : Reachable K0 [] tn2 := .release (.store (.derive r8 d) st) rl\n  exact ⟨r, progress_cycle_three_nodes.2.2.2.1, st, rl, by decide, by decide, by decide, by decide,\n    by decide, reachable_no_orphan (KT_dd [] [] [] [] []) r⟩\n\n/-- The same pattern on two leaves of the frame (G2): frame 1 has the leaves 0, 1 and 2, of roots\n0, 1 and 2. It derives 3, `Modify` on 1, and stores it into 0; derives the helper 4, `Modify` on 1\nfrom 3, then 5, `Modify` on 0, and stores 5 into 1, which the helper makes acceptable; without the\nhelper, that store is rejected. -/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e1103ce4-f8c1-4c2d-8fae-577574319874","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/validation_0.1","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"or