{"parentUuid":"f1e55a24-7083-4ce7-970f-f90a383a36a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgcfMTeawAjha4br2f1w5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019HET3uTagSUectqQQjYbm4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern && git checkout formal/Ern/.gitkeep 2>/dev/null; git status --short && git add formal/Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nJ3 step 3: MM23-H corpus as translated executions\n\nWhy: the jalon-3 material (§3) asks for each MM23-H case replayed as an\nexecution translated by simulation; H15 and H16 encoded with the obtained\nverdict and marked as known gaps (rule 8); H14 and H17 not encoded.\n\nWhat: new module Ern.MM23.Horrors. An executable translated step (sexec,\nsrun) checks each labelled MM-03 step and its obligations by decide and is\nproved to extend a SimRun (srun_sound); sim_of applies simulation. The\nlayout is computed from the places of the run (each root its own\nallocation, in index order; leaves 8 bytes). Seven runs cover H01 (split\nunder DeclaredDisjoint instantiated by byte disjointness), H02 (old block\ninactive after reset while MM-02 would read it; reset_kills_blocks), H03\n(simulation_pinned), H04 (transfer_copies), H05, H06, H07 (ok, size zero,\nfail), H08, H09, H10, H11, H12, H13, H15 and H16 (known gaps: address 0\nfor empty regions; head address 8 bytes above the lowest leaf).\n\nProof: lake build succeeds without warnings; the 203 constants of the\nmodule depend only on propext and Quot.sound.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1; SP=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad; cat >> $SP/j3/log.md <<'EOF'\n7. Step 3 done: MM23-H in Ern/MM23/Horrors.lean; executable SimRun runner (srun) with soundness;\n   layout computed from the final places so no per-case tables; 7 runs cover all encoded cases;\n 